 bug about incorrect cache invalidation in the Data Ingestion API has been resolved. You can check the details in the approved PR here: https://github.com/salesforce/AutoTuneForce/pull/54.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20270204-0-6e8da\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20270204-0-6e8da\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-iantaylor-AutoTuneForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-35b4b2\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_04a698e5\", \"timestamp\": \"2027-02-04T06:02:00\", \"text\": \"Great news, George! Could you explain what was causing the issue?\", \"utterranceID\": \"20270204-1-a994d\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20270204-1-a994d\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-iantaylor-AutoTuneForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-35b4b2\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_6a0f49ba\", \"timestamp\": \"2027-02-04T06:03:00\", \"text\": \"Sure, @eid_04a698e5. The root cause was a logic error in the cache invalidation process. Specifically, the condition to remove outdated data entries was not correctly implemented, which led to the system using stale data.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20270204-2-964c4\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20270204-2-964c4\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-iantaylor-AutoTuneForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-35b4b2\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_35e32fec\", \"timestamp\": \"2027-02-04T06:07:00\", \"text\": \"Thanks for the update, George Jones. How did you manage to fix it?\", \"utterranceID\": \"20270204-3-cc147\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20270204-3-cc147\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-iantaylor-AutoTuneForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-35b4b2\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_6a0f49ba\", \"timestamp\": \"2027-02-04T06:09:00\", \"text\": \"I updated the logic to correctly identify and remove outdated data entries from the cache. This involved adjusting the condition checks to ensure that any data older than the c