{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-georgegarcia-WorkFlowGenie\", \"channelID\": \"ch-owaix-db5d92\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_1e8695b6\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-04-17T21:32:00\", \"text\": \"I agree with Alice, the implementation looks thorough. However, I noticed that the performance benchmarks weren't included. Did you get a chance to run those, @eid_95f6d01c?\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260417-4-d00d9\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260417-4-d00d9\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-georgegarcia-WorkFlowGenie\", \"channelID\": \"ch-owaix-db5d92\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_95f6d01c\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-04-17T21:36:00\", \"text\": \"Ah, good catch, Charlie. I ran some initial tests, but I haven't documented them in the PR yet. I'll make sure to add those benchmarks. Thanks for pointing it out!\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260417-5-7e324\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260417-5-7e324\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-georgegarcia-WorkFlowGenie\", \"channelID\": \"ch-owaix-db5d92\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_e214d622\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-04-17T21:37:00\", \"text\": \"Also, I noticed a couple of test cases where the data returned wasn't exactly as expected. Could you double-check those, @eid_95f6d01c? Just to ensure accuracy. 😊\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260417-6-8a3b9\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260417-6-8a3b9\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-georgegarcia-WorkFlowGenie\", \"channelID\": \"ch-owaix-db5d92\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_95f6d01c\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-04-17T21:40:00\", \"text\": \"Absolutely, Alice. I'll revisit those test cases and make sure everything aligns with the expected results. Thanks for the feedback!\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260417-7-67a28\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260417-7-67a28\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-georgegarcia-WorkFlowGenie\", \"channelID\": \"ch-owaix-db5d92\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_1e8695b6\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-04-17T21:44:00\", \"text\": \"No worries, @eid_95f6d01c. Once you update the benchmarks and test cases, I think we'll be in a good spot. Let us know when it's ready for another round of review. 👍\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260417-8-bc8eb\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260417-8-bc8eb\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-georgegarcia-WorkFlowGenie\", \"channelID\": \"ch-owaix-db5d92\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_95f6d01c\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-04-17T21:47:00\", \"text\": \"Will do, Charlie! Thanks for the input, everyone. I'll ping you once I've made the updates. 😊\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260417-9-11694\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260417-9-11694\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-georgegarcia-WorkFlowGenie\", \"channelID\": \"ch-owaix-db5d92\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_3f26c6e5\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-04-02T02:56:00\", \"text\": \"Hi team, I just wanted to bring up PR# 4 regarding the implementation of edge computing for Slack workflow processing. I've heard that our product direction has changed, and I'm wondering if this PR is still necessary. Can someone provide more context?\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260401-0-b2aee\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260401-0-b2aee\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-georgegarcia-WorkFlowGenie\", \"channelID\": \"ch-owaix-db5d92\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_18571957\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-04-02T02:59:00\", \"text\": \"Hey @eid_3f26c6e5, yes, the PR was approved and merged because it aimed to reduce latency by processing workflows closer to the data source. However, with the new product direction, we might not need this feature anymore.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260401-1-caa14\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260401-1-caa14\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-georgegarcia-WorkFlowGenie\", \"channelID\": \"ch-owaix-db5d92\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_62e8e52d\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-04-02T03:01:00\", \"text\": \"Could someone clarify what the new product direction entails? It would help us understand if the edge computing capabilities are still relevant.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260401-2-1499d\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260401-2-1499d\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-georgegarcia-WorkFlowGenie\", \"channelID\": \"ch-owaix-db5d92\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_c92d3e03\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-04-02T03:03:00\", \"text\": \"The new direction focuses more on centralized processing to streamline our infrastructure. This means edge computing might not align with our current goals.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260401-3-500cf\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260401-3-500cf\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-georgegarcia-WorkFlowGenie\", \"channelID\": \"ch-owaix-db5d92\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_320cd970\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-04-02T03:07:00\", \"text\": \"If the product direction has shifted towards centralized processing, then maintaining edge computing could lead to unnecessary complexity. It might be best to revert the changes.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260401-4-40aa9\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260401-4-40aa9\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-georgegarcia-WorkFlowGenie\", \"channelID\": \"ch-owaix-db5d92\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_136119e9\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-04-02T03:09:00\", \"text\": \"I understand the concerns. Just to confirm, are we deciding to revert the PR because it doesn't align with the new direction?\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260401-5-359a9\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260401-5-359a9\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-georgegarcia-WorkFlowGenie\", \"channelID\": \"ch-owaix-db5d92\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_6039d1c9\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-04-02T03:11:00\", \"text\": \"Yes, @eid_136119e9, given the shift in focus, it seems reverting the PR would be the best course of action to avoid any misalignment with our current strategy.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260401-6-c0088\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260401-6-c0088\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-georgegarcia-WorkFlowGenie\", \"channelID\": \"ch-owaix-db5d92\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_136119e9\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-04-02T03:16:00\", \"text\": \"Got it. I'll take the necessary steps to revert the PR soon. Thanks for the clarification, everyone.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260401-7-91339\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260401-7-91339\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-georgegarcia-WorkFlowGenie\", \"channelID\": \"ch-owaix-db5d92\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_136119e9\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-04-02T06:25:00\", \"text\": \"https://github.com/salesforce/flowAIX/pull/5\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260402-0-9d5c1\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260402-0-9d5c1\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-georgegarcia-WorkFlowGenie\", \"channelID\": \"ch-owaix-db5d92\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_18571957\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-04-02T06:28:00\", \"text\": \"LGTM\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260402-1-568bc\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260402-1-568bc\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-georgegarcia-WorkFlowGenie\", \"channelID\": \"ch-owaix-db5d92\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_c92d3e03\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-04-02T06:30:00\", \"text\": \"Approved\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260402-2-1f3be\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260402-2-1f3be\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-georgegarcia-WorkFlowGenie\", \"channelID\": \"ch-owaix-db5d92\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_136119e9\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-05-06T21:01:00\", \"text\": \"Hi team, please check my PR for optimizing network communication between edge nodes and central servers: https://github.com/salesforce/flowAIX/pull/19. The goal is to reduce bandwidth usage by at least 15% and improve data throughput. Let me know your thoughts! 🚀\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260507-0-79ed9\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260507-0-79ed9\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-georgegarcia-WorkFlowGenie\", \"channelID\": \"ch-owaix-db5d92\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_1e8695b6\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-05-06T21:03:00\", \"text\": \"Hey @eid_136119e9, just took a quick look at the PR. The changes look promising! I'll dive deeper into the code and run some tests. 👍\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260507-1-fc2ec\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260507-1-fc2ec\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-georgegarcia-WorkFlowGenie\", \"channelID\": \"ch-owaix-db5d92\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_c92d3e03\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-05-06T21:06:00\", \"text\": \"Thanks for sharing, @eid_136119e9! I'll review the documentation updates first to ensure everything aligns with the new strategies. 📝\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260507-2-86f5e\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260507-2-86f5e\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-georgegarcia-WorkFlowGenie\", \"channelID\": \"ch-owaix-db5d92\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_1e8695b6\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-05-06T21:09:00\", \"text\": \"Alright, I've gone through the code and ran the benchmarks. The network protocols are indeed optimized, and I'm seeing a bandwidth reduction of around 16%. Great job! 👏\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260507-3-eebae\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260507-3-eebae\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-georgegarcia-WorkFlowGenie\", \"channelID\": \"ch-owaix-db5d92\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_c92d3e03\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-05-06T21:13:00\", \"text\": \"The documentation is clear and concise, @eid_136119e9. It accurately reflects the changes in the communication strategies. Also, the data synchronization tests show reliable performance within the expected timeframes. 📈\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260507-4-8142e\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260507-4-8142e\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-georgegarcia-WorkFlowGenie\", \"channelID\": \"ch-owaix-db5d92\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_1e8695b6\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-05-06T21:14:00\", \"text\": \"Performance benchmarks are solid. Data throughput has improved, and network latency is reduced as expected. Everything checks out from my side. LGTM, approved! ✅\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260507-5-62795\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260507-5-62795\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-georgegarcia-WorkFlowGenie\", \"channelID\": \"ch-owaix-db5d92\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_c92d3e03\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-05-06T21:16:00\", \"text\": \"Same here, @eid_136119e9. All acceptance criteria are met, and the improvements are evident. LGTM, approved! 🎉\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260507-6-ae008\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260507-6-ae008\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-georgegarcia-WorkFlowGenie\", \"channelID\": \"ch-owaix-db5d92\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_136119e9\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-05-06T21:19:00\", \"text\": \"Thanks, @Charlie Martinez and @Julia Brown! Appreciate the quick turnaround and feedback. Let's get this merged! 🚀\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260507-7-1b8fc\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260507-7-1b8fc\"}\n{\"title\": \"Integrate Feedback Bot into Slack\", \"summary\": \"Implement the core functionality of the feedback bot within Slack to collect real-time user feedback during the onboarding process. This includes setting up the bot's basic interaction capabilities and ensuring it can be triggered at appropriate times without disrupting user workflow.\", \"link\": \"https://github.com/salesforce/flowAIX/pull/3\", \"mergeable\": \"True\", \"merged\": \"False\", \"number\": \"3\", \"state\": \"open\", \"user\": {\"login\": \"eid_515ae627\"}, \"created_at\": \"2026-03-27T02:27:00\", \"reviews\": [{\"state\": \"APPROVED\", \"user\": {\"login\": \"eid_18571957\"}, \"comment\": \"The integration looks solid! The bot triggers perfectly during the onboarding process without any hiccups. The security measures seem robust. LGTM, approved! 🚀\", \"submitted_at\": \"2026-03-27T13:17:00\"}, {\"state\": \"COMMENTED\", \"user\": {\"login\": \"eid_1e8695b6\"}, \"comment\": \"The bot's interactions are smooth and don't disrupt the user's workflow. The bot is well integrated and secure. LGTM, approved! 🎉\", \"submitted_at\": \"2026-03-27T13:22:00\"}], \"id\": \"github_com_salesforce_flowAIX_pull_3\"}\n{\"title\": \"Implement Feedback Data Integration with Salesforce\", \"summary\": \"Develop the integration layer that allows feedback collected by the bot to be seamlessly transferred and stored in Salesforce. This ensures that user feedback is accessible for analysis and reporting.\", \"link\": \"https://github.com/salesforce/flowAIX/pull/18\", \"mergeable\": \"True\", \"merged\": \"False\", \"number\": \"18\", \"state\": \"open\", \"user\": {\"login\": \"eid_515ae627\"}, \"created_at\": \"2026-05-04T21:17:00\", \"reviews\": [{\"state\": \"APPROVED\", \"user\": {\"login\": \"eid_55f29a0d\"}, \"comment\": \"Just finished reviewing the data transfer part. Everything looks solid, and the logging is a nice touch! No data loss detected in my tests. LGTM, approved! 🚀\", \"submitted_at\": \"2026-05-05T01:28:00\"}, {\"state\": \"PENDING\", \"user\": {\"login\": \"eid_18571957\"}, \"comment\": \"I ran some performance tests, and the integration doesn't introduce any noticeable latency. Great job on optimizing the data flow! Also, I checked the data privacy measures, and everything seems secure. LGTM, approved! 🔒\", \"submitted_at\": \"2026-05-05T01:33:00\"}], \"id\": \"github_com_salesforce_flowAIX_pull_18\"}\n{\"title\": \"Integrate Transformer Models for Enhanced NLP\", \"summary\": \"This PR integrates transformer models into the existing AI framework to improve natural language processing capabilities. The focus is on leveraging pre-trained models to enhance the accuracy of Slack workflow automation.\", \"link\": \"https://github.com/salesforce/flowAIX/pull/7\", \"mergeable\": \"True\", \"merged\": \"True\", \"number\": \"7\", \"state\": \"closed\", \"user\": {\"login\": \"eid_515ae627\"}, \"created_at\": \"2026-04-11T08:17:00\", \"reviews\": [{\"state\": \"APPROVED\", \"user\": {\"login\": \"eid_e3c15ff5\"}, \"comment\": \"I've reviewed the changes, and the transformer models are integrated smoothly into the AI framework. Great job! LGTM, approved! 🚀\", \"submitted_at\": \"2026-04-11T22:28:00\"}, {\"state\": \"COMMENTED\", \"user\": {\"login\": \"eid_4812cbd8\"}, \"comment\": \"The NLP accuracy improvement is impressive, over 20% as expected. Everything checks out from my side too. Approved! ✅\", \"submitted_at\": \"2026-04-11T22:31:00\"}, {\"state\": \"COMMENTED\", \"user\": {\"login\": \"eid_d96bfd9b\"}, \"comment\": \"The integration looks promising. Checked the unit tests, and all existing ones pass with the new integration. Plus, the new tests for the transformers are comprehensive. Looks good to me as well. Approved! 🙌\", \"submitted_at\": \"2026-04-11T22:34:00\"}], \"id\": \"github_com_salesforce_flowAIX_pull_7\"}\n{\"title\": \"Design Intuitive UI Components for Feedback Bot\", \"summary\": \"Create user-friendly and intuitive UI components for the feedback bot to enhance user interaction. This includes designing message templates, buttons, and any other interactive elements that facilitate easy feedback submission.\", \"link\": \"https://github.com/salesforce/flowAIX/pull/8\", \"mergeable\": \"True\", \"merged\": \"False\", \"number\": \"8\", \"state\": \"open\", \"user\": {\"login\": \"eid_d96bfd9b\"}, \"created_at\": \"2026-04-12T03:40:00\", \"reviews\": [{\"state\": \"CHANGES_REQUESTED\", \"user\": {\"login\": \"eid_18571957\"}, \"comment\": \"The message templates look great and are user-friendly. However, the buttons need to be fully responsive on mobile devices as they appear off-center.\", \"submitted_at\": \"2026-04-12T10:07:00\"}, {\"state\": \"COMMENTED\", \"user\": {\"login\": \"eid_1e8695b6\"}, \"comment\": \"The feedback submission process is straightforward, but consider reducing the number of clicks needed to submit feedback by combining some steps.\", \"submitted_at\": \"2026-04-12T10:12:00\"}], \"id\": \"github_com_salesforce_flowAIX_pull_8\"}\n{\"transcript\": \"Attendees\\nGeorge Garcia, David Garcia, Ian Davis, David Brown, Julia Smith, Alice Taylor, Julia Brown, Charlie Davis, Charlie Martinez, Fiona Martinez, Bob Miller, Julia Garcia, Alice Taylor, Fiona Martinez, Bob Garcia, Charlie Smith, Alice Johnson\\nTranscript\\nJulia Smith: Alright team, welcome to our first sprint review session for flowAIX. Since this is our first meeting, we don't have any completed PRs to discuss, so let's dive into the pending tasks and assignments.\\nIan Davis: Sounds good, Julia. Let's start with the GraphQL integration task. George, this one's assigned to you, right?\\nGeorge Garcia: Yes, that's correct. The task is to define the GraphQL schema for Salesforce data integration. I'll be working on mirroring the existing REST API structure. I confirm, I’ll take care of this implementation.\\nDavid Brown: Great, George. Make sure to keep us updated on any blockers you might face.\\nJulia Smith: Next, we have the task of enhancing AI capabilities with natural language processing. Fiona, this one's yours.\\nFiona Martinez: Yes, I'm on it. I'll be integrating transformer models to improve our NLP capabilities. Got it, I’ll handle this.\\nAlice Taylor: Fiona, if you need any help with the pre-trained models, feel free to reach out. I've worked with them before.\\nFiona Martinez: Thanks, Alice. I might take you up on that offer.\\nJulia Smith: Moving on, we have the task of improving the user onboarding process. Bob, you're assigned to integrate the feedback bot into Slack.\\nBob Garcia: Yes, I'll be implementing the core functionality of the feedback bot. I confirm, I’ll take care of this implementation.\\nDavid Brown: Bob, make sure the bot's interactions are seamless and don't disrupt the user workflow.\\nBob Garcia: Absolutely, David. I'll ensure it's smooth.\\nJulia Smith: Lastly, we have the performance optimization task through edge computing and data caching. Bob Miller, this one's for you.\\nBob Miller: Yes, I'll be implementing edge computing for Slack workflow processing. Got it, I’ll handle this.\\nAlice Taylor: Bob, if you need any architectural insights, feel free to loop me in.\\nBob Miller: Thanks, Alice. I'll definitely reach out if needed.\\nJulia Smith: Great, I think we're all set with the assignments. Let's make sure to keep the communication open and address any issues as they arise. Thanks, everyone!\\nIan Davis: Thanks, Julia. Looking forward to seeing the progress in our next meeting.\", \"date\": \"2026-03-21T08:59:00\", \"document_type\": \"product-planning\", \"participants\": [\"eid_95f6d01c\", \"eid_f4f58faa\", \"eid_71c0d545\", \"eid_1f678d18\", \"eid_827a0ea9\", \"eid_2543da6a\", \"eid_c92d3e03\", \"eid_55f29a0d\", \"eid_1e8695b6\", \"eid_d96bfd9b\", \"eid_136119e9\", \"eid_18571957\", \"eid_e214d622\", \"eid_e3c15ff5\", \"eid_515ae627\", \"eid_686130c8\", \"eid_4812cbd8\"], \"id\": \"product_dev_flowAIX_2\"}\n{\"transcript\": \"Attendees\\nGeorge Garcia, David Garcia, Ian Davis, David Brown, Julia Smith, Alice Taylor, Julia Brown, Charlie Davis, Charlie Martinez, Fiona Martinez, Bob Miller, Julia Garcia, Alice Taylor, Fiona Martinez, Bob Garcia, Charlie Smith, Alice Johnson\\nTranscript\\nGeorge Garcia: Alright team, let's kick off this sprint review. First, let's discuss the completed PRs. David, can you start with the Feedback Bot integration?\\nDavid Garcia: Sure, George. The Feedback Bot integration into Slack",
