. I'll conduct a thorough review of the supported sensor types and document any gaps. I'll make sure we cover all critical sensor types for device compatibility.\\nJulia Martinez: Thanks, Julia. Next, we have 'Develop RESTful API framework'. Alice Garcia, this is linked to the PR 'Develop Data Processing Endpoints'.\\nAlice Garcia: I confirm, Julia. I'll implement the endpoints for AI processing on the device. This will facilitate real-time data analysis and insights, which is crucial for our product.\\nBob Miller: Perfect, Alice. Let's ensure we maintain the momentum. If anyone needs support, don't hesitate to reach out. Any questions or clarifications needed before we wrap up?\\nCharlie Davis: Just a quick one, Bob. For the hardware compatibility checks, do we have a timeline for when we need the documentation completed?\\nDavid Miller: Good question, Charlie. Ideally, we should aim to have it done by the end of this sprint to align with our release schedule.\\nJulia Smith: Understood, I'll prioritize it accordingly.\\nJulia Martinez: Great, thanks everyone. Let's keep up the good work and push forward with these tasks. Meeting adjourned.\", \"date\": \"2026-11-22T11:03:00\", \"document_type\": \"product-planning\", \"participants\": [\"eid_91523bad\", \"eid_b6a30126\", \"eid_caa2e58d\", \"eid_2d8eff4d\", \"eid_a253c65a\", \"eid_4b38019b\", \"eid_2347b567\", \"eid_bac7c6c4\", \"eid_edf6a3fc\", \"eid_4df3bcc2\", \"eid_54905dcb\", \"eid_4555ba9c\", \"eid_3e076e53\", \"eid_5058fefc\", \"eid_a0fe567d\"], \"id\": \"product_dev_EdgeForce_7\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-juliamartinez-EdgeForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-a13a7a\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_bac7c6c4\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-08T03:48:00\", \"text\": \"Hi team, please check my PR for adding support for new sensor protocols: https://github.com/salesforce/EF_AIX/pull/4. This update focuses on enhancing device compatibility by updating the device layer to recognize and process data from newly identified sensor types. Let me know your thoughts! 😊\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261007-0-ff0a9\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261007-0-ff0a9\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-juliamartinez-EdgeForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-a13a7a\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_4df3bcc2\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-08T03:49:00\", \"text\": \"Hey @eid_bac7c6c4, thanks for sharing! I'll start reviewing it now. Excited to see how these new protocols are integrated. 🔍\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261007-1-156c7\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261007-1-156c7\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-juliamartinez-EdgeForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-a13a7a\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_4b38019b\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-08T03:51:00\", \"text\": \"Checking it out now, @eid_bac7c6c4. The new sensor protocols sound like a great addition! 👍\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261007-2-f49ed\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261007-2-f49ed\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-juliamartinez-EdgeForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-a13a7a\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_2347b567\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-08T03:52:00\", \"text\": \"On it! Looking forward to seeing how the device layer handles these new protocols. 😊\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261007-3-fc5e6\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261007-3-fc5e6\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-juliamartinez-EdgeForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-a13a7a\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_4df3bcc2\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-08T03:57:00\", \"text\": \"Alright, I've gone through the changes. The device layer seems to recognize and process the new sensor protocols perfectly. Great job on that, @eid_bac7c6c4! 🎉\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261007-4-0b3b9\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261007-4-0b3b9\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-juliamartinez-EdgeForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-a13a7a\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_4b38019b\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-08T03:59:00\", \"text\": \"Just finished reviewing the unit tests. They cover all the new protocols and pass successfully. Everything looks solid from my end. Nice work, @eid_bac7c6c4! 💪\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261007-5-21671\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261007-5-21671\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-juliamartinez-EdgeForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-a13a7a\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_2347b567\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-08T04:00:00\", \"text\": \"Documentation is up-to-date and clearly outlines the new sensor protocols supported. Thanks for keeping it comprehensive, @eid_bac7c6c4! 📚\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261007-6-6cd7e\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261007-6-6cd7e\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-juliamartinez-EdgeForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-a13a7a\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_4df3bcc2\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-08T04:03:00\", \"text\": \"LGTM, approved! 🚀\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261007-7-13f03\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261007-7-13f03\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-juliamartinez-EdgeForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-a13a7a\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_4b38019b\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-08T04:06:00\", \"text\": \"Looks good to me too, approved! 👍\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261007-8-d760e\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261007-8-d760e\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-juliamartinez-EdgeForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-a13a7a\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_2347b567\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-08T04:10:00\", \"text\": \"All criteria met, approved! Great work, team! 🎉\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261007-9-77bbf\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261007-9-77bbf\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-juliamartinez-EdgeForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-a13a7a\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_bac7c6c4\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-08T04:11:00\", \"text\": \"Thanks, everyone! Appreciate the quick reviews and feedback. Let's get these new protocols live! 🚀\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261007-10-37fea\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261007-10-37fea\"}\n{\"transcript\": \"Attendees\\nJulia Martinez, Charlie Martinez, Bob Miller, David Miller, Hannah Brown, Charlie Davis, Julia Smith, Julia Jones, Fiona Taylor, Alice Miller, Alice Garcia, Ian Jones, Charlie Miller, Fiona Brown, Hannah Jones\\nTranscript\\nJulia Martinez: Alright team, welcome to our first sprint review for the Einstein Edge AI project. Let's dive into the status of our tasks and PRs. Since this is our first meeting, we don't have any completed PRs to discuss, so we'll focus on our pending tasks.\\nBob Miller: Sounds good, Julia. Let's start with the hardware compatibility checks. Julia Smith, you're assigned to this task, right?\\nJulia Smith: Yes, that's correct. I'm working on the PR titled 'Add Support for New Sensor Protocols'. The goal is to update the device layer to recognize and process data from new sensor types.\\nHannah Brown: Julia, do you foresee any challenges with implementing support for these new protocols?\\nJulia Smith: Not at the moment, but I'll keep an eye on any compatibility issues that might arise during testing.\\nJulia Martinez: Great. Let's move on to the RESTful API framework. Alice Garcia, you're handling this one, correct?\\nAlice Garcia: Yes, I'm on it. The PR is titled 'Initialize RESTful API Framework'. I'll be setting up the foundational structure and ensuring we have all the necessary libraries and configurations in place.\\nCharlie Martinez: Alice, do you need any additional resources or support to get started?\\nAlice Garcia: Not at the moment, Charlie. I have everything I need to kick things off. I'll reach out if anything comes up.\\nJulia Martinez: Perfect. Lastly, we have the JWT authentication task. Charlie Miller, you're assigned to this, right?\\nCharlie Miller: Yes, that's me. The PR is 'Implement JWT Token Generation and Validation'. I'll be working on creating a utility module for handling JWT operations.\\nDavid Miller: Charlie, make sure to coordinate with the API team to ensure seamless integration.\\nCharlie Miller: Got it, David. I'll make sure to sync up with Alice and the rest of the API team.\\nJulia Martinez: Alright, team. Let's make sure we keep communication open and address any blockers as they come up. Does anyone have any questions or need further clarification on their tasks?\\nFiona Taylor: No questions from me. Everything seems clear.\\nAlice Miller: Same here. I'm good to go.\\nJulia Martinez: Great. Let's aim to have significant progress by our next meeting. Thanks, everyone!\", \"date\": \"2026-09-25T04:45:00\", \"document_type\": \"product-planning\", \"participants\": [\"eid_91523bad\", \"eid_b6a30126\", \"eid_caa2e58d\", \"eid_2d8eff4d\", \"eid_a253c65a\", \"eid_4b38019b\", \"eid_2347b567\", \"eid_bac7c6c4\", \"eid_edf6a3fc\", \"eid_4df3bcc2\", \"eid_54905dcb\", \"eid_4555ba9c\", \"eid_3e076e53\", \"eid_5058fefc\", \"eid_a0fe567d\"], \"id\": \"product_dev_EF_AIX_2\"}\n{\"transcript\": \"Attendees\\nJulia Martinez, Charlie Martinez, Bob Miller, David Miller, Hannah Brown, Charlie Davis, Julia Smith, Julia Jones, Fiona Taylor, Alice Miller, Alice Garcia, Ian Jones, Charlie Miller, Fiona Brown, Hannah Jones\\nTranscript\\nJulia Martinez: Alright team, let's kick off this sprint review. First, let's go over the completed PRs. Charlie, can you start with the 'Add Support for New Sensor Protocols'?\\nCharlie Martinez: Sure, Julia. We successfully implemented support for additional sensor protocols. This update enhances our device compatibility by allowing the device layer to recognize and process data from new sensor types. It’s been tested and is working smoothly.\\nBob Miller: Great work, Charlie. This will definitely broaden our device compatibility. How about the RESTful API framework, Julia?\\nCharlie Davis: Yes, the foundational structure for the RESTful API framework is set up. We’ve included all necessary libraries and configurations to support further API development. It’s ready for the next steps.\\nDavid Miller: Excellent. This sets a solid base for our API work. And the JWT token generation and validation?\\nFiona Brown: That’s completed as well. We now have a utility module for handling JWT operations, including token creation, signing, and verification. It’s integrated and functioning as expected.\\nHannah Brown: Fantastic progress, everyone. Now, let's move on to the pending tasks. First up, the hardware compatibility checks. Julia Smith, this is assigned to you, correct?\\nJulia Smith: Yes, that's right. I'll be developing the module to perform hardware compatibility checks. This will ensure devices meet the necessary requirements for running EF_AIX.\\nJulia Martinez: Great, Julia. Please make sure to check for supported sensor types and necessary hardware specifications.\\nJulia Smith: Got it, I’ll handle this.\\nBob Miller: Next, we have the development of the RESTful API framework. Alice Garcia, you’re on this, right?\\nAlice Garcia: Yes, I am. I’ll be working on implementing the user authentication endpoints, including login and registration functionalities to secure the API.\\nDavid Miller: Perfect. Make sure to coordinate with the team to ensure seamless integration.\\nAlice Garcia: I confirm, I’ll take care of this implementation.\\nHannah Brown: Lastly, we have the JWT authentication integration into the user login flow. Charlie Miller, this is yours, correct?\\nCharlie Miller: Yes, I’ll be integrating JWT authentication into the existing user login flow. This involves modifying the login endpoint to issue a JWT token upon successful authentication and updating the client-side to handle token storage.\\nCharlie Martinez: Sounds good, Charlie. Let us know if you need any support.\\nCharlie Miller: I confirm, I’ll take care of this implementation.\\nJulia Martinez: Alright, team. That wraps up our sprint review. Let’s keep up the great work and stay on track with these tasks. If there are no further questions, let’s get back to it.\\nAlice Miller: No questions from me. Let’s do this!\\nFiona Taylor: All clear here. Looking forward to the next steps.\", \"date\": \"2026-10-17T21:29:00\", \"document_type\": \"product-planning\", \"participants\": [\"eid_91523bad\", \"eid_b6a30126\", \"eid_caa2e58d\", \"eid_2d8eff4d\", \"eid_a253c65a\", \"eid_4b38019b\", \"eid_2347b567\", \"eid_bac7c6c4\", \"eid_edf6a3fc\", \"eid_4df3bcc2\", \"eid_54905dcb\", \"eid_4555ba9c\", \"eid_3e076e53\", \"eid_5058fefc\", \"eid_a0fe567d\"], \"id\": \"product_dev_EdgeForce_4\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-juliamartinez-EdgeForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-a13a7a\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_2347b567\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-19T17:36:00\", \"text\": \"Hi team, please check my PR for the new Hardware Compatibility Check Module: https://github.com/salesforce/EF_AIX/pull/8. This module ensures devices meet the necessary requirements for running EF_AIX by checking supported sensor types and hardware specifications. Let me know your thoughts! 😊\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261021-0-54970\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261021-0-54970\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-juliamartinez-EdgeForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-a13a7a\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_bac7c6c4\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-19T17:38:00\", \"text\": \"Hey @eid_2347b567, thanks for sharing! I'll start reviewing it now. Excited to see how it identifies compatible and incompatible hardware. 🔍\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261021-1-fbf4b\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261021-1-fbf4b\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-juliamartinez-EdgeForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-a13a7a\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_4b38019b\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-19T17:40:00\", \"text\": \"Thanks for the heads up, @eid_2347b567! I'll dive into the integration tests to ensure everything works smoothly across different configurations. 🛠️\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261021-2-1b4e3\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261021-2-1b4e3\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-juliamartinez-EdgeForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-a13a7a\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_bac7c6c4\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-19T17:41:00\", \"text\": \"Just finished going through the code. The module accurately identifies hardware compatibility based on the criteria we discussed. Great job on that! 👍\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261021-3-d8214\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261021-3-d8214\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-juliamartinez-EdgeForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-a13a7a\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_4b38019b\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-19T17:44:00\", \"text\": \"Integration tests look solid, @eid_2347b567. Everything passes across the different hardware setups we have. Nice work! 👏\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261021-4-2cd63\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261021-4-2cd63\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-juliamartinez-EdgeForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-a13a7a\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_bac7c6c4\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-19T17:49:00\", \"text\": \"Also, the user documentation is clear and provides good instructions on using the module. This will definitely help users get started without any hiccups. 📚\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261021-5-40306\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261021-5-40306\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-juliamartinez-EdgeForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-a13a7a\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_4b38019b\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-19T17:53:00\", \"text\": \"Agreed, the documentation is spot on. @eid_2347b567, you've covered all the bases. LGTM, approved! ✅\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261021-6-7f962\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261021-6-7f962\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-juliamartinez-EdgeForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-a13a7a\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_bac7c6c4\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-19T17:58:00\", \"text\": \"Same here, everything looks great. LGTM, approved! 🚀\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261021-7-0f2c6\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261021-7-0f2c6\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-juliamartinez-EdgeForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-a13a7a\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_2347b567\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-19T18:03:00\", \"text\": \"Thanks, @eid_bac7c6c4 and @eid_4b38019b! Appreciate the quick review and feedback. Glad everything's in order. 🎉\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261021-8-b75f8\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261021-8-b75f8\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-juliamartinez-EdgeForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-a13a7a\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_54905dcb\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-20T12:07:00\", \"text\": \"Hi team, please check my PR for implementing user authentication endpoints: https://github.com/salesforce/EF_AIX/pull/9. I've added endpoints for login and registration, ensuring user data is securely managed and authentication tokens are generated and validated. Let me know your thoughts! 😊\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261020-0-4dda7\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261020-0-4dda7\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-juliamartinez-EdgeForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-a13a7a\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_4b38019b\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-20T12:11:00\", \"text\": \"Hey @eid_54905dcb, thanks for sharing! I'll take a look at it now. 🔍\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261020-1-489aa\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261020-1-489aa\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-juliamartinez-EdgeForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-a13a7a\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_2347b567\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-20T12:13:00\", \"text\": \"Hi @eid_54905dcb, I'll review it too. Excited to see how you've tackled the token generation! 🔑\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261020-2-dbcd7\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261020-2-dbcd7\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-juliamartinez-EdgeForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-a13a7a\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_4b38019b\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-20T12:16:00\", \"text\": \"Alright, I've gone through the PR. The endpoints for login and registration look solid, and I appreciate the use of bcrypt for password hashing. However, I noticed that the token validation logic seems a bit off. It doesn't handle expired tokens correctly. Can you take another look at that? 🤔\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261020-3-2a8f2\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261020-3-2a8f2\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-juliamartinez-EdgeForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-a13a7a\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_2347b567\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-20T12:19:00\", \"text\": \"I agree with Charlie. Also, @eid_54905dcb, I think we should add more unit tests for the token generation and validation process to ensure everything works as expected. Other than that, great job on securing the user data! 🔐\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261020-4-9d056\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261020-4-9d056\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-juliamartinez-EdgeForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-a13a7a\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_54905dcb\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-20T12:22:00\", \"text\": \"Thanks for the feedback, @Charlie Davis and @Julia Smith! I'll revisit the token validation logic and add more tests. Appreciate the quick review! I'll ping you once the updates are ready. 🚀\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261020-5-74ddf\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261020-5-74ddf\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-juliamartinez-EdgeForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-a13a7a\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_4b38019b\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-20T12:24:00\", \"text\": \"Sounds good, @eid_54905dcb! Looking forward to the updates. Let us know if you need any help. 👍\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261020-6-78c5d\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261020-6-78c5d\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-juliamartinez-EdgeForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-a13a7a\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_2347b567\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-20T12:29:00\", \"text\": \"Absolutely, feel free to reach out if you need a hand with anything. Thanks for addressing the feedback so promptly! 😊\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261020-7-957a3\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261020-7-957a3\"}\n{\"transcript\": \"Attendees\\nJulia Martinez, Charlie Martinez, Bob Miller, David Miller, Hannah Brown, Charlie Davis, Julia Smith, Julia Jones, Fiona Taylor, Alice Miller, Alice Garcia, Ian Jones, Charlie Miller, Fiona Brown, Hannah Jones\\nTranscript\\nJulia Martinez: Alright team, let's kick off this sprint review. First, let's go over the completed PRs. Charlie, can you start with the Hardware Compatibility Check Module?\\nCharlie Martinez: Sure, Julia. The Hardware Compatibility Check Module is complete. It ensures that devices meet the necessary requirements for running EF_AIX, including supported sensor types and hardware specifications. Everything's been tested and is working as expected.\\nBob Miller: Great work, Charlie. This is crucial for ensuring our product runs smoothly across different devices.\\nDavid Miller: Absolutely, Bob. And the JWT Authentication integration into the user login flow is also complete. This will enhance our security significantly.\\nCharlie Davis: Yes, David. The JWT integration modifies the login endpoint to issue a JWT token upon successful authentication and updates the client-side to handle token storage. It's all set.\\nHannah Brown: Fantastic. Now, let's move on to the pending tasks. First up, we have the task to conduct hardware compatibility checks for device compatibility. Julia Smith, you're assigned to update the device layer for enhanced protocol handling. Can you confirm?\\nJulia Smith: Got it, Hannah. I'll handle the refactoring to improve protocol handling and ensure seamless integration with more devices.\\nJulia Martinez: Great. Next, we have the development of the RESTful API framework. Alice Garcia, your PR needs additional revisions. Alice Miller, you'll be working on a new PR for this. Can you confirm?\\nAlice Garcia: Yes, Julia. I'll make the necessary revisions to my PR.\\nAlice Miller: I confirm, I'll take care of the new PR for the user authentication endpoints.\\nBob Miller: Thanks, Alice and Alice. This is a key part of securing our API.\\nDavid Miller: Absolutely, and finally, we have the task to implement JWT authentication for security. Charlie Miller, you're assigned to implement middleware for JWT token verification. Can you confirm?\\nCharlie Miller: I confirm, David. I'll ensure that only requests with valid tokens can access protected routes.\\nJulia Jones: Great teamwork, everyone. Let's keep up the momentum and ensure we meet our sprint goals.\\nFiona Taylor: Agreed, Julia. If anyone needs help or has questions, feel free to reach out.\\nFiona Brown: Thanks, Fiona. Let's make this sprint a success!\", \"date\": \"2026-10-27T21:17:00\", \"document_type\": \"product-planning\", \"participants\": [\"eid_91523bad\", \"eid_b6a30126\", \"eid_caa2e58d\", \"eid_2d8eff4d\", \"eid_a253c65a\", \"eid_4b38019b\", \"eid_2347b567\", \"eid_bac7c6c4\", \"eid_edf6a3fc\", \"eid_4df3bcc2\", \"eid_54905dcb\", \"eid_4555ba9c\", \"eid_3e076e53\", \"eid_5058fefc\", \"eid_a0fe567d\"], \"id\": \"product_dev_EdgeForce_5\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-juliamartinez-EdgeForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-a13a7a\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_edf6a3fc\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-08T19:58:00\", \"text\": \"Hi team, please check my PR for the 'Update Device Layer for Enhanced Protocol Handling'. I've refactored the device layer to improve handling of various communication protocols, ensuring seamless integration with a wider range of devices. Here's the link: https://github.com/salesforce/EF_AIX/pull/14. Let me know your thoughts! 😊\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261109-0-9ac75\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261109-0-9ac75\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-juliamartinez-EdgeForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-a13a7a\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_4b38019b\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-08T20:03:00\", \"text\": \"@eid_edf6a3fc Thanks for sharing! I'll start reviewing it now. Looking forward to seeing how it handles multiple protocols. 🚀\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261109-1-cc8f4\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261109-1-cc8f4\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-juliamartinez-EdgeForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-a13a7a\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_4df3bcc2\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-08T20:06:00\", \"text\": \"Hey @eid_edf6a3fc, I'll take a look at the performance benchmarks and coding standards. Excited to see the improvements! 🔍\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261109-2-f7dff\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261109-2-f7dff\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-juliamartinez-EdgeForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-a13a7a\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_2347b567\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-08T20:08:00\", \"text\": \"On it! I'll focus on ensuring there are no errors with the multiple communication protocols. Thanks for the heads up, @eid_edf6a3fc! 👍\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261109-3-b8d71\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261109-3-b8d71\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-juliamartinez-EdgeForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-a13a7a\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_4b38019b\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-08T20:11:00\", \"text\": \"Just finished reviewing the code. The refactoring looks solid, and I didn't encounter any issues with handling multiple protocols. Great job, @eid_edf6a3fc! LGTM, approved! ✅\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261109-4-b1b17\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261109-4-b1b17\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-juliamartinez-EdgeForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-a13a7a\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_4df3bcc2\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-08T20:13:00\", \"text\": \"Checked the performance benchmarks, and everything seems to be running smoothly with no degradation in processing speed. Also, the code adheres to our standards. Well done, @eid_edf6a3fc! Approved from my side too! 🎉\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261109-5-8020f\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261109-5-8020f\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-juliamartinez-EdgeForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-a13a7a\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_2347b567\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-08T20:16:00\", \"text\": \"I ran some tests on the protocol handling, and everything works perfectly without any errors. Nice work, @eid_edf6a3fc! LGTM, approved! 🙌\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261109-6-91e41\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261109-6-91e41\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-juliamartinez-EdgeForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-a13a7a\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_edf6a3fc\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-08T20:19:00\", \"text\": \"Thanks, everyone! Really appreciate the quick reviews and feedback. Glad to hear everything's in order. 😊\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261109-7-97f86\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261109-7-97f86\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"planning-EF_AIX\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-30c6d3\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_b6a30126\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-18T20:26:00\", \"text\": \"Hi team, let's review the System Design Document and update it based on the latest issues reported. We've got some feedback from the latest release of EF_AIX that we need to address. 🚀\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260918-0-defa9\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260918-0-defa9\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"planning-EF_AIX\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-30c6d3\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_a253c65a\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-18T20:30:00\", \"text\": \"Hey Charlie, I think we should start by enhancing the 'User Experience' section. The setup process is currently too complex. We could add a subsection on 'Setup Automation' and detail scripts or tools that could simplify this process. Thoughts? 🤔\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260918-1-1d2ec\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260918-1-1d2ec\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"planning-EF_AIX\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-30c6d3\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_a9002ae2\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-18T20:34:00\", \"text\": \"@Hannah Brown, I agree. Also, we should expand the 'User Experience' section to include more detailed user guidance. Maybe a step-by-step guide or a video tutorial link? This could help non-technical users a lot. 📚\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260918-2-c2bf8\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260918-2-c2bf8\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"planning-EF_AIX\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-30c6d3\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_c9c3d8d5\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-18T20:35:00\", \"text\": \"Good point, Bob. We should also consider adding a 'Support Resources' section under 'Operational' to outline available support channels and resources. This could address the lack of support during setup. 📞\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260918-3-c9ddd\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260918-3-c9ddd\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"planning-EF_AIX\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-30c6d3\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_9db3abf4\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-18T20:39:00\", \"text\": \"For the performance issues, we might need to revisit the 'Edge Processing Layer' section. We should specify improvements in data processing algorithms and resource management. Maybe add a note on optimizing for large datasets? 📈\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260918-4-e5750\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260918-4-e5750\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"planning-EF_AIX\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-30c6d3\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_1a7d9807\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-18T20:42:00\", \"text\": \"Agreed, Alice. We should also mention the need for hardware compatibility checks in the 'Device Layer' section to ensure consistent performance across different devices. 🔍\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260918-5-40cb8\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260918-5-40cb8\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"planning-EF_AIX\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-30c6d3\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_caa2e58d\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-18T20:43:00\", \"text\": \"Regarding integration, the 'Integration Layer' should include a plan for developing more APIs and connectors. This will help with third-party application integration. Let's make it a priority in the development roadmap. 🔗\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260918-6-35b70\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260918-6-35b70\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"planning-EF_AIX\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-30c6d3\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_2d8eff4d\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-18T20:44:00\", \"text\": \"And for the UI issues, we should add a 'User Feedback Loop' section in the 'User Experience' part. This can help us continuously improve the UI based on user input. 🖥️\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260918-7-35619\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260918-7-35619\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"planning-EF_AIX\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-30c6d3\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_b6a30126\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-18T20:46:00\", \"text\": \"Great suggestions, everyone! To summarize: we'll add setup automation details, enhance user guidance, outline support resources, optimize data processing, ensure hardware compatibility, expand integration options, and incorporate user feedback. Let's update the document accordingly and schedule a follow-up meeting to review the changes. Thanks for the input! 🙌\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260918-8-f1ae0\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260918-8-f1ae0\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"planning-EF_AIX\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-30c6d3\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_b6a30126\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-19T08:54:00\", \"text\": \"Here is the updated <https://sf-internal.slack.com/archives/docs/new_ef_aix_system_design_document|System Design Document>, thank you everyone!\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260918-0-abe02\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260918-0-abe02\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"planning-EF_AIX\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-30c6d3\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_4b38019b\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-19T08:57:39\", \"text\": \"@here Read about the latest advancements in edge AI technology and its potential to drive innovation in this TechCrunch article. https://techcrunch.com/2023/02/15/edge-ai-advancements/\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260919-137-7c026\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260919-137-7c026\"}\n{\"title\": \"Implement JWT Token Generation and Validation\", \"summary\": \"This PR introduces the functionality to generate and validate JWT tokens for user authentication. It includes the creation of a utility module for handling JWT operations such as token creation, signing, and verification.\", \"link\": \"https://github.com/salesforce/EF_AIX/pull/6\", \"mergeable\": \"True\", \"merged\": \"True\", \"number\": \"6\", \"state\": \"closed\", \"user\": {\"login\": \"eid_edf6a3fc\"}, \"created_at\": \"2026-10-11T04:25:00\", \"reviews\": [{\"state\": \"APPROVED\", \"user\": {\"login\": \"eid_bac7c6c4\"}, \"comment\": \"Reviewed the documentation and it is clear with good instructions on using the JWT utility. LGTM, approved!\", \"submitted_at\": \"2026-10-11T11:27:00\"}, {\"state\": \"PENDING\", \"user\": {\"login\": \"eid_4b38019b\"}, \"comment\": \"The JWT tokens are generated with a secret key and validation checks out perfectly. Looks good to me too, approved!\", \"submitted_at\": \"2026-10-11T11:31:00\"}, {\"state\": \"PENDING\", \"user\": {\"login\": \"eid_3e076e53\"}, \"comment\": \"Reviewed the unit tests, and they cover all major functions of the JWT utility module. Everything looks solid. All criteria met, approved!\", \"submitted_at\": \"2026-10-11T11:33:00\"}], \"id\": \"github_com_salesforce_EF_AIX_pull_6\"}\n{\"title\": \"Revert PR# 4: Update Device Layer for New Sensor Protocols\", \"summary\": \"This revert is necessary due to a change in product direction. The company has decided to focus on optimizing existing sensor protocols rather than supporting additional ones, making the changes introduced in PR# 4 unnecessary. Reverting this PR will help maintain a streamlined codebase and prevent the maintenance of redundant features.\", \"link\": \"https://github.com/salesforce/EF_AIX/pull/7\", \"mergeable\": \"True\", \"merged\": \"True\", \"number\": \"7\", \"state\": \"closed\", \"user\": {\"login\": \"eid_bac7c6c4\"}, \"created_at\": \"2026-10-11T04:25:00\", \"reviews\": [{\"state\": \"APPROVED\", \"user\": {\"login\": \"eid_4df3bcc2\"}, \"comment\": \"Approved\", \"submitted_at\": \"2026-10-14T06:33:00\"}, {\"state\": \"COMMENTED\", \"user\": {\"login\": \"eid_4b38019b\"}, \"comment\": \"Looks good\", \"submitted_at\": \"2026-10-14T06:34:00\"}, {\"state\": \"COMMENTED\", \"user\": {\"login\": \"eid_2347b567\"}, \"comment\": \"Approved\", \"submitted_at\": \"2026-10-14T06:37:00\"}], \"id\": \"github_com_salesforce_EF_AIX_pull_7\"}\nIntroduction: Einstein Edge AI is an innovative solution designed to transform edge AI by enabling real-time data processing directly on devices. It targets key industries such as healthcare, automotive, manufacturing, and retail, offering a robust architecture that supports efficient data collection, processing, and integration with existing IT systems. This document outlines the comprehensive system design of Einstein Edge AI, detailing its architecture, security measures, user experience, and development roadmap.\nSystem Architecture: The architecture of Einstein Edge AI is structured into three primary layers: the device layer, the edge processing layer, and the integration layer. The device layer is responsible for supporting a wide array of sensors, ensuring efficient data collection with minimal latency. The edge processing layer is equipped with high-performance processors and GPUs, optimized for real-time AI analysis and low power consumption. The integration layer facilitates seamless communication with IT systems through protocols such as MQTT and HTTP/HTTPS, ensuring smooth data flow and system interoperability.\nDevice Layer: The device layer of Einstein Edge AI is designed to support diverse sensors, enabling efficient and low-latency data collection. This layer is crucial for gathering real-time data from various sources, which is then processed at the edge. The design ensures compatibility with a wide range of sensor types, making it adaptable to different industry needs and applications. Additionally, hardware compatibility checks are implemented to ensure consistent performance across different devices, allowing for reliable operation regardless of the hardware used.\n{\"transcript\": \"Attendees\\nJulia Martinez, Charlie Martinez, Bob Miller, David Miller, Hannah Brown, Charlie Davis, Julia Smith, Julia Jones, Fiona Taylor, Alice Miller, Alice Garcia, Ian Jones, Charlie Miller, Fiona Brown, Hannah Jones\\nTranscript\\nJulia Martinez: Alright team, let's kick off this sprint review. First, let's discuss the completed PRs. Charlie, can you start with the 'Identify and Document Sensor Type Gaps'?\\nCharlie Martinez: Sure, Julia. We conducted a thorough review of the sensor types currently supported by EdgeForce. We identified several gaps, particularly in the environmental sensors category. This documentation will help us prioritize future integrations.\\nBob Miller: Great work, Charlie. This will definitely help us expand our device compatibility. Now, what about the 'Develop Data Processing Endpoints'?\\nCharlie Davis: I can take that one. We implemented endpoints that allow AI processing directly on the device. This facilitates real-time data analysis and insights, which is a big step forward for EdgeForce.\\nDavid Miller: Fantastic, Charlie. This is crucial for reducing latency and improving performance. Now, let's move on to the pending tasks.\\nHannah Brown: Right, the next task is to develop the RESTful API framework. Alice Garcia, you're assigned to the 'Add Error Handling and Logging' PR. Can you confirm?\\nAlice Garcia: Got it, I’ll handle this. I'll integrate comprehensive error handling and logging mechanisms to ensure robustness and traceability of the API.\\nIan Jones: Alice, if you need any help with the logging part, feel free to reach out. I have some experience with similar implementations.\\nAlice Garcia: Thanks, Ian. I might take you up on that offer.\\nFiona Brown: Just to clarify, Alice, this task is crucial for the stability of our API. Make sure to cover all edge cases.\\nAlice Garcia: Absolutely, Fiona. I'll ensure that all potential issues are addressed.\\nJulia Martinez: Great, with that confirmed, let's wrap up. If there are no further questions, let's get back to work. Thanks, everyone!\\nJulia Smith: Thanks, Julia. Looking forward to seeing the progress in the next sprint.\", \"date\": \"2026-12-02T12:44:00\", \"document_type\": \"product-planning\", \"participants\": [\"eid_91523bad\", \"eid_b6a30126\", \"eid_caa2e58d\", \"eid_2d8eff4d\", \"eid_a253c65a\", \"eid_4b38019b\", \"eid_2347b567\", \"eid_bac7c6c4\", \"eid_edf6a3fc\", \"eid_4df3bcc2\", \"eid_54905dcb\", \"eid_4555ba9c\", \"eid_3e076e53\", \"eid_5058fefc\", \"eid_a0fe567d\"], \"id\": \"product_dev_EdgeForce_8\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-juliamartinez-EdgeForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-a13a7a\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_9db3abf4\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-25T18:53:00\", \"text\": \"Hi team, I noticed that PR# 10 is approved but not merged yet. I heard there's been a change in product direction. Can someone provide more context on this?\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261025-0-65d43\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261025-0-65d43\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-juliamartinez-EdgeForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-a13a7a\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_edf6a3fc\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-25T18:56:00\", \"text\": \"Yes, the product team decided to go in a different direction that doesn't require JWT authentication for the user login flow. So, this PR might not be necessary anymore.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261025-1-41cc2\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261025-1-41cc2\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-juliamartinez-EdgeForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-a13a7a\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_c9c3d8d5\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-25T18:58:00\", \"text\": \"Thanks for the update. @eid_3e076e53, could you confirm if the PR has been merged or if it's still open?\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261025-2-b2172\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261025-2-b2172\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-juliamartinez-EdgeForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-a13a7a\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_3e076e53\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-25T19:02:00\", \"text\": \"Hi all, the PR is still open and hasn't been merged yet.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261025-3-63df2\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261025-3-63df2\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-juliamartinez-EdgeForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-a13a7a\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_bac7c6c4\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-25T19:05:00\", \"text\": \"In that case, should we hold off on merging it? It seems like it won't align with the new product strategy.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261025-4-3139b\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261025-4-3139b\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-juliamartinez-EdgeForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-a13a7a\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_1a7d9807\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-25T19:07:00\", \"text\": \"I agree. If the JWT integration isn't needed anymore, it makes sense not to merge it.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261025-5-67ad9\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261025-5-67ad9\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-juliamartinez-EdgeForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-a13a7a\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_a9002ae2\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-25T19:09:00\", \"text\": \"Agreed. @eid_3e076e53, could you please ensure that the PR is not merged?\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261025-6-3844e\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261025-6-3844e\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-juliamartinez-EdgeForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-a13a7a\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_3e076e53\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-25T19:13:00\", \"text\": \"Sure, I'll make sure it stays unmerged. I'll take the necessary action soon. Thanks for the heads-up, everyone.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261025-7-f788d\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261025-7-f788d\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"