98d618\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-06-11T21:07:00\", \"text\": \"I agree with @Charlie Miller, the integration looks solid. However, I noticed that the performance tests for responsiveness are missing. We need to ensure these components perform well under different conditions. 📈\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260612-4-60e24\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260612-4-60e24\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-alicemartinez-FlowForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-ceaix-29b8e9\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_8605f7ee\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-06-11T21:09:00\", \"text\": \"Thanks for the feedback, @Ian Miller and @Charlie Miller! I did overlook the performance tests. I'll work on adding those and update the PR. Appreciate the catch! 🙌\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260612-5-e33e5\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260612-5-e33e5\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-alicemartinez-FlowForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-ceaix-29b8e9\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_d0d918f1\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-06-11T21:12:00\", \"text\": \"No worries, @eid_8605f7ee! Once you add those tests, I think we'll be in a good spot. Let us know when it's ready for another round of review. 👍\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260612-6-39198\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260612-6-39198\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-alicemartinez-FlowForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-ceaix-29b8e9\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_d098d618\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-06-11T21:17:00\", \"text\": \"Exactly, @eid_8605f7ee. Just ping us once you've made the updates. Looking forward to seeing the improvements! 😊\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260612-7-6eb4d\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260612-7-6eb4d\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-alicemartinez-FlowForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-ceaix-29b8e9\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_8605f7ee\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-06-11T21:18:00\", \"text\": \"Will do, @Charlie Miller and @Ian Miller! Thanks for the quick review and feedback. I'll get on it right away. 🚀\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260612-8-c0bde\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260612-8-c0bde\"}\n{\"transcript\": \"Attendees\\nAlice Davis, Alice Martinez, Alice Martinez, Hannah Taylor, Hannah Martinez, Ian Miller, George Martinez, Julia Garcia, George Brown, Fiona Davis, Ian Miller, Charlie Miller, Fiona Brown, Alice Taylor, Charlie Taylor\\nTranscript\\nAlice Davis: Alright team, let's kick off this sprint review. First, let's go over the completed PRs. Ian, could you start with the Efficient Algorithms for Real-Time Processing?\\nIan Miller: Sure, Alice. The PR for implementing efficient algorithms is complete. We've managed to reduce the computational complexity significantly, which has improved the execution speed of our real-time processing modules.\\nAlice Martinez: That's great to hear, Ian. How about the JWT-based Authentication Mechanism?\\nGeorge Martinez: I handled that one. The JWT integration is now live, and it enhances our security by ensuring secure token generation, validation, and expiration handling.\\nHannah Taylor: Excellent work, George. This will definitely bolster our security measures. Now, let's move on to the pending tasks.\\nHannah Martinez: First up, we have the task of optimizing the real-time processing modules. George Brown, you're assigned to integrate the event-driven architecture for API flow optimization. How's that looking?\\nGeorge Brown: Got it, I'll handle this. I'll start working on transitioning the architecture to an event-driven model to improve scalability and responsiveness.\\nAlice Martinez: Great, George. Next, we have the task of expanding the analytics dashboard. Julia, your PR needs some revisions. Fiona Brown, you'll be working on a new PR for this task.\\nJulia Garcia: Understood, I'll make the necessary revisions to my PR.\\nFiona Brown: I confirm, I'll take care of the new PR for developing dynamic frontend components using React.\\nHannah Taylor: Perfect. Lastly, we have the task of improving security measures. I'll be conducting the initial security audit and implementing the findings.\\nHannah Martinez: Thanks, Hannah. It's crucial we address any vulnerabilities identified during the audit. Does anyone have any questions or need clarifications on their tasks?\\nCharlie Miller: No questions from me. Everything seems clear.\\nAlice Taylor: Same here, all clear.\\nAlice Davis: Great! Let's aim to have these tasks completed by the end of the sprint. Thanks, everyone, for your hard work and dedication. Let's make this sprint a success!\", \"date\": \"2026-06-20T15:00:00\", \"document_type\": \"product-planning\", \"participants\": [\"eid_e5e36dc1\", \"eid_294ba09d\", \"eid_610a4c21\", \"eid_4e8b2cdc\", \"eid_5827604d\", \"eid_9a7b2132\", \"eid_f2474622\", \"eid_8605f7ee\", \"eid_71071933\", \"eid_399e4119\", \"eid_d098d618\", \"eid_d0d918f1\", \"eid_fc0f17c3\", \"eid_ba9224d2\", \"eid_b6268ef7\"], \"id\": \"product_dev_FlowForce_4\"}\n{\"transcript\": \"Attendees\\nAlice Davis, Alice Martinez, Alice Martinez, Hannah Taylor, Hannah Martinez, Ian Miller, George Martinez, Julia Garcia, George Brown, Fiona Davis, Ian Miller, Charlie Miller, Fiona Brown, Alice Taylor, Charlie Taylor\\nTranscript\\nAlice Davis: Alright team, let's get started with our sprint review for the FForceAIX project. Since this is our first review meeting, we don't have any completed PRs to discuss. So, let's dive into the pending tasks and assignments.\\nAlice Martinez: Sounds good, Alice. Let's start with the task on optimizing the real-time processing modules. George Brown, this one's assigned to you. The PR is titled 'Implement Efficient Algorithms for Real-Time Processing'.\\nGeorge Brown: Got it, I’ll handle this. I’ve already started looking into some algorithms that could reduce computational complexity. I’ll make sure to keep the team updated on my progress.\\nHannah Martinez: Great, George. Just make sure to focus on improving execution speed as well. If you need any help, feel free to reach out.\\nGeorge Brown: Will do, thanks!\\nHannah Taylor: Next up, we have the task of expanding the analytics dashboard. Julia, this is your task. The PR is titled 'Add New Visualization Options to Analytics Dashboard'.\\nJulia Garcia: I confirm, I’ll take care of this implementation. I’m planning to add bar charts, line graphs, and pie charts as discussed. I’ll also ensure the new visualizations integrate smoothly with the existing dashboard.\\nAlice Martinez: Perfect, Julia. Make sure to test the new visualizations thoroughly to ensure they enhance data representation effectively.\\nJulia Garcia: Absolutely, I’ll make sure to cover all the bases.\\nHannah Taylor: Lastly, we have the task of improving security measures. This involves implementing a JWT-based authentication mechanism. I’ll be handling this one myself.\\nHannah Martinez: Hannah, just a reminder to focus on secure token generation, validation, and expiration handling. If you need any architectural insights, feel free to reach out.\\nHannah Taylor: Thanks, I’ll definitely keep that in mind. I’ll ensure the integration is seamless and secure.\\nAlice Davis: Alright, team. That wraps up our task assignments for this sprint. Let’s keep the communication open and ensure we’re on track for our next review. Any questions or concerns before we wrap up?\\nIan Miller: No questions from me. Looking forward to seeing the progress on these tasks.\\nGeorge Martinez: Same here. Let’s make sure to document any challenges we face so we can address them in our next meeting.\\nAlice Davis: Great point, George. Alright, team, let’s get to work. Thanks, everyone!\", \"date\": \"2026-05-20T08:56:00\", \"document_type\": \"product-planning\", \"participants\": [\"eid_e5e36dc1\", \"eid_294ba09d\", \"eid_610a4c21\", \"eid_4e8b2cdc\", \"eid_5827604d\", \"eid_9a7b2132\", \"eid_f2474622\", \"eid_8605f7ee