I ran the unit tests and they're all passing. Looks like you've covered all the bases. LGTM, approved! ✅\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260602-7-491ef\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260602-7-491ef\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-iangarcia-LeadForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-a-aix-2eecee\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_a43a4389\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-05-30T05:13:00\", \"text\": \"Same here, all tests are green and the code looks clean. Approved from my side too! 🎉\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260602-8-c41df\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260602-8-c41df\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-iangarcia-LeadForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-a-aix-2eecee\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_a23a73c4\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-05-30T05:18:00\", \"text\": \"Everything checks out for me as well. Great job, @eid_207da0e7! Approved! 🙌\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260602-9-f9ee3\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260602-9-f9ee3\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-iangarcia-LeadForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-a-aix-2eecee\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_207da0e7\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-05-30T05:20:00\", \"text\": \"Thanks, everyone! Appreciate the quick reviews and feedback. Let's get this merged! 🚀\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260602-10-d453a\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260602-10-d453a\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-iangarcia-LeadForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-a-aix-2eecee\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_a23a73c4\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-05-30T07:43:00\", \"text\": \"@here take a look at our product demo, available here https://sf-internal.slack.com/archives/LeadForce/demo_3\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260530-0-092f1\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260530-0-092f1\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-iangarcia-LeadForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-a-aix-2eecee\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"slack_admin_bot\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-06-03T11:48:00\", \"text\": \"@eid_b814ccfb, @eid_88e74382 joined develop-iangarcia-LeadForce.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260603-73-fa200\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260603-73-fa200\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-iangarcia-LeadForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-a-aix-2eecee\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_7b85a749\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-06-03T14:31:00\", \"text\": \"Hi team, I noticed that PR# 8, which implements Salesforce API integration, is approved but not merged yet. I've heard that our product direction has changed. Should we discuss whether this PR is still necessary?\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260603-0-4b53b\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260603-0-4b53b\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-iangarcia-LeadForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-a-aix-2eecee\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_90359c89\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-06-03T14:36:00\", \"text\": \"Good point, @eid_7b85a749. Can someone clarify what the new product direction is and why this integration might no longer be needed?\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260603-1-0842d\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260603-1-0842d\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-iangarcia-LeadForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-a-aix-2eecee\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_b814ccfb\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-06-03T14:39:00\", \"text\": \"From what I understand, we're shifting focus away from Salesforce and towards a different CRM solution. This means the integration might not be needed anymore.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260603-2-ee3e2\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260603-2-ee3e2\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-iangarcia-LeadForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-a-aix-2eecee\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_a43a4389\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-06-03T14:40:00\", \"text\": \"That makes sense. @eid_207da0e7, could you provide some insight into how much work went into this PR and if there are any parts that might still be useful?\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260603-3-218db\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260603-3-218db\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-iangarcia-LeadForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-a-aix-2eecee\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_207da0e7\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-06-03T14:42:00\", \"text\": \"Sure, the PR involved setting up authentication, defining endpoints, and handling data requests and responses. If we're moving away from Salesforce, most of this work might not be reusable.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260603-4-f3184\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260603-4-f3184\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-iangarcia-LeadForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-a-aix-2eecee\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_88e74382\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-06-03T14:47:00\", \"text\": \"Thanks for the info, @eid_207da0e7. Given the change in direction, it seems like merging this PR might not be beneficial. What do others think?\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260603-5-801c5\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260603-5-801c5\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-iangarcia-LeadForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-a-aix-2eecee\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_a23a73c4\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-06-03T14:51:00\", \"text\": \"I agree. If the integration doesn't align with our new goals, it might be best not to merge it.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260603-6-fe8e1\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260603-6-fe8e1\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-iangarcia-LeadForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-a-aix-2eecee\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_55f01e31\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-06-03T14:56:00\", \"text\": \"I concur. It seems like the best course of action is to hold off on merging this PR.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260603-7-a2c29\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260603-7-a2c29\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-iangarcia-LeadForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-a-aix-2eecee\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_7b85a749\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-06-03T14:58:00\", \"text\": \"Alright, it sounds like we're all on the same page. @eid_207da0e7, could you please ensure that PR# 8 is not merged? If it has already been merged, could you revert it?\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260603-8-fbe56\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260603-8-fbe56\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-iangarcia-LeadForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-a-aix-2eecee\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_207da0e7\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-06-03T15:02:00\", \"text\": \"Got it, I'll make sure to take care of it soon. Thanks for the discussion, everyone.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260603-9-7f1c7\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260603-9-7f1c7\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-iangarcia-LeadForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-a-aix-2eecee\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_9f4e2c6f\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-07-19T02:26:00\", \"text\": \"Hi team, please check my PR for optimizing model hyperparameters: https://github.com/salesforce/AIX/pull/28. I've focused on tuning the hyperparameters to enhance the model's predictive capabilities and reduce overfitting. Let me know your thoughts! 😊\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260718-0-9fdb9\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260718-0-9fdb9\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-iangarcia-LeadForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-a-aix-2eecee\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_a43a4389\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-07-19T02:31:00\", \"text\": \"@eid_9f4e2c6f Thanks for sharing! I'll take a look at it now. Just to confirm, did you use a systematic approach like grid search or random search for the tuning?\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260718-1-01b20\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260718-1-01b20\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-iangarcia-LeadForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-a-aix-2eecee\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_9f4e2c6f\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-07-19T02:36:00\", \"text\": \"Yes, @eid_a43a4389! I used grid search to systematically explore the hyperparameter space. The results were validated using cross-validation to ensure robustness. 📊\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260718-2-81146\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260718-2-81146\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-iangarcia-LeadForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-a-aix-2eecee\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_a23a73c4\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-07-19T02:39:00\", \"text\": \"Hey @eid_9f4e2c6f, I just started reviewing the PR. I see you've documented the changes in hyperparameters with the rationale for each adjustment. That's super helpful! 👍\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260718-3-19af5\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260718-3-19af5\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-iangarcia-LeadForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-a-aix-2eecee\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_a43a4389\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-07-19T02:44:00\", \"text\": \"Great to hear, @eid_a23a73c4! I also noticed the unit tests confirm the model performs better with the new hyperparameters. The cross-validation results look promising. Nice work, @eid_9f4e2c6f! 🚀\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260718-4-2eab0\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260718-4-2eab0\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-iangarcia-LeadForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-a-aix-2eecee\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_a23a73c4\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-07-19T02:48:00\", \"text\": \"Agreed, the improvements are clear. Everything seems to meet the acceptance criteria. LGTM, approved! ✅\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260718-5-0fce4\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260718-5-0fce4\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-iangarcia-LeadForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-a-aix-2eecee\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_a43a4389\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-07-19T02:50:00\", \"text\": \"Same here, @eid_9f4e2c6f. The systematic approach and thorough documentation make it easy to follow. LGTM, approved! 🎉\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260718-6-0df37\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260718-6-0df37\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-iangarcia-LeadForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-a-aix-2eecee\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_9f4e2c6f\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-07-19T02:53:00\", \"text\": \"Thanks, @eid_a43a4389 and @eid_a23a73c4! Appreciate the quick review and feedback. I'll merge it now. 🙌\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260718-7-3eb71\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260718-7-3eb71\"}\n{\"title\": \"Fix UI Freeze During Bulk Lead Import by Offloading Processing to Background Thread\", \"summary\": \"### Summary of the Issue\\nThe user interface was freezing during the bulk import of leads due to the UI thread being blocked by synchronous data processing.\\n\\n### Changes Made\\n- Refactored the bulk import logic to run asynchronously on a background thread, ensuring the UI thread remains responsive.\\n- Implemented a progress indicator to provide feedback to users during the import process.\\n- Added error handling to manage any issues that arise during the asynchronous operation.\\n\\n### Testing\\n- Conducted manual testing by importing a large dataset of leads to verify that the UI remains responsive throughout the process.\\n- Automated tests were updated to cover the new asynchronous logic and ensure no regressions in functionality.\", \"link\": \"https://github.com/salesforce/LeadForce/pull/53\", \"mergeable\": \"True\", \"merged\": \"True\", \"number\": \"53\", \"state\": \"closed\", \"user\": {\"login\": \"eid_90359c89\"}, \"created_at\": \"2026-11-03T05:34:00\", \"reviews\": [{\"state\": \"APPROVED\", \"user\": {\"login\": \"eid_f98d7490\"}, \"comment\": \"The changes look great! The refactoring to use a background thread effectively resolves the UI freeze issue. I tested the functionality and confirmed that the UI remains responsive during bulk imports. Well done!\", \"submitted_at\": \"2026-11-03T03:13:00\"}], \"id\": \"github_com_salesforce_LeadForce_pull_53\"}\n{\"title\": \"Mitigate Bias in AI Model by Enhancing Training Data Diversity\", \"summary\": \"### Summary\\nThe AI model was producing skewed lead scores due to biases in the training dataset, which had a disproportionate representation of certain lead characteristics.\\n\\n### Changes Made\\n- Augmented the training dataset to include a more diverse range of lead characteristics, ensuring a balanced representation.\\n- Implemented data preprocessing steps to identify and mitigate potential biases in future datasets.\\n- Updated the model training pipeline to incorporate these changes.\\n\\n### Testing\\n- Conducted a series of tests to validate that the updated model produces more accurate and unbiased lead scores.\\n- Compared the new model's outputs against a benchmark dataset to ensure improved performance and fairness.\\n- Reviewed the distribution of lead scores to confirm the reduction of bias.\\n\\nThis fix aims to enhance the fairness and accuracy of the lead scoring system by addressing the root cause of bias in the training data.\", \"link\": \"https://github.com/salesforce/LeadForce/pull/54\", \"mergeable\": \"True\", \"merged\": \"True\", \"number\": \"54\", \"state\": \"closed\", \"user\": {\"login\": \"eid_207da0e7\"}, \"created_at\": \"2026-11-06T18:50:00\", \"reviews\": [{\"state\": \"APPROVED\", \"user\": {\"login\": \"eid_f98d7490\"}, \"comment\": \"The changes look great! The updated training data and preprocessing steps effectively address the bias issue. I've reviewed the test results, and they confirm that the model now produces more balanced lead scores. Approved for merge.\", \"submitted_at\": \"2026-11-06T17:18:00\"}], \"id\": \"github_com_salesforce_LeadForce_pull_54\"}\n{\"title\": \"Fix Data Type Mismatch in Lead Attributes\", \"summary\": \"### Summary\\nThis pull request addresses the issue of data type mismatches in lead attributes, which were causing errors in lead scoring algorithms and inaccurate prioritization.\\n\\n### Changes Made\\n- Updated the application layer to ensure correct data type casting during data insertion.\\n- Modified the database schema to align with the application layer's expected data types.\\n- Added validation checks to prevent future mismatches.\\n\\n### Testing\\n- Conducted unit tests to verify that data types are correctly cast during insertion.\\n- Performed integration tests to ensure lead scoring algorithms function accurately with the corrected data types.\\n- Validated that no existing data was corrupted during the schema update.\", \"link\": \"https://github.com/salesforce/LeadForce/pull/55\", \"mergeable\": \"True\", \"merged\": \"True\", \"number\": \"55\", \"state\": \"closed\", \"user\": {\"login\": \"eid_c39dc658\"}, \"created_at\": \"2026-11-15T18:23:00\", \"reviews\": [{\"state\": \"APPROVED\", \"user\": {\"login\": \"eid_99835861\"}, \"comment\": \"Looks great! The changes effectively resolve the data type mismatch issue, and the testing confirms that the fix works as intended. Approved.\", \"submitted_at\": \"2026-11-15T15:59:00\"}], \"id\": \"github_com_salesforce_LeadForce_pull_55\"}\n{\"title\": \"Optimize Data Serialization in API Gateway for Improved Performance\", \"summary\": \"### Summary\\nThis pull request addresses the data serialization bottleneck in the API Gateway, which was causing delays in data transmission and updates.\\n\\n### Issue\\nThe serialization process for lead data was inefficient due to the use of an outdated library, leading to slow data processing.\\n\\n### Changes Made\\n- Updated the serialization library to the latest version, which is optimized for complex data structures.\\n- Refactored the serialization logic to leverage new features and improvements in the updated library.\\n- Added unit tests to ensure the new serialization process is functioning correctly and efficiently.\\n\\n### Testing\\n- Conducted performance benchmarks comparing the old and new serialization processes, showing significant improvements in speed.\\n- Verified data integrity and accuracy through comprehensive unit and integration tests.\\n- Deployed changes to a staging environment for further validation and testing by the QA team.\", \"link\": \"https://github.com/salesforce/LeadForce/pull/48\", \"mergeable\": \"True\", \"merged\": \"True\", \"number\": \"48\", \"state\": \"closed\", \"user\": {\"login\": \"eid_cac9a0ac\"}, \"created_at\": \"2026-10-18T06:30:00\", \"reviews\": [{\"state\": \"APPROVED\", \"user\": {\"login\": \"eid_f98d7490\"}, \"comment\": \"The changes look great! The updated serialization library significantly improves performance, and the tests confirm the fix is effective. Approved for merge.\", \"submitted_at\": \"2026-10-18T05:30:00\"}], \"id\": \"github_com_salesforce_LeadForce_pull_48\"}\n{\"title\": \"Fix Real-Time Data Integration in AI Model Scoring\", \"summary\": \"### Summary\\nThis Pull Request addresses the issue where the AI model was failing to integrate real-time data updates, resulting in lead scores being calculated based on outdated information.\\n\\n### Changes Made\\n- Updated the data pipeline to ensure real-time data is correctly fed into the scoring algorithm.\\n- Refactored the data ingestion module to handle real-time updates more efficiently.\\n- Added logging to monitor data flow and detect any future integration issues promptly.\\n\\n### Testing\\n- Conducted unit tests to verify that real-time data is now correctly integrated into the scoring algorithm.\\n- Performed end-to-end testing in a staging environment to ensure lead scores are updated with the latest data.\\n- Monitored system performance to confirm that the fix does not introduce any latency or bottlenecks.\", \"link\": \"https://github.com/salesforce/LeadForce/pull/49\", \"mergeable\": \"True\", \"merged\": \"True\", \"number\": \"49\", \"state\": \"closed\", \"user\": {\"login\": \"eid_207da0e7\"}, \"created_at\": \"2026-10-19T21:42:00\", \"reviews\": [{\"state\": \"APPROVED\", \"user\": {\"login\": \"eid_f98d7490\"}, \"comment\": \"Looks great! The fix effectively resolves the real-time data integration issue, and the testing confirms that lead scores are now accurate. Approved for merge.\", \"submitted_at\": \"2026-10-19T19:07:00\"}], \"id\": \"github_com_salesforce_LeadForce_pull_49\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-iangarcia-LeadForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-a-aix-2eecee\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_a43a4389\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-07-20T15:09:00\", \"text\": \"Hi team, please check my PR for the HubSpot integration: https://github.com/salesforce/AIX/pull/29. This outlines the data mapping strategy to ensure data fields between AIX and HubSpot are correctly aligned and transformed. Let me know your thoughts! 😊\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260722-0-a4838\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260722-0-a4838\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-iangarcia-LeadForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-a-aix-2eecee\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_cac9a0ac\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-07-20T15:12:00\", \"text\": \"@eid_a43a4389 Thanks for sharing, I'll take a look now. 🔍\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260722-1-28850\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260722-1-28850\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-iangarcia-LeadForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-a-aix-2eecee\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_90359c89\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-07-20T15:15:00\", \"text\": \"Hey @eid_a43a4389, just skimmed through the PR. The mapping strategy looks solid. I'll dive deeper into the transformation logic next. 👍\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260722-2-73f7e\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260722-2-73f7e\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-iangarcia-