the lead scoring data. I'll work on the UI components to display scores and insights in a user-friendly manner.\\nCharlie Taylor: Sounds good, David. Let's make sure we integrate user feedback loops into the design process. We want to ensure the UI is intuitive and meets user needs.\\nBob Smith: Moving on to real-time engagement tracking, we need to discuss the event-driven architecture. This will allow us to capture and process lead interactions as they happen.\\nHannah Taylor: I'll take the lead on setting up the event-driven system. We can use Kafka for real-time data streaming and processing. This will ensure we have the scalability we need.\\nIan Miller: For predictive analytics, we should focus on refining our AI models. Regular retraining and dataset updates are crucial to maintain accuracy and reduce bias.\\nIan Brown: I'll oversee the AI model retraining process. We'll set up a schedule for periodic updates and ensure we're using diverse datasets to improve model performance.\\nGeorge Garcia: Regarding task prioritization, let's ensure we're aligned on deadlines. Are there any features at risk of missing their timelines?\\nBob Brown: The integration with CRM platforms might be a challenge. We need to ensure seamless data flow with Salesforce and HubSpot. I'll need some support on this.\\nIan Jones: I can assist with the CRM integration. Let's set up a meeting to discuss the APIs and data mapping strategies. We need to ensure efficient data handling.\\nHannah Taylor: Great collaboration, everyone. Let's finalize the feature roadmap. Ian Garcia, you'll handle security protocols. Fiona, you're on data structures. David, UI components. Charlie, event-driven architecture. Ian Brown, AI model retraining. Ian Jones and Bob Brown, CRM integration. Does everyone agree with these assignments?\\nIan Garcia: Yes, I'm clear on my tasks.\\nFiona Miller: Same here. I'll get started on the data structures.\\nDavid Smith: UI components are my focus. I'll ensure we have a user-friendly interface.\\nCharlie Taylor: Event-driven architecture is in good hands. I'll coordinate with the team for seamless implementation.\\nIan Miller: AI model retraining is a priority. I'll keep the team updated on progress.\\nIan Brown: CRM integration will be handled efficiently. Ian and I will ensure smooth data flow.\\nJulia Jones: Perfect. Let's keep communication open and address any issues as they arise. Thanks, everyone, for your input and collaboration.\\nHannah Taylor: Thanks, team. Let's reconvene next week to review our progress. Meeting adjourned.\", \"date\": \"2026-04-27T15:48:00\", \"document_type\": \"product-planning\", \"participants\": [\"eid_f98d7490\", \"eid_99835861\", \"eid_46e00bc4\", \"eid_8efef28a\", \"eid_b48f959b\", \"eid_207da0e7\", \"eid_a43a4389\", \"eid_a23a73c4\", \"eid_cac9a0ac\", \"eid_90359c89\", \"eid_c39dc658\", \"eid_9f4e2c6f\", \"eid_3f4b2681\", \"eid_07cc9100\", \"eid_652e8cd0\"], \"id\": \"product_dev_AIX_1\"}\n{\"transcript\": \"Attendees\\nIan Garcia, Ian Jones, Julia Jones, Bob Garcia, Hannah Taylor, Ian Garcia, Fiona Miller, Bob Brown, David Smith, Charlie Taylor, Ian Miller, Ian Brown, Hannah Taylor, George Garcia, Bob Smith\\nTranscript\\nHannah Taylor: Good morning, everyone. Let's kick off this sprint review by discussing the status of our completed PRs. Ian Garcia, could you start with the data encryption and access controls?\\nIan Garcia: Sure, Hannah. The data encryption and access controls have been successfully implemented. We've added robust encryption mechanisms and set up access control policies to ensure data security. Everything is working as expected.\\nJulia Jones: Great work, Ian. This is crucial for maintaining our data integrity and security. How about the Kafka infrastructure setup?\\nHannah Taylor: I can take that. The Kafka infrastructure is up and running. We've configured the brokers, topics, and partitions to handle real-time data streaming efficiently. It's scalable and reliable, ready for our lead engagement events.\\nBob Garcia: Fantastic, Hannah. This will really enhance our real-time data processing capabilities. Now, let's move on to the Salesforce API integration.\\nIan Garcia: The Salesforce API integration is complete. We've set up authentication, defined endpoints, and ensured smooth data flow between AIX and Salesforce. It's all tested and functioning well.\\nIan Jones: Awesome, Ian. This integration is a big step forward for us. Now, let's discuss the pending tasks and PRs. Starting with the AI-driven lead scoring feature, which involves conducting security audits for GDPR and CCPA compliance.\\nIan Garcia: That's assigned to me. I'll be implementing the security audits to ensure we're compliant with GDPR and CCPA regulations.\\nJulia Jones: Thanks, Ian. Please keep us updated on your progress. Next, we have the real-time engagement tracking task, which involves implementing a Kafka producer for lead engagement events.\\nHannah Taylor: That's on my plate. I'll handle the Kafka producer implementation to ensure it can manage high throughput and reliable message delivery.\\nBob Garcia: Great, Hannah. Let us know if you need any support. Moving on to the predictive analytics AI model retraining task.\\nIan Brown: I submitted a PR for the automated model retraining pipeline, but it needs some revisions. Charlie, could you take over and submit a new PR?\\nCharlie Taylor: Got it, Ian. I'll work on the new PR and ensure the pipeline is set up for regular model retraining.\\nJulia Jones: Thanks, Charlie. Finally, we have the CRM platform integration task, which involves implementing the HubSpot API integration.\\nIan Jones: That's assigned to me. I'll take care of the HubSpot API integration, covering authentication, endpoint configuration, and data handling.\\nBob Garcia: Perfect, Ian. Let's aim to have these tasks completed by the end of the sprint. If anyone encounters any blockers, please reach out. Thanks, everyone, for your hard work and 