\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-09T06:25:00\", \"text\": \"Agreed with Hannah. Maintaining backward compatibility is crucial. Let us know if you need any help with debugging the AppX issue. Also, did you update the authentication methods as part of this PR?\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261109-4-5d4d9\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261109-4-5d4d9\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-alicesmith-SearchForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-shaix-b12e0e\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_160fca3c\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-09T06:27:00\", \"text\": \"Thanks, @eid_51f0b41f and Bob! I appreciate the feedback. I'll prioritize fixing the AppX issue. As for the authentication methods, I did update them to align with the latest security protocols. I'll double-check to ensure everything is covered.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261109-5-ea112\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261109-5-ea112\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-alicesmith-SearchForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-shaix-b12e0e\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_51f0b41f\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-09T06:32:00\", \"text\": \"Sounds good, @eid_160fca3c. Once the AppX issue is resolved, we can re-run the tests and hopefully get this merged. Let us know if you need any assistance. 🚀\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261109-6-0027c\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261109-6-0027c\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-alicesmith-SearchForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-shaix-b12e0e\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_0aa7db32\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-09T06:33:00\", \"text\": \"Yeah, feel free to reach out if you need a second pair of eyes on the issue. Looking forward to the updates! 😊\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261109-7-c2fb3\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261109-7-c2fb3\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-alicesmith-SearchForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-shaix-b12e0e\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_160fca3c\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-09T06:37:00\", \"text\": \"Thanks, team! I'll keep you posted on the progress. Appreciate the support! 🙌\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261109-8-f47cd\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261109-8-f47cd\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-alicesmith-SearchForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-shaix-b12e0e\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_b7f0726e\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-29T10:31:00\", \"text\": \"Hi team, please check my PR for updating shAIX's API to ensure compatibility with the latest versions of third-party applications. Here's the link: https://github.com/salesforce/shAIX/pull/11. I've updated the API endpoints, ensured backward compatibility, and updated the documentation. Let me know your thoughts! 😊\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261130-0-84293\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261130-0-84293\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-alicesmith-SearchForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-shaix-b12e0e\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_0aa7db32\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-29T10:35:00\", \"text\": \"@eid_b7f0726e Thanks for the update! I'll start reviewing it now. Just to confirm, have all the integration tests passed with the supported third-party applications?\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261130-1-7d94d\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261130-1-7d94d\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-alicesmith-SearchForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-shaix-b12e0e\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_b7f0726e\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-29T10:39:00\", \"text\": \"Yes, @eid_0aa7db32, all integration tests have passed successfully. 🎉\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261130-2-467eb\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261130-2-467eb\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-alicesmith-SearchForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-shaix-b12e0e\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_51f0b41f\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-29T10:44:00\", \"text\": \"Hey @eid_b7f0726e, I just went through the changes. The updates to the API endpoints look solid, and I appreciate the detailed documentation. Everything seems to be in order from my side. LGTM, approved! 👍\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261130-3-f456d\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261130-3-f456d\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-alicesmith-SearchForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-shaix-b12e0e\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_160fca3c\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-29T10:49:00\", \"text\": \"Great work, @eid_b7f0726e! I checked the backward compatibility, and it looks like you've covered all the bases. The documentation updates are clear and concise. LGTM, approved! 🚀\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261130-4-e7aad\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261130-4-e7aad\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-alicesmith-SearchForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-shaix-b12e0e\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_0aa7db32\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-29T10:52:00\", \"text\": \"Just finished my review. The changes are well-implemented, and I didn't find any issues. Thanks for ensuring everything is compatible with the third-party apps. LGTM, approved! 🙌\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261130-5-6d3b5\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261130-5-6d3b5\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-alicesmith-SearchForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-shaix-b12e0e\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_b7f0726e\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-29T10:56:00\", \"text\": \"Thanks, everyone, for the quick reviews and approvals! I'll go ahead and merge the PR. Appreciate the feedback! 😊\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261130-6-1db2b\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261130-6-1db2b\"}\n{\"title\": \"Implement Responsive Auto-Suggestions Feature\", \"summary\": \"This PR aims to improve the responsiveness of the auto-suggestions feature in the search bar, ensuring suggestions appear quickly and accurately as users type.\", \"link\": \"https://github.com/salesforce/shAIX/pull/8\", \"mergeable\": \"True\", \"merged\": \"False\", \"number\": \"8\", \"state\": \"open\", \"user\": {\"login\": \"eid_3fa288cf\"}, \"created_at\": \"2026-11-11T14:24:00\", \"reviews\": [{\"state\": \"APPROVED\", \"user\": {\"login\": \"eid_4eec2a5a\"}, \"comment\": \"Just reviewed the code, and it looks solid! The auto-suggestions are indeed appearing within 200ms, and they seem very relevant to the input. Great job on that! 👏 LGTM, approved! 🚀\", \"submitted_at\": \"2026-11-11T21:56:00\"}, {\"state\": \"COMMENTED\", \"user\": {\"login\": \"eid_12c203a5\"}, \"comment\": \"I ran some performance tests, and there's no degradation in speed. Everything's running smoothly. Nice work, @eid_3fa288cf! 🎉 Same here, LGTM! Approved! 🙌\", \"submitted_at\": \"2026-11-11T21:58:00\"}], \"id\": \"github_com_salesforce_shAIX_pull_8\"}\n{\"transcript\": \"Attendees\\nJulia Taylor, Alice Smith, David Williams, George Davis, Charlie Miller, Fiona Davis, Julia Martinez, David Taylor, Emma Johnson, David Garcia, Alice Taylor, David Jones, Hannah Brown, George Davis, Charlie Miller, Bob Jones, Charlie Jones, Fiona Taylor, Hannah Brown, Alice Miller, George Johnson, Bob Miller, Julia Jones, Alice Jones\\nTranscript\\nJulia Taylor: Alright team, let's kick off this sprint review. We'll start by discussing the status of our completed PRs. First up, the 'Update NLP API to Support Hybrid Model Approach'. Alice, could you give us a quick overview?\\nAlice Smith: Sure, Julia. This update allows our NLP API to handle more complex queries by combining rule-based and machine learning techniques. We've seen a significant improvement in query processing flexibility and accuracy.\\nGeorge Davis: That's great to hear, Alice. How about the 'Develop API for Session Data Management'? David, can you fill us in?\\nDavid Williams: Absolutely, George. The API for session data management is up and running. It allows us to create, retrieve, and delete session information, which is crucial for our context-aware search feature.\\nFiona Davis: Fantastic work, David. And lastly, the 'Conduct A/B Testing for UI Changes'. Charlie, any insights?\\nCharlie Miller: Yes, Fiona. The A/B testing setup is complete, and we're currently gathering data on user engagement and satisfaction. Early results are promising, showing a preference for the new design.\\nJulia Taylor: Great progress, everyone. Now, let's move on to the pending tasks and PRs. First, we have 'Enhancing natural language processing capabilities'. Emma, this involves the 'Adjust Database Schema for Additional Training Data' PR. Are you ready to take this on?\\nEmma Johnson: Got it, Julia. I'll handle the database schema adjustments to accommodate the additional training data.\\nGeorge Davis: Thanks, Emma. Next, we have the 'Implementation of context awareness algorithms'. Alice, this is linked to the 'Integrate Context Awareness into AI Search Queries' PR. Can you confirm?\\nAlice Taylor: I confirm, George. I'll take care of integrating context awareness into our AI search queries using session data.\\nFiona Davis: Perfect. Lastly, we need to address 'Improving integration with third-party applications'. David Garcia, your PR needs some revisions. Can you update us on that?\\nDavid Garcia: Yes, Fiona. I've received feedback and will make the necessary revisions to ensure our integration scenarios are functioning as expected.\\nCharlie Miller: And Bob, you'll be working on a new PR for this task. Are you set to start?\\nBob Jones: Absolutely, Charlie. I'll submit a new PR once I've completed the integration tests.\\nJulia Taylor: Great teamwork, everyone. Let's keep up the momentum and ensure we meet our sprint goals. If there are no further questions, let's wrap up.\\nDavid Taylor: Just a quick note, if anyone needs assistance with their tasks, feel free to reach out. Collaboration is key.\\nDavid Williams: Thanks, David. We'll keep that in mind. Looking forward to another productive sprint.\", \"date\": \"2027-01-02T12:34:00\", \"document_type\": \"product-planning\", \"participants\": [\"eid_d0b6cb92\", \"eid_439a052b\", \"eid_6d14c4ec\", \"eid_887367ca\", \"eid_5b61c55e\", \"eid_efc9418c\", \"eid_aa99608e\", \"eid_9b8bc088\", \"eid_e5715d9e\", \"eid_160fca3c\", \"eid_13786f09\", \"eid_7db4431d\", \"eid_3fa288cf\", \"eid_990f697c\", \"eid_b7f0726e\", \"eid_0aa7db32\", \"eid_7bd14403\", \"eid_e7622cfb\", \"eid_51f0b41f\", \"eid_070b6e41\", \"eid_12c203a5\", \"eid_681e9def\", \"eid_b20b58ad\", \"eid_4eec2a5a\"], \"id\": \"product_dev_SearchForce_7\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-alicesmith-SearchForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-shaix-b12e0e\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_160fca3c\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-25T04:24:00\", \"text\": \"Hi team, please check my PR for enhancing error handling in our third-party integration: https://github.com/salesforce/shAIX/pull/3. I've added specific error messages, retry logic, and fallback procedures to improve resilience. Let me know your thoughts! 😊\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261028-0-04390\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261028-0-04390\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-alicesmith-SearchForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-shaix-b12e0e\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_b7f0726e\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-25T04:26:00\", \"text\": \"Hey @eid_160fca3c, thanks for sharing! I'll start reviewing it now. Just to confirm, you've documented all the new error handling mechanisms, right?\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261028-1-1ec88\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261028-1-1ec88\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-alicesmith-SearchForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-shaix-b12e0e\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_160fca3c\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-25T04:27:00\", \"text\": \"Yes, @eid_b7f0726e, all new mechanisms are documented in the README and inline comments. Let me know if anything's unclear!\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261028-2-94120\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261028-2-94120\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-alicesmith-SearchForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-shaix-b12e0e\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_0aa7db32\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-25T04:28:00\", \"text\": \"Jumping in to review as well. @eid_160fca3c, did you include unit tests for all the new error scenarios?\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261028-3-30b19\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261028-3-30b19\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-alicesmith-SearchForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-shaix-b12e0e\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_160fca3c\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-25T04:30:00\", \"text\": \"Absolutely, Bob! Each new error scenario has corresponding unit tests. You can find them in the `tests/error_handling` directory. 👍\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261028-4-0e566\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261028-4-0e566\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-alicesmith-SearchForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-shaix-b12e0e\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_b7f0726e\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-25T04:32:00\", \"text\": \"Just finished going through the code. The retry logic looks solid, and I appreciate the detailed comments. The integration tests also show a clear improvement in resilience. Great job! 👏\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261028-5-e9447\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261028-5-e9447\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-alicesmith-SearchForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-shaix-b12e0e\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_0aa7db32\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-25T04:36:00\", \"text\": \"I agree with Charlie. The code adheres to our standards, and the fallback procedures are well thought out. Everything looks good to me. LGTM, approved! ✅\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261028-6-91c33\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261028-6-91c33\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-alicesmith-SearchForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-shaix-b12e0e\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_b7f0726e\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-25T04:39:00\", \"text\": \"LGTM, approved! Thanks for the hard work, @eid_160fca3c. This will definitely make our integration more robust. 🚀\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261028-7-a3408\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261028-7-a3408\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-alicesmith-SearchForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-shaix-b12e0e\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_160fca3c\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-25T04:44:00\", \"text\": \"Thanks, @eid_b7f0726e and Bob! Appreciate the quick review and feedback. Let's get this merged! 🎉\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261028-8-24490\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261028-8-24490\"}\n{\"transcript\": \"Attendees\\nJulia Taylor, Alice Smith, David Williams, George Davis, Charlie Miller, Fiona Davis, Julia Martinez, David Taylor, Emma Johnson, David Garcia, Alice Taylor, David Jones, Hannah Brown, George Davis, Charlie Miller, Bob Jones, Charlie Jones, Fiona Taylor, Hannah Brown, Alice Miller, George Johnson, Bob Miller, Julia Jones, Alice Jones\\nTranscript\\nJulia Taylor: Alright team, let's kick off this sprint review. First, let's go over the completed PRs. Emma, can you start with the API documentation update?\\nEmma Johnson: Sure, Julia. The API documentation for third-party integration has been revised and expanded. We included more examples and troubleshooting tips, which should make it easier for developers to integrate with shAIX.\\nGeorge Davis: Great work, Emma. This will definitely help in reducing integration issues. Now, how about the redesign of the filter options?\\nAlice Smith: I handled that one. The filter options have been updated for better usability. We focused on making them more intuitive and accessible, which should enhance the user experience significantly.\\nCharlie Miller: Thanks, Alice. The feedback from the initial tests has been positive, so that's a win for us.\\nJulia Taylor: Alright, moving on to the pending tasks. Let's start with enhancing the natural language processing capabilities. Emma, your PR needs some revisions. Alice Jones, you'll be taking over this task, correct?\\nAlice Jones: Yes, that's right. I'll work on the new PR for the NLP API to support the hybrid model approach. I'll make sure to address the feedback from the previous submission.\\nGeorge Davis: Great, Alice. Please keep us updated on your progress.\\nJulia Taylor: Next, we have the implementation of context awareness algorithms. Alice Taylor, your PR needs revisions. Bob Miller, you'll be handling this next, correct?\\nBob Miller: Yes, I'll take care of the new PR for the session data management API. I'll ensure it aligns with our context-aware search goals.\\nFiona Davis: Thanks, Bob. This is a crucial part of our project, so let's aim for a robust implementation.\\nJulia Taylor: Moving on, we have the task of improving integration with third-party applications. David Garcia, you're up for this one, right?\\nDavid Garcia: Yes, I'll be developing and executing the integration tests. I'll make sure all scenarios are thoroughly validated.\\nCharlie Miller: Perfect, David. Let us know if you need any additional resources.\\nJulia Taylor: Lastly, we have the task of enhancing the user interface. Hannah, you're assigned to this, correct?\\nHannah Brown: Yes, I'll be setting up the A/B testing for the UI changes. I'll focus on comparing user engagement and satisfaction metrics.\\nJulia Martinez: Thanks, Hannah. This will be key in ensuring our UI changes are effective.\\nJulia Taylor: Alright, team. That wraps up our sprint review. Let's keep the momentum going and aim for another successful sprint. If there are no further questions, let's get to work!\", \"date\": \"2026-12-17T05:43:00\", \"document_type\": \"product-planning\", \"participants\": [\"eid_d0b6cb92\", \"eid_439a052b\", \"eid_6d14c4ec\", \"eid_887367ca\", \"eid_5b61c55e\", \"eid_efc9418c\", \"eid_aa99608e\", \"eid_9b8bc088\", \"eid_e5715d9e\", \"eid_160fca3c\", \"eid_13786f09\", \"eid_7db4431d\", \"eid_3fa288cf\", \"eid_990f697c\", \"eid_b7f0726e\", \"eid_0aa7db32\", \"eid_7bd14403\", \"eid_e7622cfb\", \"eid_51f0b41f\", \"eid_070b6e41\", \"eid_12c203a5\", \"eid_681e9def\", \"eid_b20b58ad\", \"eid_4eec2a5a\"], \"id\": \"product_dev_SearchForce_6\"}\n{\"transcript\": \"Attendees\\nJulia Taylor, Alice Smith, David Williams, George Davis, Charlie Miller, Fiona Davis, Julia Martinez, David Taylor, Emma Johnson, David Garcia, Alice Taylor, David Jones, Hannah Brown, George Davis, Charlie Miller, Bob Jones, Charlie Jones, Fiona Taylor, Hannah Brown, Alice Miller, George Johnson, Bob Miller, Julia Jones, Alice Jones\\nTranscript\\nJulia Taylor: Alright team, let's kick off this sprint review. We'll start by discussing the completed PRs. First up, we have the 'Refine NLU Models for Improved Context Understanding'. Great work on this, everyone. Any comments or feedback?\\nGeorge Davis: I just want to say that the improvements in context understanding are already showing positive results in our initial tests. Kudos to the team!\\nDavid Williams: Absolutely, the refined models are performing much better. The expanded dataset really made a difference.\\nJulia Taylor: Great to hear! Next, we have the 'Create Database Table for Session Data Storage'. This was crucial for our context-aware features. Any issues encountered during implementation?\\nAlice Smith: No major issues, but we should keep an eye on the indexing performance as we scale.\\nGeorge Davis: Good point, Alice. Let's monitor that closely.\\nJulia Taylor: Lastly, the 'Ensure API Compatibility with Third-Party Applications'. This was a big one. How did it go?\\nDavid Garcia: It went smoothly. We ensured compatibility with all major third-party apps, and the feedback has been positive so far.\\nJulia Taylor: Fantastic. Now, let's move on to the pending tasks and PR assignments. First, we have 'Enhancing natural language processing capabilities'. Emma, you're up for the 'Update NLP API to Support Hybrid Model Approach'.\\nEmma Johnson: Got it, I’ll handle this. Looking forward to implementing the hybrid model approach.\\nJulia Taylor: Great. Next, 'Implementation of context awareness algorithms'. Alice, you'll be working on the 'Develop API for Session Data Management'.\\nAlice Taylor: I confirm, I’ll take care of this implementation. I'll ensure the API is robust and efficient.\\nJulia Taylor: Perfect. Moving on to 'Improving integration with third-party applications'. David, you're assigned to 'Update API Documentation for Third-Party Integration'.\\nDavid Garcia: Understood, I'll make sure the documentation is comprehensive and user-friendly.\\nJulia Taylor: Lastly, 'Enhancing user interface'. Hannah, your PR needs additional revisions, and George, you'll work on a new PR for this.\\nHannah Brown: I'll make the necessary revisions and ensure the filter options are more intuitive.\\nGeorge Johnson: And I'll start fresh on the new PR to enhance usability. I'll coordinate with Hannah to ensure consistency.\\nJulia Taylor: Excellent. Let's aim to have these tasks completed by the end of the sprint. Any questions or concerns before we wrap up?\\nFiona Davis: Just a quick note, let's ensure we have regular check-ins to track progress and address any blockers.\\nJulia Taylor: Absolutely, Fiona. We'll schedule those. Thanks, everyone, for your hard work and dedication. Let's make this sprint a success!\", \"date\": \"2026-12-02T13:12:00\", \"document_type\": \"product-planning\", \"participants\": [\"eid_d0b6cb92\", \"eid_439a052b\", \"eid_6d14c4ec\", \"eid_887367ca\", \"eid_5b61c55e\", \"eid_efc9418c\", \"eid_aa99608e\", \"eid_9b8bc088\", \"eid_e5715d9e\", \"eid_160fca3c\", \"eid_13786f09\", \"eid_7db4431d\", \"eid_3fa288cf\", \"eid_990f697c\", \"eid_b7f0726e\", \"eid_0aa7db32\", \"eid_7bd14403\", \"eid_e7622cfb\", \"eid_51f0b41f\", \"eid_070b6e41\", \"eid_12c203a5\", \"eid_681e9def\", \"eid_b20b58ad\", \"eid_4eec2a5a\"], \"id\": \"product_dev_SearchForce_5\"}\n{\"transcript\": \"Attendees\\nJulia Taylor, Alice Smith, David Williams, George Davis, Charlie Miller, Fiona Davis, Julia Martinez, David Taylor, Emma Johnson, David Garcia, Alice Taylor, David Jones, Hannah Brown, George Davis, Charlie Miller, Bob Jones, Charlie Jones, Fiona Taylor, Hannah Brown, Alice Miller, George Johnson, Bob Miller, Julia Jones, Alice Jones\\nTranscript\\nJulia Taylor: Alright team, let's kick off this sprint review. We'll start by discussing the status of our completed PRs. First up, we have the 'Implement Session Data Structure for Context Awareness'. Emma, could you give us a quick overview?\\nEmma Johnson: Sure, Julia. This PR introduces a new data structure to store session data, which includes user ID and session timestamp. This will help us maintain context for AI search queries, making our search results more relevant.\\nGeorge Davis: Great work, Emma. This is a crucial step for enhancing our context awareness capabilities.\\nJulia Taylor: Next, we have 'Enhance Error Handling for Third-Party Integration'. David, could you walk us through this one?\\nDavid Garcia: Absolutely. We've implemented robust error handling mechanisms to improve resilience when integrating with third-party applications. This includes specific error messages, retry logic, and fallback procedures.\\nCharlie Miller: This will definitely help in reducing downtime and improving user experience. Well done, David.\\nJulia Taylor: Finally, we have 'Enhance Search Bar UI for Intuitiveness'. Hannah, could you share some insights on this?\\nHannah Brown: Sure, Julia. We've redesigned the search bar to make it more intuitive based on user feedback. Changes include layout adjustments, a new color scheme, and updated iconography.\\nFiona Davis: The new design looks great and should make the search experience much smoother for users.\\nJulia Taylor: Alright, let's move on to the pending tasks and PR assignments. First, we have 'Enhancing natural language processing capabilities'. Emma, your PR needs additional revisions. Alice, you'll be working on a new PR for this task.\\nAlice Jones: Got it, I'll handle this and submit a new PR soon.\\nJulia Taylor: Next, we have 'Implementation of context awareness algorithms'. Alice Taylor, you'll be setting up a new database table for session data storage.\\nAlice Taylor: I confirm, I'll take care of this implementation.\\nJulia Taylor: Moving on, we have 'Improving integration with third-party applications'. David Garcia, you'll be updating the API for compatibility with the latest versions of third-party applications.\\nDavid Garcia: Got it, I'll ensure the API is up to date and compatible.\\nJulia Taylor: Lastly, we have 'Enhancing user interface'. Hannah, you'll be working on implementing the responsive auto-suggestions feature.\\nHannah Brown: I confirm, I'll take care of this feature.\\nJulia Taylor: Great, thanks everyone. Let's make sure we stay on track and reach out if you need any help. That's it for today. Have a productive sprint!\", \"date\": \"2026-11-03T03:23:00\", \"document_type\": \"product-planning\", \"participants\": [\"eid_d0b6cb92\", \"eid_439a052b\", \"eid_6d14c4ec\", \"eid_887367ca\", \"eid_5b61c55e\", \"eid_efc9418c\", \"eid_aa99608e\", \"eid_9b8bc088\", \"eid_e5715d9e\", \"eid_160fca3c\", \"eid_13786f09\", \"eid_7db4431d\", \"eid_3fa288cf\", \"eid_990f697c\", \"eid_b7f0726e\", \"eid_0aa7db32\", \"eid_7bd14403\", \"eid_e7622cfb\", \"eid_51f0b41f\", \"eid_070b6e41\", \"eid_12c203a5\", \"eid_681e9def\", \"eid_b20b58ad\", \"eid_4eec2a5a\"], \"id\": \"product_dev_SearchForce_3\"}\n{\"title\": \"Develop API for Session Data Management\", \"summary\": \"Implement an API to manage session data, allowing for the creation, retrieval, and deletion of session information as needed for context-aware search.\", \"link\": \"https://github.com/salesforce/shAIX/pull/14\", \"mergeable\": \"True\", \"merged\": \"False\", \"number\": \"14\", \"state\": \"closed\", \"user\": {\"login\": \"eid_13786f09\"}, \"created_at\": \"2026-12-04T11:40:00\", \"reviews\": [{\"state\": \"CHANGES_REQUESTED\", \"user\": {\"login\": \"eid_4eec2a5a\"}, \"comment\": \"The endpoints for creating, retrieving, and deleting session data look solid. Great job on that! However, the API documentation is a bit sparse. It would be helpful to have more detailed examples for each endpoint, especially for new team members.\", \"submitted_at\": \"2026-12-04T21:24:00\"}, {\"state\": \"PENDING\", \"user\": {\"login\": \"eid_b20b58ad\"}, \"comment\": \"The endpoints are well-structured, but the input validation could be tightened up. Consider handling unexpected data types, overly large payloads, and ensuring all required fields are checked before processing.\", \"submitted_at\": \"2026-12-04T21:22:00\"}], \"id\": \"github_com_salesforce_shAIX_pull_14\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-alicesmith-SearchForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-shaix-b12e0e\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_0aa7db32\", \"timestamp\": \"2027-01-12T01:00:00\", \"text\": \"Hi team, please check my PR for the integration tests with third-party applications: https://github.com/salesforce/shAIX/pull/23. I've developed a suite of tests to ensure our interactions with external apps are solid. Let me know your thoughts! 😊\", \"utterranceID\": \"20270111-0-7e20d\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20270111-0-7e20d\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-alicesmith-SearchForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-shaix-b12e0e\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_070b6e41\", \"timestamp\": \"2027-01-12T01:05:00\", \"text\": \"@eid_0aa7db32 Thanks for sharing! I'll start reviewing it now. Excited to see how you've tackled the edge cases. 🔍\", \"utterranceID\": \"20270111-1-13f85\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20270111-1-13f85\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-alicesmith-SearchForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-shaix-b12e0e\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_7bd14403\", \"timestamp\": \"2027-01-12T01:09:00\", \"text\": \"Hey @eid_0aa7db32, just took a quick look. The automation part looks solid. I'll dive deeper into the scenarios covered. 👍\", \"utterranceID\": \"20270111-2-14059\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20270111-2-14059\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-alicesmith-SearchForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-shaix-b12e0e\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_160fca3c\", \"timestamp\": \"2027-01-12T01:14:00\", \"text\": \"Great work on this, @eid_0aa7db32! I'll focus on the CI/CD integration and make sure everything runs smoothly there. 🚀\", \"utterranceID\": \"20270111-3-a7e5a\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20270111-3-a7e5a\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-alicesmith-SearchForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-shaix-b12e0e\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_070b6e41\", \"timestamp\": \"2027-01-12T01:16:00\", \"text\": \"I've gone through the test scenarios, and they cover all the major and edge cases I could think of. The documentation is clear and concise. Well done! LGTM, approved! ✅\", \"utterranceID\": \"20270111-4-d950f\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20270111-4-d950f\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-alicesmith-SearchForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-shaix-b12e0e\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_7bd14403\", \"timestamp\": \"2027-01-12T01:20:00\", \"text\": \"Just finished my review. All tests are automated and integrate perfectly with our CI/CD pipeline. Everything passes without a hitch. Approved! 🎉\", \"utterranceID\": \"20270111-5-4d00a\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20270111-5-4d00a\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-alicesmith-SearchForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-shaix-b12e0e\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_160fca3c\", \"timestamp\": \"2027-01-12T01:25:00\", \"text\": \"Checked the test results and QA documentation. Everything looks great, and the QA team has already given their thumbs up. LGTM, approved! 🥳\", \"utterranceID\": \"20270111-6-1caf8\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20270111-6-1caf8\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-alicesmith-SearchForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-shaix-b12e0e\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_0aa7db32\", \"timestamp\": \"2027-01-12T01:26:00\", \"text\": \"Thanks, everyone! Appreciate the quick reviews and feedback. Glad to see everything's in order. Let's get this merged! 🚀\", \"utterranceID\": \"20270111-7-7a4bf\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20270111-7-7a4bf\"}\n{\"title\": \"Expand Training Data for Complex Query Patterns\", \"summary\": \"This PR focuses on expanding the training dataset to include more complex query patterns. The goal is to enhance the natural language understanding capabilities of shAIX by incorporating diverse and intricate query examples.\", \"link\": \"https://github.com/salesforce/shAIX/pull/5\", \"mergeable\": \"True\", \"merged\": \"False\", \"number\": \"5\", \"state\": \"open\", \"user\": {\"login\": \"eid_4eec2a5a\"}, \"created_at\": \"2026-11-05T11:24:00\", \"reviews\": [{\"state\": \"APPROVED\", \"user\": {\"login\": \"eid_681e9def\"}, \"comment\": \"The new training data looks great and covers a wide range of complex queries. Everything is properly formatted and integrated into the pipeline. Nice work!\", \"submitted_at\": \"2026-11-05T13:23:00\"}, {\"state\": \"COMMENTED\", \"user\": {\"login\": \"eid_12c203a5\"}, \"comment\": \"The integration into the training pipeline is seamless, and the unit tests have been updated to reflect these changes. Everything checks out. LGTM, approved!\", \"submitted_at\": \"2026-11-05T13:24:00\"}, {\"state\": \"PENDING\", \"user\": {\"login\": \"eid_e5715d9e\"}, \"comment\": \"The variety in the new data is impressive, and the thoroughness in updating the unit tests is appreciated. Great job! LGTM, approved!\", \"submitted_at\": \"2026-11-05T13:27:00\"}], \"id\": \"github_com_salesforce_shAIX_pull_5\"}\n{\"title\": \"Create Database Table for Session Data Storage\", \"summary\": \"Set up a new database table to store session data, indexed by user ID and session timestamp, to facilitate quick retrieval of context information.\", \"link\": \"https://github.com/salesforce/shAIX/pull/6\", \"mergeable\": \"True\", \"merged\": \"False\", \"number\": \"6\", \"state\": \"closed\", \"user\": {\"login\": \"eid_13786f09\"}, \"created_at\": \"2026-11-07T03:20:00\", \"reviews\": [{\"state\": \"CHANGES_REQUESTED\", \"user\": {\"login\": \"eid_12c203a5\"}, \"comment\": \"The table structure looks good, but the migration script needs to include the index creation for the session timestamp to ensure optimal query performance.\", \"submitted_at\": \"2026-11-07T13:09:00\"}, {\"state\": \"PENDING\", \"user\": {\"login\": \"eid_b20b58ad\"}, \"comment\": \"I agree with the need for indexing the session timestamp for performance. Everything else looks solid.\", \"submitted_at\": \"2026-11-07T13:11:00\"}], \"id\": \"github_com_salesforce_shAIX_pull_6\"}\n{\"title\": \"Ensure API Compatibility with Third-Party Applications\", \"summary\": \"Update shAIX's API to ensure compatibility with the latest versions of third-party applications. This involves reviewing API endpoints, data formats, and authentication methods.\", \"link\": \"https://github.com/salesforce/shAIX/pull/7\", \"mergeable\": \"True\", \"merged\": \"False\", \"number\": \"7\", \"state\": \"open\", \"user\": {\"login\": \"eid_160fca3c\"}, \"created_at\": \"2026-11-08T17:45:00\", \"reviews\": [{\"state\": \"CHANGES_REQUESTED\", \"user\": {\"login\": \"eid_51f0b41f\"}, \"comment\": \"Great work on the documentation updates! However, we need to address the AppX issue before moving forward. Once resolved, we can re-run the tests and proceed with merging.\", \"submitted_at\": \"2026-11-09T06:32:00\"}, {\"state\": \"COMMENTED\", \"user\": {\"login\": \"eid_0aa7db32\"}, \"comment\": \"Agreed with the need to address the AppX issue. Let us know if you need help with debugging. Looking forward to the updates!\", \"submitted_at\": \"2026-11-09T06:33:00\"}], \"id\": \"github_com_salesforce_shAIX_pull_7\"}\n{\"transcript\": \"Attendees\\nJulia Taylor, Alice Smith, David Williams, George Davis, Charlie Miller, Fiona Davis, Julia Martinez, David Taylor, Emma Johnson, David Garcia, Alice Taylor, David Jones, Hannah Brown, George Davis, Charlie Miller, Bob Jones, Charlie Jones, Fiona Taylor, Hannah Brown, Alice Miller, George Johnson, Bob Miller, Julia Jones, Alice Jones\\nTranscript\\nJulia Taylor: Alright team, let's kick off this sprint review. We'll start by discussing the status of our completed PRs. First up, we have the 'Adjust Database Schema for Additional Training Data'. Emma, could you give us a quick overview?\\nEmma Johnson: Sure, Julia. This PR involved modifying the database schema to store additional training data. The changes were necessary to support our enhanced NLP capabilities. Everything went smoothly, and the database is now optimized for efficient data retrieval.\\nGeorge Davis: Great work, Emma. This will definitely help us manage the data more effectively. Next, let's talk about 'Integrate Context Awareness into AI Search Queries'. David, could you update us on this?\\nDavid Williams: Absolutely, George. We modified the AI search algorithm to use session data for context awareness. This means our search results are now more relevant as they consider the user's session information. The integration tests showed significant improvements in search accuracy.\\nCharlie Miller: That's fantastic to hear, David. Context awareness is a key feature for SearchForce. Now, moving on to 'Test Integration Scenarios with Third-Party Applications'. Alice, could you fill us in?\\nAlice Smith: Of course, Charlie. We developed a suite of integration tests to ensure our interactions with third-party applications are seamless. All scenarios passed successfully, confirming that our integrations are functioning as expected.\\nFiona Davis: Excellent job, Alice. This is crucial for maintaining our product's reliability. Now, let's discuss the pending tasks. We have the 'Implementation of context awareness algorithms'. Julia, could you elaborate on the corresponding PR?\\nJulia Taylor: Sure, Fiona. The pending task involves implementing a session data cleanup mechanism. This is crucial for maintaining database efficiency and managing storage costs. The PR titled 'Implement Session Data Cleanup Mechanism' is linked to this task.\\nAlice Taylor: Got it, I’ll handle this. I'll ensure the cleanup mechanism is efficient and doesn't interfere with ongoing sessions.\\nDavid Taylor: Thanks, Alice. It's important to keep our database lean and efficient. Does anyone have any questions or need further clarification on this task?\\nHannah Brown: No questions from me, David. Just a quick note, Alice, if you need any help with the cleanup logic, feel free to reach out.\\nAlice Taylor: Thanks, Hannah. I’ll definitely reach out if I need any assistance.\\nGeorge Davis: Alright, if there are no more questions, let's wrap up. Great work, everyone. Let's keep up the momentum and make sure we hit our targets for the next sprint.\\nJulia Taylor: Thanks, George. Let's aim for another productive sprint. Meeting adjourned!\", \"date\": \"2027-01-16T13:30:00\", \"document_type\": \"product-planning\", \"participants\": [\"eid_d0b6cb92\", \"eid_439a052b\", \"eid_6d14c4ec\", \"eid_887367ca\", \"eid_5b61c55e\", \"eid_efc9418c\", \"eid_aa99608e\", \"eid_9b8bc088\", \"eid_e5715d9e\", \"eid_160fca3c\", \"eid_13786f09\", \"eid_7db4431d\", \"eid_3fa288cf\", \"eid_990f697c\", \"eid_b7f0726e\", \"eid_0aa7db32\", \"eid_7bd14403\", \"eid_e7622cfb\", \"eid_51f0b41f\", \"eid_070b6e41\", \"eid_12c203a5\", \"eid_681e9def\", \"eid_b20b58ad\", \"eid_4eec2a5a\"], \"id\": \"product_dev_SearchForce_8\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"planning-shAIX\", \"channelID\": \"ch-shaix-1539d5\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_887367ca\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-02T11:16:00\", \"text\": \"Hi team, I just wanted to kick off our discussion about the shAIX product. Let's start by reviewing the documents from the last release. Here are the <https://sf-internal.slack.com/archives/docs/chprox_market_research_report_final|chprox_market_research_report_final> and <https://sf-internal.slack.com/archives/docs/latest_shaix_market_research_report|latest_shaix_market_research_report>.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260902-0-f2e36\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260902-0-f2e36\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"planning-shAIX\", \"channelID\": \"ch-shaix-1539d5\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_d0b6cb92\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-02T11:21:00\", \"text\": \"Thanks, George. I'll take a look at the market research reports. It's crucial to understand the context and intent behind the queries our users are making.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260902-1-f3870\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260902-1-f3870\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"planning-shAIX\", \"channelID\": \"ch-shaix-1539d5\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_9b8bc088\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-02T11:25:00\", \"text\": \"I've got the Product Vision Document here: <https://sf-internal.slack.com/archives/docs/chprox_product_vision_document_final|chprox_product_vision_document_final> and <https://sf-internal.slack.com/archives/docs/latest_shaix_product_vision_document|latest_shaix_product_vision_document>. Let's ensure we're aligned with the original vision.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260902-2-1e974\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260902-2-1e974\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"planning-shAIX\", \"channelID\": \"ch-shaix-1539d5\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_5b61c55e\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-02T11:28:00\", \"text\": \"Great, thanks David. I'll review the Product Requirements Document: <https://sf-internal.slack.com/archives/docs/chprox_product_requirements_document_final|chprox_product_requirements_document_final> and <https://sf-internal.slack.com/archives/docs/latest_shaix_product_requirements_document|latest_shaix_product_requirements_document>.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260902-3-55f12\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260902-3-55f12\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"planning-shAIX\", \"channelID\": \"ch-shaix-1539d5\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_6d14c4ec\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-02T11:31:00\", \"text\": \"I'll dive into the Technical Specifications Document: <https://sf-internal.slack.com/archives/docs/chprox_technical_specifications_document_final|chprox_technical_specifications_document_final> and <https://sf-internal.slack.com/archives/docs/latest_shaix_technical_specifications_document|latest_shaix_technical_specifications_document>. We need to ensure our architecture supports the AI capabilities effectively.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260902-4-48310\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260902-4-48310\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"planning-shAIX\", \"channelID\": \"ch-shaix-1539d5\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_3fa288cf\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-02T11:35:00\", \"text\": \"I'll check out the System Design Document: <https://sf-internal.slack.com/archives/docs/chprox_system_design_document_final|chprox_system_design_document_final> and <https://sf-internal.slack.com/archives/docs/latest_shaix_system_design_document|latest_shaix_system_design_document>. It's important to understand how everything fits together.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260902-5-07b64\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260902-5-07b64\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"planning-shAIX\", \"channelID\": \"ch-shaix-1539d5\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_efc9418c\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-02T11:39:00\", \"text\": \"Thanks, everyone. Once we've reviewed these, let's regroup to discuss any potential improvements or issues we might foresee.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260902-6-4c843\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260902-6-4c843\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"planning-shAIX\", \"channelID\": \"ch-shaix-1539d5\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_160fca3c\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-02T11:41:00\", \"text\": \"Sounds good. I'll also keep an eye on any feedback or issues reported by customers and QA specialists. Let's make sure we're addressing those as we move forward.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260902-7-bfd33\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260902-7-bfd33\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"planning-shAIX\", \"channelID\": \"ch-shaix-1539d5\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_d0b6cb92\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-03T16:52:00\", \"text\": \"@here here’s a quick video showcasing the updates in our last release https://sf-internal.slack.com/archives/chProX/demo_4\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261008-0-0be88\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261008-0-0be88\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"planning-shAIX\", \"channelID\": \"ch-shaix-1539d5\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"slack_admin_bot\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-04T19:38:00\", \"text\": \"@eid_9a9cf08a joined planning-shAIX.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260904-11-399da\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260904-11-399da\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"planning-shAIX\", \"channelID\": \"ch-shaix-1539d5\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"slack_admin_bot\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-06T23:26:00\", \"text\": \"@eid_6148bfae, @eid_abff6bea joined planning-shAIX.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260906-12-ce9d4\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260906-12-ce9d4\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"planning-shAIX\", \"channelID\": \"ch-shaix-1539d5\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_6148bfae\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-07T07:20:00\", \"text\": \"Hi team, QA team found some issues in the last release of shAIX. The report came from QA Specialist eid_7c6dd6a6.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260930-0-84eb2\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260930-0-84eb2\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"planning-shAIX\", \"channelID\": \"ch-shaix-1539d5\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_439a052b\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-07T07:23:00\", \"text\": \"Thanks, Emma. What exactly did they find?\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260930-1-f00d3\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260930-1-f00d3\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"planning-shAIX\", \"channelID\": \"ch-shaix-1539d5\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_f944b0ee\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-07T07:25:22\", \"text\": \"@here Read about how AI is redefining enterprise search in this article. It covers the impact of AI on improving search relevance and user experience. https://www.forbes.com/sites/forbestechcouncil/2023/ai-redefining-enterprise-search/\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260907-15-e8d4e\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260907-15-e8d4e\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"planning-shAIX\", \"channelID\": \"ch-shaix-1539d5\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_6148bfae\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-07T07:26:00\", \"text\": \"The main issue is with integration. It seems inconsistent with third-party apps, leading to incomplete data retrieval.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260930-2-17cfd\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260930-2-17cfd\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"planning-shAIX\", \"channelID\": \"ch-shaix-1539d5\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_abff6bea\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-07T07:31:00\", \"text\": \"Could it be an API compatibility issue? Maybe the third-party apps updated their APIs.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260930-3-5bf0a\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260930-3-5bf0a\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"planning-shAIX\", \"channelID\": \"ch-shaix-1539d5\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_d0b6cb92\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-07T07:32:00\", \"text\": \"@eid_abff6bea That's possible. We should check if there have been any recent changes in their API versions.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260930-4-44fbc\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260930-4-44fbc\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"planning-shAIX\", \"channelID\": \"ch-shaix-1539d5\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_6d14c4ec\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-07T07:36:00\", \"text\": \"Another angle could be operational. Maybe there's a lack of standardized integration protocols.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260930-5-6e84b\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260930-5-6e84b\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"planning-shAIX\", \"channelID\": \"ch-shaix-1539d5\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_439a052b\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-07T07:40:00\", \"text\": \"Good point, David. Standardizing protocols could help reduce these inconsistencies.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260930-6-d4514\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260930-6-d4514\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"planning-shAIX\", \"channelID\": \"ch-shaix-1539d5\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_6148bfae\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-07T07:41:00\", \"text\": \"Also, the design might be lacking in error handling for integration failures. We should look into that.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260930-7-055f5\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260930-7-055f5\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"planning-shAIX\", \"channelID\": \"ch-shaix-1539d5\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_d0b6cb92\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-07T07:46:00\", \"text\": \"Agreed, Emma. Better error handling could prevent data retrieval issues from going unnoticed.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260930-8-dd322\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260930-8-dd322\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"planning-shAIX\", \"channelID\": \"ch-shaix-1539d5\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_abff6bea\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-07T07:49:00\", \"text\": \"Let's make sure to document these issues and potential causes in our planning documents for the next release.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260930-9-2b74f\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260930-9-2b74f\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"planning-shAIX\", \"channelID\": \"ch-shaix-1539d5\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_6d14c4ec\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-07T07:53:00\", \"text\": \"Yes, definitely. We need to ensure these are addressed in the next iteration of shAIX.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260930-10-b6b58\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260930-10-b6b58\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"planning-shAIX\", \"channelID\": \"ch-shaix-1539d5\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_439a052b\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-07T07:54:00\", \"text\": \"I'll start drafting the documentation for this. Thanks, everyone!\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260930-11-fa310\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260930-11-fa310\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"planning-shAIX\", \"channelID\": \"ch-shaix-1539d5\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"slack_admin_bot\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-08T09:29:00\", \"text\": \"@eid_f944b0ee, @eid_5a940dab joined planning-shAIX.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260908-25-0f05e\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260908-25-0f05e\"}\nAttendees\nJulia Taylor, Alice Smith, David Williams, George Davis, Charlie Miller, Fiona Davis, Julia Martinez, David Taylor, Emma Johnson, David Garcia, Alice Taylor, David Jones, Hannah Brown, George Davis, Charlie Miller, Bob Jones, Charlie Jones, Fiona Taylor, Hannah Brown, Alice Miller, George Johnson, Bob Miller, Julia Jones, Alice Jones\nTranscript\nDavid Taylor: Team, let’s get started. Today our focus is on finalizing the next set of features for Salesforce AI Search. We need to ensure these align with our product goals and technical specifications. Let's dive into the precise feature discussion first.\nGeorge Davis: Absolutely, David. The first feature we need to discuss is enhancing our natural language processing capabilities. This is crucial for improving user query understanding and delivering more accurate search results.\nDavid Williams: For this, we should consider expanding our training data to include more complex query patterns. We also need to refine our NLU models. Emma, could you take the lead on this?\nEmma Johnson: Sure, David. I'll start by reviewing our current datasets and identify gaps. We might need to integrate additional data sources to improve model accuracy.\nAlice Smith: Great. The second feature is the implementation of context awareness algorithms. This will help us retain context across user interactions, making search results more relevant.\nAlice Taylor: I suggest we use a session-based approach to maintain context. We can store session data temporarily and use it to refine search results. I'll draft a proposal for the data structures and APIs needed.\nCharlie Miller: Sounds good, Alice. The third feature is improving our integration with third-party applications. We need to ensure our APIs are robust and well-documented.\nDavid Garcia: For this, we should enhance our error handling mechanisms and ensure API compatibility. I'll work on updating the API documentation and testing integration scenarios.\nFiona Davis: The fourth feature is enhancing our user interface. We need to incorporate more user feedback and improve the flexibility of search parameter configurations.\nHannah Brown: I can take this on. I'll gather recent user feedback and work with the design team to implement necessary UI changes. We should also consider A/B testing to validate improvements.\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"planning-shAIX\", \"channelID\": \"ch-shaix-1539d5\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_aa99608e\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-24T01:44:00\", \"text\": \"Hi team, let's review the Product Vision Document and update it based on the latest issues reported. We've got some challenges to address, like AI misinterpreting complex queries and integration inconsistencies. Let's dive in! 🚀\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260923-0-9f528\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260923-0-9f528\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"planning-shAIX\", \"channelID\": \"ch-shaix-1539d5\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_6d14c4ec\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-24T01:45:00\", \"text\": \"Thanks, Julia! For the AI misinterpretation issue, I think we should enhance the 'Intelligent Search Algorithms' section. We could specify the need for improved NLU capabilities and more diverse training data for complex queries. Thoughts? 🤔\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260923-1-c2df5\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260923-1-c2df5\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"planning-shAIX\", \"channelID\": \"ch-shaix-1539d5\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_d0b6cb92\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-24T01:49:11\", \"text\": \"@here For those interested in AI search, the Haystack library is a fantastic resource for building search systems that understand context and intent. https://github.com/deepset-ai/haystack\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260924-101-2254f\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260924-101-2254f\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"planning-shAIX\", \"channelID\": \"ch-shaix-1539d5\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_abff6bea\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-24T01:50:00\", \"text\": \"@eid_6d14c4ec, I agree. We should also consider adding a subsection on user feedback loops to continuously refine these algorithms. This could help in adapting to new query patterns over time.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260923-2-3afcc\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260923-2-3afcc\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"planning-shAIX\", \"channelID\": \"ch-shaix-1539d5\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_439a052b\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-24T01:54:00\", \"text\": \"On the integration front, maybe we should add a point under 'Integration' about establishing standardized protocols for third-party apps. This could help mitigate API compatibility issues.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260923-3-fa265\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260923-3-fa265\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"planning-shAIX\", \"channelID\": \"ch-shaix-1539d5\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_d0b6cb92\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-24T01:57:00\", \"text\": \"Good point, Alice. We should also enhance error handling mechanisms. Maybe a dedicated section on 'Error Handling and Recovery' could be beneficial? This would address incomplete data retrieval issues.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260923-4-66b97\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260923-4-66b97\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"planning-shAIX\", \"channelID\": \"ch-shaix-1539d5\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_6148bfae\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-24T02:02:00\", \"text\": \"For the performance issues, under 'Scalability', we might want to emphasize the need for better load balancing strategies and server resource optimization. This could help with the slow performance during peak times.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260923-5-03564\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260923-5-03564\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"planning-shAIX\", \"channelID\": \"ch-shaix-1539d5\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_aa99608e\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-24T02:05:00\", \"text\": \"Great suggestions, everyone! 😊 Let's also consider adding more customization options in the 'User Interface' section to address the difficulty users face in customizing search parameters.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260923-6-949f4\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260923-6-949f4\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"planning-shAIX\", \"channelID\": \"ch-shaix-1539d5\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_abff6bea\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-24T02:09:00\", \"text\": \"Yes, and maybe a note on improving user training and documentation under 'Operational' aspects could be useful. This might help users better understand customization features.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260923-7-3282a\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260923-7-3282a\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"planning-shAIX\", \"channelID\": \"ch-shaix-1539d5\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_6d14c4ec\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-24T02:10:00\", \"text\": \"Regarding reliability, we should bolster the 'Performance Monitoring' section with more robust monitoring and alert systems. This could help us catch and address downtime issues more proactively.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260923-8-75f25\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260923-8-75f25\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"planning-shAIX\", \"channelID\": \"ch-shaix-1539d5\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_aa99608e\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-24T02:12:00\", \"text\": \"Thanks for the input, team! Here's a quick summary: \\n- Enhance NLU and training data in 'Intelligent Search Algorithms'\\n- Add standardized protocols and error handling in 'Integration'\\n- Improve load balancing in 'Scalability'\\n- Expand customization in 'User Interface'\\n- Strengthen monitoring in 'Performance Monitoring'\\nLet's work on these updates and reconvene next week to finalize. 👍\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260923-9-0040b\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260923-9-0040b\"}\n\nIntegration: Salesforce AI Search integrates seamlessly with Salesforce CRM, Service Cloud, and Marketing Cloud through robust APIs and connectors. This integration enhances search capabilities without disrupting existing workflows, allowing users to access and retrieve data efficiently. The system supports various data formats and ensures compatibility with Salesforce's existing infrastructure, providing a cohesive user experience. Additionally, a standardized protocol for third-party integrations has been implemented, along with improved error handling mechanisms. API compatibility requirements are clearly documented to assist third-party developers in integrating their solutions effectively.\nIntelligent Search Algorithms: At the core of Salesforce AI Search are intelligent search algorithms that leverage machine learning to understand user intent. These algorithms refine user queries to deliver precise and relevant results, improving search accuracy and user satisfaction. The system supports natural language processing, enabling users to perform searches in a conversational manner, further enhancing usability. Enhanced NLU capabilities have been specified, and the training data has been expanded to accommodate complex query patterns. A feedback loop mechanism is implemented for continuous learning from user interactions, improving AI accuracy over time.\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"planning-shAIX\", \"channelID\": \"ch-shaix-1539d5\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_aa99608e\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-26T11:47:00\", \"text\": \"Here is the updated <https://sf-internal.slack.com/archives/docs/new_shaix_product_vision_document|Product Vision Document>, thank you everyone!\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260926-0-0a300\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260926-0-0a300\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"planning-shAIX\", \"channelID\": \"ch-shaix-1539d5\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_887367ca\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-27T17:32:00\", \"text\": \"Hi team, let's review the Product Requirements Document and update it based on the latest issues reported. We need to address the AI's misinterpretation of complex queries, integration inconsistencies, slow performance during peak times, customization difficulties, and reliability issues. Let's dive in! 🚀\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260927-0-496b5\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260927-0-496b5\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"planning-shAIX\", \"channelID\": \"ch-shaix-1539d5\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_439a052b\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-27T17:34:00\", \"text\": \"Thanks, George! For the AI misinterpretation issue, I suggest we enhance the 'Intelligent Search Algorithms' section to include improvements in NLU capabilities. We should also consider expanding our training data to cover more complex query patterns. Thoughts, @eid_6d14c4ec?\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260927-1-41413\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260927-1-41413\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"planning-shAIX\", \"channelID\": \"ch-shaix-1539d5\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_6d14c4ec\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-27T17:38:00\", \"text\": \"I agree, Alice. We could also add a subsection on 'Context Awareness' to improve how the system handles complex queries. This might involve refining our algorithms to better understand user context. @eid_abff6bea, any UX insights on this?\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260927-2-660e2\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260927-2-660e2\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"planning-shAIX\", \"channelID\": \"ch-shaix-1539d5\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_abff6bea\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-27T17:42:00\", \"text\": \"Great points, David. From a UX perspective, we should ensure that the interface provides feedback when a query is too complex or misunderstood. This could guide users to rephrase their queries. Adding this to the 'User Interface' section could be beneficial.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260927-3-1ab8e\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260927-3-1ab8e\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"planning-shAIX\", \"channelID\": \"ch-shaix-1539d5\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_4f731d34\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-27T17:45:00\", \"text\": \"Regarding integration issues, we should update the 'Integration' section to include standardized protocols and improved error handling. This will help with API compatibility and data retrieval consistency. @eid_5a940dab, what do you think?\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260927-4-9b87b\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260927-4-9b87b\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"planning-shAIX\", \"channelID\": \"ch-shaix-1539d5\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_5a940dab\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-27T17:47:00\", \"text\": \"I agree, Ian. We should also consider adding a monitoring system for third-party integrations to quickly identify and resolve issues. This could be part of the 'Performance Monitoring' section.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260927-5-4a31c\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260927-5-4a31c\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"planning-shAIX\", \"channelID\": \"ch-shaix-1539d5\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_d0b6cb92\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-27T17:52:00\", \"text\": \"For the performance issues during peak times, we should enhance the 'Scalability' section. Let's include strategies for better load balancing and possibly upgrading server resources. @eid_b34186ad, any operational insights?\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260927-6-76e76\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260927-6-76e76\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"planning-shAIX\", \"channelID\": \"ch-shaix-1539d5\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_b34186ad\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-27T17:55:00\", \"text\": \"Yes, Julia. We need to ensure our load balancing strategies are robust enough to handle peak loads. Including a plan for regular stress testing in the 'Performance Monitoring' section could help us stay ahead of these issues.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260927-7-96f6e\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260927-7-96f6e\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"planning-shAIX\", \"channelID\": \"ch-shaix-1539d5\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_f944b0ee\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-27T17:58:00\", \"text\": \"On customization difficulties, we should expand the 'User Interface' section to offer more flexible search parameter configurations. Also, better documentation and training resources could be added to the 'Operational' part of the document.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260927-8-cd83f\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260927-8-cd83f\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"planning-shAIX\", \"channelID\": \"ch-shaix-1539d5\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_887367ca\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-27T18:02:00\", \"text\": \"Thanks for the input, everyone! To summarize, we'll enhance NLU capabili",
