 it done by the end of this sprint to align with our release schedule.\\nJulia Smith: Understood, I'll prioritize it accordingly.\\nJulia Martinez: Great, thanks everyone. Let's keep up the good work and push forward with these tasks. Meeting adjourned.\", \"date\": \"2026-11-22T11:03:00\", \"document_type\": \"product-planning\", \"participants\": [\"eid_91523bad\", \"eid_b6a30126\", \"eid_caa2e58d\", \"eid_2d8eff4d\", \"eid_a253c65a\", \"eid_4b38019b\", \"eid_2347b567\", \"eid_bac7c6c4\", \"eid_edf6a3fc\", \"eid_4df3bcc2\", \"eid_54905dcb\", \"eid_4555ba9c\", \"eid_3e076e53\", \"eid_5058fefc\", \"eid_a0fe567d\"], \"id\": \"product_dev_EdgeForce_7\"}\n{\"transcript\": \"Attendees\\nJulia Martinez, Charlie Martinez, Bob Miller, David Miller, Hannah Brown, Charlie Davis, Julia Smith, Julia Jones, Fiona Taylor, Alice Miller, Alice Garcia, Ian Jones, Charlie Miller, Fiona Brown, Hannah Jones\\nTranscript\\nHannah Brown: Team, let’s get started. Today our focus is on finalizing the next set of features for Einstein Edge AI. We need to ensure our development roadmap aligns with our product goals, particularly in enhancing core functionalities and expanding device support.\\nBob Miller: Absolutely, Hannah. I think we should start by discussing the high-level tasks. First, we need to enhance our edge processing capabilities to handle more complex AI models. Second, we should expand our device compatibility to include more sensor types. Third, we need to improve our integration layer with additional APIs for third-party applications. Lastly, let's focus on enhancing our security features.\\nJulia Martinez: For the edge processing enhancements, we should look into optimizing our current algorithms. Charlie, do you think we should consider using TensorFlow Lite for better performance on edge devices?\\nCharlie Martinez: Yes, Julia, TensorFlow Lite could be a great fit. It’s lightweight and designed for mobile and edge devices. We’ll need to refactor some of our existing models to ensure compatibility, but the performance gains should be worth it.\\nCharlie Davis: I can take on the task of refactoring the models. I’ll also look into the data structures we’re using to see if there are any optimizations we can make there.\\nDavid Miller: Great. For the device compatibility, we need to ensure our system can support a wider range of sensors. Julia Smith, could you lead the effort on conducting hardware compatibility checks?\\nJulia Smith: Sure, David. I’ll start by reviewing the current sensor types we support and identify any gaps. We might need to update our device layer to accommodate new protocols.\\nFiona Taylor: Regarding the integration layer, I suggest we focus on developing RESTful APIs first. They’re widely used and will make it easier for third-party applications to integrate with our system.\\nAlice Miller: I agree, Fiona. We should also consider GraphQL for more complex queries. It could provide more flexibility for developers using our APIs.\\nAlice Garcia: I can work on setting up the initial RESTful API framework. Once that’s in place, we can explore adding GraphQL support.\\nIan Jones: For security, we need to ensure our data encryption and authentication mechanisms are up to date. I suggest we implement JWT authentication for better security and scalability.\\nCharlie Miller: I can handle the JWT implementation. We’ll need to update our access control policies to integrate with this new system.\\nFiona Brown: Before we wrap up, are there any concerns about timelines or resources? We need to ensure no one is overloaded and that we can meet our deadlines.\\nHannah Jones: I’m a bit concerned about the timeline for the API development. If we’re adding both REST and GraphQL, it might take longer than expected.\\nHannah Brown: Good point, Hannah. Let’s prioritize RESTful APIs first and schedule GraphQL for the next phase. This way, we can ensure we meet our immediate integration goals.\\nBob Miller: Agreed. Let’s finalize the assignments: Charlie Davis will handle model refactoring, Julia Smith will lead device compatibility checks, Fiona Taylor will start on RESTful APIs, and Ian Jones will implement JWT authentication.\\nJulia Martinez: Sounds like a solid plan. Let’s make sure we have regular check-ins to track progress and address any issues that arise.\\nCharlie Martinez: Absolutely. Let’s aim for a weekly sync to keep everyone updated. If there are no further questions, I think we’re all set.\\nHannah Brown: Great work, team. Let’s make sure we stay on track and deliver these features on time. Meeting adjourned.\", \"date\": \"2026-09-23T04:09:00\", \"document_type\": \"product-planning\", \"participants\": [\"eid_91523bad\", \"eid_b6a30126\", \"eid_caa2e58d\", \"eid_2d8eff4d\", \"eid_a253c65a\", \"eid_4b38019b\", \"eid_2347b567\", \"eid_bac7c6c4\", \"eid_edf6a3fc\", \"eid_4df3bcc2\", \"eid_54905dcb\", \"eid_4555ba9c\", \"eid_3e076e53\", \"eid_5058fefc\", \"eid_a0fe567d\"], \"id\": \"product_dev_EF_AIX_1\"}\n{\"transcript\": \"Attendees\\nJulia Martinez, Charlie Martinez, Bob Miller, David Miller, Hannah Brown, Charlie Davis, Julia Smith, Julia Jones, Fiona Taylor, Alice Miller, Alice Garcia, Ian Jones, Charlie Miller, Fiona Brown, Hannah Jones\\nTranscript\\nJulia Martinez: Alright team, let's kick off this sprint review. First, let's go over the completed PRs. Charlie, can you start with the user authentication endpoints?\\nCharlie Martinez: Sure, Julia. The user authentication endpoints are up and running. We've implemented both login and registration functionalities, and everything's been tested thoroughly. No issues reported so far.\\nBob Miller: Great work, Charlie. This is crucial for securing our API. How about the JWT token verification middleware?\\nDavid Miller: I can take that. The middleware for JWT token verification is also complete. It’s working as expected, ensuring only requests with valid tokens can access protected routes.\\nHannah Brown: Fantastic. These are significant steps forward for our security. Now, let's move on to the pending tasks. First up, the hardware compatibility checks. Julia Smith, can you update us on the status?\\nJulia Smith: Sure, Hannah. I submitted a PR for updating the device layer to enhance protocol handling, but it needs some revisions. Fiona, you'll be taking over this, right?\\nFiona Taylor: Yes, Julia. I'll work on the new PR and make sure to address the feedback. I'll submit it by the end of the week.\\nJulia Martinez: Great, Fiona. Please keep us posted on your progress. Next, we have the development of the RESTful API framework. Alice Garcia, you're up for this task, correct?\\nAlice Garcia: That's right, Julia. I'll be working on creating the data retrieval endpoints. I'll start on this today and aim to have a draft by mid-week.\\nBob Miller: Perfect, Alice. This will be key for enabling real-time insights. Lastly, we have the implementation of JWT authentication for security. Charlie Miller, you're handling this one?\\nCharlie Miller: Yes, Bob. I'll update the access control policies to integrate with the new JWT authentication system. I'll ensure that user permissions are checked based on the JWT claims.\\nDavid Miller: Sounds good, Charlie. Do you have an estimated timeline for this?\\nCharlie Miller: I plan to have it ready for review by the end of next week.\\nHannah Brown: Alright, team. Let's make sure we stay on track with these tasks. If anyone needs help or runs into issues, don't hesitate to reach out. Thanks, everyone, for your hard work.\\nJulia Martinez: Yes, thank you all. Let's keep the momentum going. Meeting adjourned.\", \"date\": \"2026-11-07T00:40:00\", \"document_type\": \"product-planning\", \"participants\": [\"eid_91523bad\", \"eid_b6a30126\", \"eid_caa2e58d\", \"eid_2d8eff4d\", \"eid_a253c65a\", \"eid_4b38019b\", \"eid_2347b567\", \"eid_bac7c6c4\", \"eid_edf6a3fc\", \"eid_4df3bcc2\", \"eid_54905dcb\", \"eid_4555ba9c\", \"eid_3e076e53\", \"eid_5058fefc\", \"eid_a0fe567d\"], \"id\": \"product_dev_EdgeForce_6\"}\n{\"transcript\": \"Attendees\\nJulia Martinez, Charlie Martinez, Bob Miller, David Miller, Hannah Brown, Charlie Davis, Julia Smith, Julia Jones, Fiona Taylor, Alice Miller, Alice Garcia, Ian Jones, Charlie Miller, Fiona Brown, Hannah Jones\\nTranscript\\nJulia Martinez: Alright team, let's get started with our sprint review. First, let's go over the status of our completed PRs. I see we have a few pending tasks that need our attention.\\nBob Miller: Sounds good, Julia. Let's dive into the pending tasks and see where we stand.\\nHannah Brown: Sure, I'll start with the hardware compatibility checks. We have a PR titled 'Add Support for New Sensor Protocols'. Julia Smith, you submitted this PR, but it needs some revisions.\\nJulia Smith: Yes, I noticed some issues with the sensor data processing. Julia Jones, could you take over and submit a new PR?\\nJulia Jones: Got it, I’ll handle this. I'll make sure to address the feedback and submit a new PR soon.\\nJulia Martinez: Great, thanks Julia Jones. Next, we have the task to develop the RESTful API framework. Alice Garcia, you submitted the initial PR, but it needs some additional work.\\nAlice Garcia: Yes, I realized there were some missing configurations. Julia Smith, could you take this on and submit a new PR?\\nJulia Smith: I confirm, I’ll take care of this implementation. I'll ensure the framework is set up correctly.\\nJulia Martinez: Perfect, thank you Julia. Lastly, we have the task to implement JWT authentication for security. Charlie Miller, your PR needs some revisions.\\nCharlie Miller: Yes, I missed a few edge cases in the token validation. Fiona Taylor, could you work on this and submit a new PR?\\nFiona Taylor: I confirm, I’ll take care of this. I'll make sure the JWT implementation is robust and secure.\\nDavid Miller: Thanks everyone for stepping up. Let's make sure we address these revisions promptly so we can keep our momentum going.\\nCharlie Martinez: Absolutely, and if anyone needs help or has questions, feel free to reach out. We're all here to support each other.\\nJulia Martinez: Great teamwork, everyone. Let's aim to have these new PRs submitted by the end of the week. Thanks for your hard work!\", \"date\": \"2026-10-05T06:53:00\", \"document_type\": \"product-planning\", \"participants\": [\"eid_91523bad\", \"eid_b6a30126\", \"eid_caa2e58d\", \"eid_2d8eff4d\", \"eid_a253c65a\", \"eid_4b38019b\", \"eid_2347b567\", \"eid_bac7c6c4\", \"eid_edf6a3fc\", \"eid_4df3bcc2\", \"eid_54905dcb\", \"eid_4555ba9c\", \"eid_3e076e53\", \"eid_5058fefc\", \"eid_a0fe567d\"], \"id\": \"product_dev_EdgeForce_3\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-juliamartinez-EdgeForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-a13a7a\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_54905dcb\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-29T08:18:00\", \"text\": \"Hi team, please check my PR for initializing the RESTful API framework: https://github.com/salesforce/EF_AIX/pull/2. 🚀 I've set up the foundational structure, installed essential libraries, and completed the basic server setup. Let me know your thoughts!\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261002-0-e33b4\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261002-0-e33b4\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-juliamartinez-EdgeForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-a13a7a\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_edf6a3fc\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-29T08:20:00\", \"text\": \"Hey @eid_54905dcb, thanks for sharing! I'll take a look at it now. 😊\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261002-1-e4a4b\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261002-1-e4a4b\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-juliamartinez-EdgeForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-a13a7a\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_4df3bcc2\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-29T08:23:00\", \"text\": \"Thanks for the heads up, @eid_54905dcb! I'll review it shortly. 🕵️‍♀️\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261002-2-6d1fb\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261002-2-6d1fb\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-juliamartinez-EdgeForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-a13a7a\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_edf6a3fc\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-29T08:27:00\", \"text\": \"Alright, I've gone through the PR. The project structure looks solid and the libraries are well-chosen and configured. Nice work on that front! 👍\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261002-3-40530\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261002-3-40530\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-juliamartinez-EdgeForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-a13a7a\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_4df3bcc2\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-29T08:30:00\", \"text\": \"I agree with @Fiona Taylor, the setup is clean and organized. However, I noticed that the server setup doesn't seem to handle HTTP requests yet. Did you mean to include a basic endpoint for testing?\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261002-4-e7e10\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261002-4-e7e10\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-juliamartinez-EdgeForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-a13a7a\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_54905dcb\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-29T08:31:00\", \"text\": \"Ah, good catch, @Alice Miller! I did plan to include a basic endpoint but it seems I missed it. 😅 I'll add a simple GET endpoint for testing purposes.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261002-5-a82d7\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261002-5-a82d7\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-juliamartinez-EdgeForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-a13a7a\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_edf6a3fc\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-29T08:33:00\", \"text\": \"No worries, @eid_54905dcb! Once you add that, it should meet all the acceptance criteria. Let us know when it's ready for another round of review. 🚀\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261002-6-d1de4\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261002-6-d1de4\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-juliamartinez-EdgeForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-a13a7a\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_4df3bcc2\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-29T08:36:00\", \"text\": \"Exactly, just ping us once you've made the updates. Looking forward to seeing the changes! 😊\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261002-7-65104\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261002-7-65104\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-juliamartinez-EdgeForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-a13a7a\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_54905dcb\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-29T08:40:00\", \"text\": \"Will do, thanks for the feedback, @Fiona Taylor and @Alice Miller! I'll make the changes and update the PR soon. 🙌\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261002-8-38464\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261002-8-38464\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-juliamartinez-EdgeForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-a13a7a\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_91523bad\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-29T21:29:00\", \"text\": \"@here here's a short demo highlighting the main features of our last release https://sf-internal.slack.com/archives/EdProX/demo_2\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260909-0-5b942\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260909-0-5b942\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-juliamartinez-EdgeForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-a13a7a\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"slack_admin_bot\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-30T21:54:00\", \"text\": \"@eid_caa2e58d joined develop-juliamartinez-EF_AIX.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260930-25-8e132\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260930-25-8e132\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-juliamartinez-EdgeForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-a13a7a\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_caa2e58d\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-01T01:53:00\", \"text\": \"@here I've been thinking about our product name, and I believe renaming it from EF_AIX to EdgeForce could better reflect its value to customers. What do you think? I'd love to hear your thoughts and feedback!\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260930-0-cb9eb\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260930-0-cb9eb\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-juliamartinez-EdgeForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-a13a7a\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_b6a30126\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-01T01:55:00\", \"text\": \"Absolutely agree! EdgeForce is a much better fit.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260930-1-22b5c\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260930-1-22b5c\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-juliamartinez-EdgeForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-a13a7a\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_91523bad\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-01T02:00:00\", \"text\": \"Love this idea! EdgeForce feels much more aligned with the product’s value and positioning. Great suggestion!\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260930-2-aa53f\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260930-2-aa53f\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-juliamartinez-EdgeForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-a13a7a\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"slack_admin_bot\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-01T02:01:00\", \"text\": \"@eid_caa2e58d renamed the channel to develop-juliamartinez-EdgeForce.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261001-29-108cd\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261001-29-108cd\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-juliamartinez-EdgeForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-a13a7a\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"slack_admin_bot\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-01T04:38:00\", \"text\": \"@eid_3e076e53 joined develop-juliamartinez-EdgeForce.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261001-30-baac0\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261001-30-baac0\"}\n{\"transcript\": \"Attendees\\nJulia Martinez, Charlie Martinez, Bob Miller, David Miller, Hannah Brown, Charlie Davis, Julia Smith, Julia Jones, Fiona Taylor, Alice Miller, Alice Garcia, Ian Jones, Charlie Miller, Fiona Brown, Hannah Jones\\nTranscript\\nJulia Martinez: Alright team, welcome to our first sprint review for the Einstein Edge AI project. Let's dive into the status of our tasks and PRs. Since this is our first meeting, we don't have any completed PRs to discuss, so we'll focus on our pending tasks.\\nBob Miller: Sounds good, Julia. Let's start with the hardware compatibility checks. Julia Smith, you're assigned to this task, right?\\nJulia Smith: Yes, that's correct. I'm working on the PR titled 'Add Support for New Sensor Protocols'. The goal is to update the device layer to recognize and process data from new sensor types.\\nHannah Brown: Julia, do you foresee any challenges with implementing support for these new protocols?\\nJulia Smith: Not at the moment, but I'll keep an eye on any compatibility issues that might arise during testing.\\nJulia Martinez: Great. Let's move on to the RESTful API framework. Alice Garcia, you're handling this one, correct?\\nAlice Garcia: Yes, I'm on it. The PR is titled 'Initialize RESTful API Framework'. I'll be setting up the foundational structure and ensuring we have all the necessary libraries and configurations in place.\\nCharlie Martinez: Alice, do you need any additional resources or support to get started?\\nAlice Garcia: Not at the moment, Charlie. I have everything I need to kick things off. I'll reach out if anything comes up.\\nJulia Martinez: Perfect. Lastly, we have the JWT authentication task. Charlie Miller, you're assigned to this, right?\\nCharlie Miller: Yes, that's me. The PR is 'Implement JWT Token Generation and Validation'. I'll be working on creating a utility module for handling JWT operations.\\nDavid Miller: Charlie, make sure to coordinate with the API team to ensure seamless integration.\\nCharlie Miller: Got it, David. I'll make sure to sync up with Alice and the rest of the API team.\\nJulia Martinez: Alright, team. Let's make sure we keep communication open and address any blockers as they come up. Does anyone have any questions or need further clarification on their tasks?\\nFiona Taylor: No questions from me. Everything seems clear.\\nAlice Miller: Same here. I'm good to go.\\nJulia Martinez: Great. Let's aim to have significant progress by our next meeting. Thanks, everyone!\", \"date\": \"2026-09-25T04:45:00\", \"document_type\": \"product-planning\", \"participants\": [\"eid_91523bad\", \"eid_b6a30126\", \"eid_caa2e58d\", \"eid_2d8eff4d\", \"eid_a253c65a\", \"eid_4b38019b\", \"eid_2347b567\", \"eid_bac7c6c4\", \"eid_edf6a3fc\", \"eid_4df3bcc2\", \"eid_54905dcb\", \"eid_4555ba9c\", \"eid_3e076e53\", \"eid_5058fefc\", \"eid_a0fe567d\"], \"id\": \"product_dev_EF_AIX_2\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-juliamartinez-EdgeForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-a13a7a\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_bac7c6c4\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-08T03:48:00\", \"text\": \"Hi team, please check my PR for adding support for new sensor protocols: https://github.com/salesforce/EF_AIX/pull/4. This update focuses on enhancing device compatibility by updating the device layer to recognize and process data from newly identified sensor types. Let me know your thoughts! 😊\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261007-0-ff0a9\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261007-0-ff0a9\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-juliamartinez-EdgeForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-a13a7a\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_4df3bcc2\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-08T03:49:00\", \"text\": \"Hey @eid_bac7c6c4, thanks for sharing! I'll start reviewing it now. Excited to see how these new protocols are integrated. 🔍\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261007-1-156c7\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261007-1-156c7\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-juliamartinez-EdgeForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-a13a7a\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_4b38019b\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-08T03:51:00\", \"text\": \"Checking it out now, @eid_bac7c6c4. The new sensor protocols sound like a great addition! 👍\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261007-2-f49ed\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261007-2-f49ed\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-juliamartinez-EdgeForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-a13a7a\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_2347b567\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-08T03:52:00\", \"text\": \"On it! Looking forward to seeing how the device layer handles these new protocols. 😊\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261007-3-fc5e6\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261007-3-fc5e6\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-juliamartinez-EdgeForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-a13a7a\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_4df3bcc2\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-08T03:57:00\", \"text\": \"Alright, I've gone through the changes. The device layer seems to recognize and process the new sensor protocols perfectly. Great job on that, @eid_bac7c6c4! 🎉\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261007-4-0b3b9\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261007-4-0b3b9\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-juliamartinez-EdgeForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-a13a7a\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_4b38019b\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-08T03:59:00\", \"text\": \"Just finished reviewing the unit tests. They cover all the new protocols and pass successfully. Everything looks solid from my end. Nice work, @eid_bac7c6c4! 💪\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261007-5-21671\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261007-5-21671\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-juliamartinez-EdgeForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-a13a7a\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_2347b567\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-08T04:00:00\", \"text\": \"Documentation is up-to-date and clearly outlines the new sensor protocols supported. Thanks for keeping it comprehensive, @eid_bac7c6c4! 📚\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261007-6-6cd7e\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261007-