ed support for additional sensor protocols. This update enhances our device compatibility by allowing the device layer to recognize and process data from new sensor types. It’s been tested and is working smoothly.\\nBob Miller: Great work, Charlie. This will definitely broaden our device compatibility. How about the RESTful API framework, Julia?\\nCharlie Davis: Yes, the foundational structure for the RESTful API framework is set up. We’ve included all necessary libraries and configurations to support further API development. It’s ready for the next steps.\\nDavid Miller: Excellent. This sets a solid base for our API work. And the JWT token generation and validation?\\nFiona Brown: That’s completed as well. We now have a utility module for handling JWT operations, including token creation, signing, and verification. It’s integrated and functioning as expected.\\nHannah Brown: Fantastic progress, everyone. Now, let's move on to the pending tasks. First up, the hardware compatibility checks. Julia Smith, this is assigned to you, correct?\\nJulia Smith: Yes, that's right. I'll be developing the module to perform hardware compatibility checks. This will ensure devices meet the necessary requirements for running EF_AIX.\\nJulia Martinez: Great, Julia. Please make sure to check for supported sensor types and necessary hardware specifications.\\nJulia Smith: Got it, I’ll handle this.\\nBob Miller: Next, we have the development of the RESTful API framework. Alice Garcia, you’re on this, right?\\nAlice Garcia: Yes, I am. I’ll be working on implementing the user authentication endpoints, including login and registration functionalities to secure the API.\\nDavid Miller: Perfect. Make sure to coordinate with the team to ensure seamless integration.\\nAlice Garcia: I confirm, I’ll take care of this implementation.\\nHannah Brown: Lastly, we have the JWT authentication integration into the user login flow. Charlie Miller, this is yours, correct?\\nCharlie Miller: Yes, I’ll be integrating JWT authentication into the existing user login flow. This involves modifying the login endpoint to issue a JWT token upon successful authentication and updating the client-side to handle token storage.\\nCharlie Martinez: Sounds good, Charlie. Let us know if you need any support.\\nCharlie Miller: I confirm, I’ll take care of this implementation.\\nJulia Martinez: Alright, team. That wraps up our sprint review. Let’s keep up the great work and stay on track with these tasks. If there are no further questions, let’s get back to it.\\nAlice Miller: No questions from me. Let’s do this!\\nFiona Taylor: All clear here. Looking forward to the next steps.\", \"date\": \"2026-10-17T21:29:00\", \"document_type\": \"product-planning\", \"participants\": [\"eid_91523bad\", \"eid_b6a30126\", \"eid_caa2e58d\", \"eid_2d8eff4d\", \"eid_a253c65a\", \"eid_4b38019b\", \"eid_2347b567\", \"eid_bac7c6c4\", \"eid_edf6a3fc\", \"eid_4df3bcc2\", \"eid_54905dcb\", \"eid_4555ba9c\", \"eid_3e076e53\", \"eid_5058fefc\", \"eid_a0fe567d\"], \"id\": \"product_dev_EdgeForce_4\"}\n{\"transcript\": \"Attendees\\nJulia Martinez, Charlie Martinez, Bob Miller, David Miller, Hannah Brown, Charlie Davis, Julia Smith, Julia Jones, Fiona Taylor, Alice Miller, Alice Garcia, Ian Jones, Charlie Miller, Fiona Brown, Hannah Jones\\nTranscript\\nJulia Martinez: Alright team, let's kick off this sprint review. First, let's go over the completed PRs. Charlie, can you start with the Hardware Compatibility Check Module?\\nCharlie Martinez: Sure, Julia. The Hardware Compatibility Check Module is complete. It ensures that devices meet the necessary requirements for running EF_AIX, including supported sensor types and hardware specifications. Everything's been tested and is working as expected.\\nBob Miller: Great work, Charlie. This is crucial for ensuring our product runs smoothly across different devices.\\nDavid Miller: Absolutely, Bob. And the JWT Authentication integration into the user login flow is also complete. This will enhance our security significantly.\\nCharlie Davis: Yes, David. The JWT integration modifies the login endpoint to issue a JWT token upon successful authentication and updates the client-side to handle token storage. It's all set.\\nHannah Brown: Fantastic. Now, let's move on to the pending tasks. First up, we have the task to conduct hardware compatibility checks for device compatibility. Julia Smith, you're assigned to update the device layer for enhanced protocol handling. Can you confirm?\\nJulia Smith: Got it, Hannah. I'll handle the refactoring to improve protocol handling and ensure seamless integration with more devices.\\nJulia Martinez: Great. Next, we have the development of the RESTful API framework. Alice Garcia, your PR needs additional revisions. Alice Miller, you'll be working on a new PR for this. Can you confirm?\\nAlice Garcia: Yes, Julia. I'll make the necessary revisions to my PR.\\nAlice Miller: I confirm, I'll take care of the new PR for the user authentication endpoints.\\nBob Miller: Thanks, Alice and Alice. This is a key part of securing our API.\\nDavid Miller: Absolutely, and finally, we have the task to implement JWT authentication for security. Charlie Miller, you're assigned to implement middleware for JWT token verification. Can you confirm?\\nCharlie Miller: I confirm, David. I'll ensure that only requests with valid tokens can access protected routes.\\nJulia Jones: Great teamwork, everyone. Let's keep up the momentum and ensure we meet our sprint goals.\\nFiona Taylor: Agreed, Julia. If anyone needs help or has questions, feel free to reach out.\\nFiona Brown: Thanks, Fiona. Let's make this sprint a success!\", \"date\": \"2026-10-27T21:17:00\", \"document_type\": \"product-planning\", \"participants\": [\"eid_91523bad\", \"eid_b6a30126\", \"eid_caa2e58d\", \"eid_2d8eff4d\", \"eid_a253c65a\", \"eid_4b38019b\", \"eid_2347b567\", \"eid_bac7c6c4\", \"eid_edf6a3fc\", \"eid_4df3bcc2\", \"eid_54905dcb\", \"eid_4555ba9c\", \"eid_3e076e53\", \"eid_5058fefc\", \"eid_a0fe567d\"], \"id\": \"product_dev_EdgeForce_5\"}\n{\"title\": \"Add Support for New Sensor Protocols\", \"summary\": \"Implement support for additional sensor protocols to enhance device compatibility. This PR focuses on updating the device layer to recognize and process data from newly identified sensor types.\", \"link\": \"https://github.com/salesforce/EF_AIX/pull/4\", \"mergeable\": \"True\", \"merged\": \"True\", \"number\": \"4\", \"state\": \"closed\", \"user\": {\"login\": \"eid_bac7c6c4\"}, \"created_at\": \"2026-10-07T15:14:00\", \"reviews\": [{\"state\": \"APPROVED\", \"user\": {\"login\": \"eid_4df3bcc2\"}, \"comment\": \"The device layer recognizes and processes the new sensor protocols perfectly. Great job! LGTM, approved! 🚀\", \"submitted_at\": \"2026-10-08T04:03:00\"}, {\"state\": \"PENDING\", \"user\": {\"login\": \"eid_4b38019b\"}, \"comment\": \"Unit tests cover all new protocols and pass successfully. Everything looks solid. Looks good to me too, approved! 👍\", \"submitted_at\": \"2026-10-08T04:06:00\"}, {\"state\": \"COMMENTED\", \"user\": {\"login\": \"eid_2347b567\"}, \"comment\": \"Documentation is up-to-date and clearly outlines the new sensor protocols supported. All criteria met, approved! Great work, team! 🎉\", \"submitted_at\": \"2026-10-08T04:10:00\"}], \"id\": \"github_com_salesforce_EF_AIX_pull_4\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"planning-EF_AIX\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-30c6d3\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_caa2e58d\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-12T00:27:00\", \"text\": \"Hi team, let's review the Product Requirements Document and update it based on the latest issues reported. We need to address the setup complexity, performance inconsistencies, limited integration options, UI challenges, and update disruptions. Let's dive in! 🚀\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260911-0-d0bf6\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260911-0-d0bf6\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"planning-EF_AIX\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-30c6d3\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_b6a30126\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-12T00:31:00\", \"text\": \"Hey @eid_caa2e58d, for the setup complexity, I suggest we add a section on developing comprehensive setup automation tools. We could include scripts that simplify the initial configuration process. This should help reduce the technical expertise required. Thoughts? 🤔\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260911-1-c0b5e\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260911-1-c0b5e\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"planning-EF_AIX\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-30c6d3\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_1a7d9807\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-12T00:34:00\", \"text\": \"I agree with Charlie. Also, we should enhance the user guidance documentation. Maybe include a step-by-step setup guide with visuals? This could be part of the 'User Experience' section. 📚\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260911-2-e00c0\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260911-2-e00c0\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"planning-EF_AIX\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-30c6d3\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_c9c3d8d5\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-12T00:37:00\", \"text\": \"For the performance issue, we might need to revisit the 'Edge Processing Layer' section. Let's consider optimizing our data processing algorithms and resource management strategies. We should also mention testing on varied hardware to ensure consistent performance. 💻\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260911-3-42f67\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260911-3-42f67\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"planning-EF_AIX\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-30c6d3\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_91523bad\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-12T00:38:00\", \"text\": \"@eid_c9c3d8d5, good point. We should also explore architectural improvements for handling large datasets more efficiently. Maybe add a subsection under 'System Architecture' to address this? 📈\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260911-4-51d40\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260911-4-51d40\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"planning-EF_AIX\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-30c6d3\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_a9002ae2\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-12T00:42:00\", \"text\": \"Regarding integration options, we need to expand on the 'Integration Layer' section. Let's propose developing more APIs and connectors for third-party applications. This will enhance flexibility and compatibility. 🔗\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260911-5-e43ac\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260911-5-e43ac\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"planning-EF_AIX\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-30c6d3\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_9db3abf4\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-12T00:47:00\", \"text\": \"Absolutely, Bob. We should also consider a more open ecosystem approach. This could be a strategic shift mentioned in the 'Development Roadmap' section. 🌐\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260911-6-75d39\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260911-6-75d39\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"planning-EF_AIX\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-30c6d3\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_edf6a3fc\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-12T00:48:55\", \"text\": \"@here Explore TensorFlow Lite, a powerful library for deploying machine learning models on edge devices. Perfect for enhancing EF_AIX capabilities! https://www.tensorflow.org/lite\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260912-114-86809\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260912-114-86809\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"planning-EF_AIX\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-30c6d3\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_e51b439b\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-12T00:49:00\", \"text\": \"For the UI, let's add a focus on user-friendly design in the 'User Experience' section. We should incorporate more user feedback and possibly introduce customization options to cater to non-technical users. 🖥️\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260911-7-f0368\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260911-7-f0368\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"planning-EF_AIX\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-30c6d3\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_caa2e58d\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-12T00:54:00\", \"text\": \"Great suggestions, everyone! To summarize: we'll add automation tools and detailed guides for setup, optimize data processing and architecture for performance, expand integration options, enhance UI design, and improve update management. Let's draft these changes and reconvene next week to finalize. Thanks for the input! 👍\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260911-8-81ffa\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260911-8-81ffa\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"planning-EF_AIX\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-30c6d3\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_caa2e58d\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-14T03:03:00\", \"text\": \"Here is the updated <https://sf-internal.slack.com/archives/docs/new_ef_aix_product_requirements_document|Product Requirements Document>, thank you everyone!\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260914-0-66d4d\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260914-0-66d4d\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"planning-EF_AIX\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-30c6d3\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_a13234f2\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-14T08:54:16\", \"text\": \"@here This blog post explores the challenges and solutions in deploying AI models on edge devices, a must-read for EF_AIX enthusiasts! https://www.edge-ai-blog.com/challenges-and-solutions-in-edge-ai-deployment\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260914-114-106e5\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260914-114-106e5\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"planning-EF_AIX\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-30c6d3\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_a253c65a\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-15T14:34:00\", \"text\": \"Hi team, let's review the Technical Specifications Document and update it based on the latest issues reported. We've got a few areas to focus on, especially around setup complexity, performance inconsistencies, integration limitations, UI usability, and update disruptions. Let's dive in! 😊\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260915-0-dda1f\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260915-0-dda1f\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"planning-EF_AIX\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-30c6d3\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_91523bad\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-15T14:39:00\", \"text\": \"Hey @eid_a253c65a, for the setup complexity, I think we should add a section on setup automation tools. Maybe we can include scripts or a step-by-step guide to simplify the process. Thoughts? 🤔\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260915-1-14fd9\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260915-1-14fd9\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"planning-EF_AIX\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-30c6d3\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_b6a30126\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-15T14:40:00\", \"text\": \"I agree with Julia. We could also enhance the user guidance section with more detailed documentation. Perhaps a quick-start guide for non-technical users? 📚\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260915-2-5b178\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260915-2-5b178\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"planning-EF_AIX\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-30c6d3\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_c9c3d8d5\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-15T14:43:00\", \"text\": \"For the performance inconsistencies, should we look into optimizing the data processing algorithms? The document could include a section on performance tuning tips for large datasets. @eid_91523bad, what do you think?\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260915-3-b3572\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260915-3-b3572\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"planning-EF_AIX\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-30c6d3\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_91523bad\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-15T14:47:00\", \"text\": \"Absolutely, @eid_c9c3d8d5. We should also consider adding a note on recommended hardware specs to ensure consistent performance across devices. 💡\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260915-4-9b42e\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260915-4-9b42e\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"planning-EF_AIX\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-30c6d3\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_a9002ae2\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-15T14:48:00\", \"text\": \"Regarding integration options, we might want to expand the integration layer section to include potential APIs or connectors. This could help with third-party app compatibility. 🤝\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260915-5-b633c\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260915-5-b633c\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"planning-EF_AIX\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-30c6d3\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_1a7d9807\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-15T14:51:00\", \"text\": \"Good point, Bob. We should also address the closed ecosystem approach in the design section. Maybe suggest a more open architecture to enhance flexibility? 🔄\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260915-6-0851a\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260915-6-0851a\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"planning-EF_AIX\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-30c6d3\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_9db3abf4\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-15T14:56:00\", \"text\": \"For the UI, let's add a subsection on user feedback incorporation. We need to make sure the design is intuitive for non-technical users. Perhaps more user-friendly features or customization options? 🖥️\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260915-7-0eb18\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260915-7-0eb18\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"planning-EF_AIX\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-30c6d3\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_caa2e58d\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-15T14:57:00\", \"text\": \"And for update disruptions, we should include a section on update management and rollback procedures. Ensuring backward compatibility is crucial for reliability. 🔄\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260915-8-d26b9\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260915-8-d26b9\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"planning-EF_AIX\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-30c6d3\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_2d8eff4d\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-15T14:58:00\", \"text\": \"Agreed, @eid_caa2e58d. We could also emphasize the importance of thorough testing before deployment in the technical section. 🧪\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260915-9-ec3b0\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260915-9-ec3b0\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"planning-EF_AIX\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-30c6d3\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_a253c65a\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-15T15:03:00\", \"text\": \"Great suggestions, everyone! Here's a quick summary: \\n1. Add setup automation tools and detailed user guidance. \\n2. Optimize data processing algorithms and specify hardware recommendations. \\n3. Expand integration options with APIs/connectors. \\n4. Enhance UI with user feedback and customization options. \\n5. Improve update management and ensure backward compatibility. \\nLet's start drafting these changes and reconvene next week to finalize. Thanks for the input! 🚀\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260915-10-05054\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260915-10-05054\"}\n{\"title\": \"Write API Documentation\", \"summary\": \"Create detailed documentation for the RESTful API, including usage instructions and endpoint details for third-party developers.\", \"link\": \"https://github.com/salesforce/EF_AIX/pull/23\", \"mergeable\": \"True\", \"merged\": \"True\", \"number\": \"23\", \"state\": \"closed\", \"user\": {\"login\": \"eid_54905dcb\"}, \"created_at\": \"2026-12-09T07:08:00\", \"reviews\": [{\"state\": \"APPROVED\", \"user\": {\"login\": \"eid_2347b567\"}, \"comment\": \"The documentation is comprehensive and well-organized. The endpoint descriptions and example usage are clear and easy to follow. Nice work! 👍\", \"submitted_at\": \"2026-12-09T21:17:00\"}, {\"state\": \"COMMENTED\", \"user\": {\"login\": \"eid_4df3bcc2\"}, \"comment\": \"The request/response formats are clearly outlined, and the examples are super helpful. Everything looks complete to me. Great job! 👏\", \"submitted_at\": \"2026-12-09T21:21:00\"}], \"id\": \"github_com_salesforce_EF_AIX_pull_23\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-juliamartinez-EdgeForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-7bfbef\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_91523bad\", \"timestamp\": \"2027-01-18T20:23:00\", \"text\": \"Hi team, several customers are reporting issues with EdgeForce that need our attention. Let's go through them one by one. 🚀\", \"utterranceID\": \"20270118-0-db28c\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20270118-0-db28c\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-juliamartinez-EdgeForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-7bfbef\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_91523bad\", \"timestamp\": \"2027-01-18T20:25:00\", \"text\": \"First up, we have an issue titled 'Inconsistent Model Visualization Updates'. The problem is that model visualizations aren't updating consistently when new data is processed. This affects the User Interface & Visualization Module and is causing frustration for users like CUST-0041. @eid_4df3bcc2, can you take this one?\", \"utterranceID\": \"20270118-1-3c041\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20270118-1-3c041\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-juliamartinez-EdgeForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-7bfbef\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_4df3bcc2\", \"timestamp\": \"2027-01-18T20:29:00\", \"text\": \"Got it! I'll look into the visualization updates and see what's causing the discrepancies. Thanks for the heads-up! 👍\", \"utterranceID\": \"20270118-2-16cd9\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20270118-2-16cd9\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-juliamartinez-EdgeForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-7bfbef\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_91523bad\", \"timestamp\": \"2027-01-18T20:34:00\", \"text\": \"Great, thanks! Next, we have a 'Faulty Edge Device Firmware Update' issue. The recent update is disrupting the AI Processing Engine's ability to handle concurrent tasks efficiently, impacting real-time data processing for customers like CUST-0012. @eid_bac7c6c4, can you handle this?\", \"utterranceID\": \"20270118-3-1913b\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20270118-3-1913b\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-juliamartinez-EdgeForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-7bfbef\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_bac7c6c4\", \"timestamp\": \"2027-01-18T20:35:00\", \"text\": \"Sure thing! I'll dive into the firmware update and see what's causing the disruption. Real-time processing is crucial, so I'll prioritize this. 🔍\", \"utterranceID\": \"20270118-4-3ca5e\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20270118-4-3ca5e\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-juliamartinez-EdgeForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-7bfbef\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_91523bad\", \"timestamp\": \"2027-01-18T20:38:00\", \"text\": \"Thanks, @eid_bac7c6c4! Lastly, there's an 'Unresponsive UI During Data Synchronization' issue. The UI becomes unresponsive during data sync, affecting the User Interface & Visualization Module and causing workflow interruptions for users like CUST-0021. @eid_2347b567, can you take a look?\", \"utterranceID\": \"20270118-5-c8155\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20270118-5-c8155\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-juliamartinez-EdgeForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-7bfbef\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_2347b567\", \"timestamp\": \"2027-01-18T20:39:00\", \"text\": \"On it! I'll investigate why the UI is freezing during data sync and work on a fix. Thanks for assigning this to me! 😊\", \"utterranceID\": \"20270118-6-09288\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20270118-6-09288\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-juliamartinez-EdgeForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-7bfbef\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_91523bad\", \"timestamp\": \"2027-01-18T20:40:00\", \"text\": \"Awesome, thanks everyone for jumping on these issues so quickly! Let's keep the impacted customers in the loop with updates as we make progress. Feel free to reach out if you need any more info or help. 🙌\", \"utterranceID\": \"20270118-7-33441\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20270118-7-33441\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-juliamartinez-EdgeForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-7bfbef\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_4df3bcc2\", \"timestamp\": \"2027-01-18T20:44:00\", \"text\": \"Will do! I'll keep you posted on the visualization updates. 🖼️\", \"utterranceID\": \"20270118-8-54757\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20270118-8-54757\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-juliamartinez-EdgeForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-7bfbef\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_bac7c6c4\", \"timestamp\": \"2027-01-18T20:49:00\", \"text\": \"Same here, I'll update once I have more info on the firmware issue. 🔧\", \"utterranceID\": \"20270118-9-7f29a\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20270118-9-7f29a\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-juliamartinez-EdgeForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-7bfbef\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_2347b567\", \"timestamp\": \"2027-01-18T20:54:00\", \"text\": \"I'll make sure to share any findings on the UI responsiveness. Thanks, team! 💪\", \"utterranceID\": \"20270118-10-821d5\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20270118-10-821d5\"}\n{\"title\": \"Create Data Retrieval Endpoints\", \"summary\": \"Develop endpoints to retrieve data from the local environment, enabling real-time insights through the API.\", \"link\": \"https://github.com/salesforce/EF_AIX/pull/15\", \"mergeable\": \"True\", \"merged\": \"True\", \"number\": \"15\", \"state\": \"closed\", \"user\": {\"login\": \"eid_54905dcb\"}, \"created_at\": \"2026-11-12T03:27:00\", \"reviews\": [{\"state\": \"APPROVED\", \"user\": {\"login\": \"eid_4df3bcc2\"}, \"comment\": \"The endpoints are well-documented and include examples in the API docs. Performance-wise, they are responsive and reliable. LGTM, approved! Great work on this, @eid_54905dcb. This will definitely enhance our API capabilities.\", \"submitted_at\": \"2026-11-12T17:13:00\"}, {\"state\": \"PENDING\", \"user\": {\"login\": \"eid_2347b567\"}, \"comment\": \"The documentation is clear and concise. I ran tests, and the data is fetched correctly from the local environment. No performance issues encountered. Approved from me too! Everything meets the acceptance criteria. Well done, @eid_54905dcb!\", \"submitted_at\": \"2026-11-12T17:14:00\"}], \"id\": \"github_com_salesforce_EF_AIX_pull_15\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-juliamartinez-EdgeForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-a13a7a\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_54905dcb\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-12-04T10:26:00\", \"text\": \"Hi team, please check my PR for adding error handling and logging: https://github.com/salesforce/EF_AIX/pull/21. I've integrated comprehensive error handling across all endpoints and set up logging to capture API requests and errors. Let me know your thoughts! 😊\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261204-0-37b42\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261204-0-37b42\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-juliamartinez-EdgeForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-a13a7a\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_2347b567\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-12-04T10:31:00\", \"text\": \"@eid_54905dcb Thanks for sharing! I'll start reviewing it now. 🕵️‍♀️\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261204-1-37419\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261204-1-37419\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-juliamartinez-EdgeForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-a13a7a\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_4b38019b\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-12-04T10:35:00\", \"text\": \"Hey @eid_54905dcb, I'll take a look as well. Error handling and logging are crucial, so I'm excited to see what you've implemented! 🔍\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261204-2-ca8cc\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261204-2-ca8cc\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-juliamartinez-EdgeForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-a13a7a\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_2347b567\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-12-04T10:39:00\", \"text\": \"Just went through the PR, and it looks solid! Error handling is well-implemented for all endpoints, and the logging setup is capturing everything we need. Great job! 👍\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261204-3-f4b17\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261204-3-f4b17\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-juliamartinez-EdgeForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-a13a7a\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_4b38019b\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-12-04T10:41:00\", \"text\": \"I agree with Julia. The error handling is comprehensive, and the logging is detailed enough for traceability. I also ran some tests, and errors are logged and handled gracefully. Well done, @eid_54905dcb! 👏\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261204-4-0874c\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261204-4-0874c\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-juliamartinez-EdgeForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-a13a7a\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_2347b567\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-12-04T10:44:00\", \"text\": \"LGTM, approved! 🚀\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261204-5-2391a\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261204-5-2391a\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-juliamartinez-EdgeForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-a13a7a\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_4b38019b\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-12-04T10:49:00\", \"text\": \"Same here, LGTM! Approved! 🎉\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261204-6-4db3a\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261204-6-4db3a\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-juliamartinez-EdgeForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-a13a7a\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_54905dcb\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-12-04T10:51:00\", \"text\": \"Thanks, @Julia Smith and @Charlie Davis! Appreciate the quick review and feedback. I'll merge it now. 😊\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261204-7-6775e\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261204-7-6775e\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-juliamartinez-EdgeForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-a13a7a\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_a9002ae2\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-12-04T17:09:00\", \"text\": \"Hi team, I wanted to discuss PR# 21. It was approved and merged, but I've heard that the product direction has changed, making this PR unnecessary. Can we talk about whether we should revert it?\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261204-0-3e65e\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261204-0-3e65e\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-juliamartinez-EdgeForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-a13a7a\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_2347b567\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-12-04T17:10:00\", \"text\": \"Hey @eid_a9002ae2, thanks for bringing this up. Can someone clarify what the new product direction is and why this PR might not be needed anymore?\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261204-1-1b686\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261204-1-1b686\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-juliamartinez-EdgeForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-a13a7a\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_1a7d9807\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-12-04T17:12:00\", \"text\": \"From what I understand, the focus has shifted towards a different API architecture that inherently includes error handling and logging. So, this PR might be redundant.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261204-2-7644b\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261204-2-7644b\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-juliamartinez-EdgeForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-a13a7a\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_4b38019b\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-12-04T17:16:00\", \"text\": \"That makes sense. But before we decide, @eid_54905dcb, could you provide some insight into the changes you made in the PR? Are there any parts that might still be useful?\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261204-3-974b7\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261204-3-974b7\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-juliamartinez-EdgeForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-a13a7a\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_54905dcb\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-12-04T17:21:00\", \"text\": \"Sure, the PR added comprehensive error handling and logging. It was meant to improve robustness and traceability. If the new architecture already covers these aspects, then reverting might be the right call.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261204-4-14671\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261204-4-14671\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-juliamartinez-EdgeForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-a13a7a\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_c9c3d8d5\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-12-04T17:26:00\", \"text\": \"Thanks for the explanation, @eid_54905dcb. Given the new direction, I agree that we should consider reverting it. Does anyone see any reason to keep it?\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261204-5-b9447\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261204-5-b9447\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-juliamartinez-EdgeForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-a13a7a\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_9db3abf4\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-12-04T17:29:00\", \"text\": \"I don't see any reason to keep it if the new architecture covers these features. Reverting seems like the best option to avoid unnecessary complexity.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261204-6-138a0\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261204-6-138a0\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-juliamartinez-EdgeForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-a13a7a\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_a9002ae2\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-12-04T17:31:00\", \"text\": \"Alright, it sounds like we're all in agreement. @eid_54905dcb, could you please handle reverting the PR?\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261204-7-d70b2\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261204-7-d70b2\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-juliamartinez-EdgeForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-a13a7a\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_54905dcb\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-12-04T17:34:00\", \"text\": \"Got it, I'll take care of reverting the PR soon. Thanks for the input, everyone.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261204-8-c0ce0\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261204-8-c0ce0\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-juliamartinez-EdgeForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-a13a7a\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_54905dcb\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-12T16:55:00\", \"text\": \"Hi team, please check my PR for the new data retrieval endpoints: https://github.com/salesforce/EF_AIX/pull/15. I've implemented endpoints to fetch data from the local environment, which should help with real-time insights through the API. Let me know your thoughts! 😊\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261114-0-0c120\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261114-0-0c120\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-juliamartinez-EdgeForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-a13a7a\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_4df3bcc2\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-12T16:58:00\", \"text\": \"Hey @eid_54905dcb, thanks for sharing! I'll take a look at it now. Excited to see how these endpoints are shaping up! 🚀\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261114-1-a74fc\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261114-1-a74fc\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-juliamartinez-EdgeForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-a13a7a\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_2347b567\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-12T17:00:00\", \"text\": \"Hi @eid_54905dcb, I'll review it too. Looking forward to seeing how you've tackled the data retrieval. 👍\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261114-2-5081c\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261114-2-5081c\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-juliamartinez-EdgeForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-a13a7a\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_4df3bcc2\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-12T17:02:00\", \"text\": \"Alright, I've gone through the PR. The endpoints are well-documented, and I see you've included examples in the API docs. Great job on that! 📚\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261114-3-96b89\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261114-3-96b89\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-juliamartinez-EdgeForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-a13a7a\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_2347b567\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-12T17:06:00\", \"text\": \"I agree with Alice. The documentation is clear and concise. I also ran some tests, and the data is being fetched correctly from the local environment. Everything seems to be working smoothly. 🛠️\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261114-4-29a56\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261114-4-29a56\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-juliamartinez-EdgeForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-a13a7a\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_4df3bcc2\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-12T17:08:00\", \"text\": \"Performance-wise, the endpoints are responsive, and I didn't encounter any reliability issues during my testing. Looks solid to me! 💪\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261114-5-189be\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261114-5-189be\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-juliamartinez-EdgeForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-a13a7a\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_2347b567\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-12T17:10:00\", \"text\": \"Same here, no performance hiccups on my end either. The endpoints are reliable and quick. Nice work, @eid_54905dcb! 🎉\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261114-6-ebd18\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261114-6-ebd18\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-juliamartinez-EdgeForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-a13a7a\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_4df3bcc2\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-12T17:13:00\", \"text\": \"LGTM, approved! Great work on this, @eid_54905dcb. This will definitely enhance our API capabilities. 😊\", \"utterran",
    "statements": [
        "EdgeForce received a RESTful API framework built through multiple sprints.",
        "The RESTful API framework includes an initial foundational structure.",
        "The initial foundational structure involved setting up a basic server.",
        "The initial foundational structure involved installing essential libraries.",
        "The initial foundational structure involved configuring the project structure to handle HTTP requests.",
        "Alice Garcia initialized the foundational structure.",
        "A later revision added a basic GET endpoint for testing to the foundational structure.",
        "The RESTful API framework includes data retrieval endpoints.",
        "Data retrieval endpoints fetch data from the local environment.",
        "Data retrieval endpoints enable real-time insights via the API.",
        "The RESTful API framework includes data processing endpoints.",
        "Data processing endpoints enable AI processing directly on the device.",
        "Data processing endpoints enable real-time data analysis.",
        "The RESTful API framework includes user authentication endpoints.",
        "User authentication endpoints provide login functionality.",
        "User authentication endpoints provide registration functionality.",
        "User authentication endpoints secure the API.",
        "The RESTful API framework includes JWT authentication integration.",
        "JWT authentication integration includes a JWT token generation/validation utility module.",
        "JWT authentication integration includes middleware for JWT token verification.",
        "JWT authentication integration involves integration into the login flow.",
        "JWT tokens are issued on successful login.",
        "Access control policies were updated to check permissions based on JWT claims.",
        "The RESTful API framework includes error handling and logging.",
