ed support for additional sensor protocols. This update enhances our device compatibility by allowing the device layer to recognize and process data from new sensor types. It’s been tested and is working smoothly.\\nBob Miller: Great work, Charlie. This will definitely broaden our device compatibility. How about the RESTful API framework, Julia?\\nCharlie Davis: Yes, the foundational structure for the RESTful API framework is set up. We’ve included all necessary libraries and configurations to support further API development. It’s ready for the next steps.\\nDavid Miller: Excellent. This sets a solid base for our API work. And the JWT token generation and validation?\\nFiona Brown: That’s completed as well. We now have a utility module for handling JWT operations, including token creation, signing, and verification. It’s integrated and functioning as expected.\\nHannah Brown: Fantastic progress, everyone. Now, let's move on to the pending tasks. First up, the hardware compatibility checks. Julia Smith, this is assigned to you, correct?\\nJulia Smith: Yes, that's right. I'll be developing the module to perform hardware compatibility checks. This will ensure devices meet the necessary requirements for running EF_AIX.\\nJulia Martinez: Great, Julia. Please make sure to check for supported sensor types and necessary hardware specifications.\\nJulia Smith: Got it, I’ll handle this.\\nBob Miller: Next, we have the development of the RESTful API framework. Alice Garcia, you’re on this, right?\\nAlice Garcia: Yes, I am. I’ll be working on implementing the user authentication endpoints, including login and registration functionalities to secure the API.\\nDavid Miller: Perfect. Make sure to coordinate with the team to ensure seamless integration.\\nAlice Garcia: I confirm, I’ll take care of this implementation.\\nHannah Brown: Lastly, we have the JWT authentication integration into the user login flow. Charlie Miller, this is yours, correct?\\nCharlie Miller: Yes, I’ll be integrating JWT authentication into the existing user login flow. This involves modifying the login endpoint to issue a JWT token upon successful authentication and updating the client-side to handle token storage.\\nCharlie Martinez: Sounds good, Charlie. Let us know if you need any support.\\nCharlie Miller: I confirm, I’ll take care of this implementation.\\nJulia Martinez: Alright, team. That wraps up our sprint review. Let’s keep up the great work and stay on track with these tasks. If there are no further questions, let’s get back to it.\\nAlice Miller: No questions from me. Let’s do this!\\nFiona Taylor: All clear here. Looking forward to the next steps.\", \"date\": \"2026-10-17T21:29:00\", \"document_type\": \"product-planning\", \"participants\": [\"eid_91523bad\", \"eid_b6a30126\", \"eid_caa2e58d\", \"eid_2d8eff4d\", \"eid_a253c65a\", \"eid_4b38019b\", \"eid_2347b567\", \"eid_bac7c6c4\", \"eid_edf6a3fc\", \"eid_4df3bcc2\", \"eid_54905dcb\", \"eid_4555ba9c\", \"eid_3e076e53\", \"eid_5058fefc\", \"eid_a0fe567d\"], \"id\": \"product_dev_EdgeForce_4\"}\n{\"transcript\": \"Attendees\\nJulia Martinez, Charlie Martinez, Bob Miller, David Miller, Hannah Brown, Charlie Davis, Julia Smith, Julia Jones, Fiona Taylor, Alice Miller, Alice Garcia, Ian Jones, Charlie Miller, Fiona Brown, Hannah Jones\\nTranscript\\nJulia Martinez: Alright team, let's kick off this sprint review. First, let's go over the completed PRs. Charlie, can you start with the Hardware Compatibility Check Module?\\nCharlie Martinez: Sure, Julia. The Hardware Compatibility Check Module is complete. It ensures that devices meet the necessary requirements for running EF_AIX, including supported sensor types and hardware specifications. Everything's been tested and is working as expected.\\nBob Miller: Great work, Charlie. This is crucial for ensuring our product runs smoothly across different devices.\\nDavid Miller: Absolutely, Bob. And the JWT Authentication integration into the user login flow is also complete. This will enhance our security significantly.\\nCharlie Davis: Yes, David. The JWT integration modifies the login endpoint to issue a JWT token upon successful authentication and updates the client-side to handle token storage. It's all set.\\nHannah Brown: Fantastic. Now, let's move on to the pending tasks. First up, we have the task to conduct hardware compatibility checks for device compatibility. Julia Smith, you're assigned to update the device layer for enhanced protocol handling. Can you confirm?\\nJulia Smith: Got it, Hannah. I'll handle the refactoring to improve protocol handling and ensure seamless integration with more devices.\\nJulia Martinez: Great. Next, we have the development of the RESTful API framework. Alice Garcia, your PR needs additional revisions. Alice Miller, you'll be working on a new PR for this. Can you confirm?\\nAlice Garcia: Yes, Julia. I'll make the necessary revisions to my PR.\\nAlice Miller: I confirm, I'll take care of the new PR for the user authentication endpoints.\\nBob Miller: Thanks, Alice and Alice. This is a key part of securing our API.\\nDavid Miller: Absolutely, and finally, we have the task to implement JWT authentication for security. Charlie Miller, you're assigned to implement middleware for JWT token verification. Can you confirm?\\nCharlie Miller: I confirm, David. I'll ensure that only requests with valid tokens can access protected routes.\\nJulia Jones: Great teamwork, everyone. Let's keep up the momentum and ensure we meet our sprint goals.\\nFiona Taylor: Agreed, Julia. If anyone needs help or has questions, feel free to reach out.\\nFiona Brown: Thanks, Fiona. Let's make this sprint a success!\", \"date\": \"2026-10-27T21:17:00\", \"document_type\": \"product-planning\", \"participants\": [\"eid_91523bad\", \"eid_b6a30126\", \"eid_caa2e58d\", \"eid_2d8eff4d\", \"eid_a253c65a\", \"eid_4b38019b\", \"eid_2347b567\", \"eid_bac7c6c4\", \"eid_edf6a3fc\", \"eid_4df3bcc2\", \"eid_54905dcb\", \"eid_4555ba9c\", \"eid_3e076e53\", \"eid_5058fefc\", \"eid_a0fe567d\"], \"id\": \"product_dev_EdgeForce_5\"}\n{\"title\": \"Add Support for New Sensor Protocols\", \"summary\": \"Implement support for additional sensor protocols to enhance device compatibility. This PR focuses on updating the device layer to recognize and process data from newly identified sensor types.\", \"link\": \"https://github.com/salesforce/EF_AIX/pull/4\", \"mergeable\": \"True\", \"merged\": \"True\", \"number\": \"4\", \"state\": \"closed\", \"user\": {\"login\": \"eid_bac7c6c4\"}, \"created_at\": \"2026-10-07T15:14:00\", \"reviews\": [{\"state\": \"APPROVED\", \"user\": {\"login\": \"eid_4df3bcc2\"}, \"comment\": \"The device layer recognizes and processes the new sensor protocols perfectly. Great job! LGTM, approved! 🚀\", \"submitted_at\": \"2026-10-08T04:03:00\"}, {\"state\": \"PENDING\", \"user\": {\"login\": \"eid_4b38019b\"}, \"comment\": \"Unit tests cover all new protocols and pass successfully. Everything looks solid. Looks good to me too, approved! 👍\", \"submitted_at\": \"2026-10-08T04:06:00\"}, {\"state\": \"COMMENTED\", \"user\": {\"login\": \"eid_2347b567\"}, \"comment\": \"Documentation is up-to-date and clearly outlines the new sensor protocols supported. All criteria met, approved! Great work, team! 🎉\", \"submitted_at\": \"2026-10-08T04:10:00\"}], \"id\": \"github_com_salesforce_EF_AIX_pull_4\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"planning-EF_AIX\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-30c6d3\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_caa2e58d\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-12T00:27:00\", \"text\": \"Hi team, let's review the Product Requirements Document and update it based on the latest issues reported. We need to address the setup complexity, performance inconsistencies, limited integration options, UI challenges, and update disruptions. Let's dive in! 🚀\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260911-0-d0bf6\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260911-0-d0bf6\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"planning-EF_AIX\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-30c6d3\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_b6a30126\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-12T00:31:00\", \"text\": \"Hey @eid_caa2e58d, for the setup complexity, I suggest we add a section on developing comprehensive setup automation tools. We could include scripts that simplify the initial configuration process. This should help reduce the technical expertise required. Thoughts? 🤔\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260911-1-c0b5e\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260911-1-c0b5e\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"planning-EF_AIX\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-30c6d3\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_1a7d9807\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-12T00:34:00\", \"text\": \"I agree with Charlie. Also, we should enhance the user guidance documentation. Maybe include a step-by-step setup guide with visuals? This could be part of the 'User Experience' section. 📚\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260911-2-e00c0\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260911-2-e00c0\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"planning-EF_AIX\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-30c6d3\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_c9c3d8d5\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-12T00:37:00\", \"text\": \"For the performance issue, we might need to revisit the 'Edge Processing Layer' section. Let's consider optimizing our data processing algorithms and resource management strategies. We should also mention testing on varied hardware to ensure consistent performance. 💻\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260911-3-42f67\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260911-3-42f67\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"planning-EF_AIX\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-30c6d3\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_91523bad\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-12T00:38:00\", \"text\": \"@eid_c9c3d8d5, good point. We should also explore architectural improvements for handling large datasets more efficiently. Maybe add a subsection under 'System Architecture' to address this? 📈\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260911-4-51d40\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260911-4-51d40\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"planning-EF_AIX\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-30c6d3\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_a9002ae2\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-12T00:42:00\", \"text\": \"Regarding integration options, we need to expand on the 'Integration Layer' section. Let's propose developing more APIs and connectors for third-party applications. This will enhance flexibility and compatibility. 🔗\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260911-5-e43ac\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260911-5-e43ac\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"planning-EF_AIX\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-30c6d3\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_9db3abf4\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-12T00:47:00\", \"text\": \"Absolutely, Bob. We should also consider a more open ecosystem approach. This could be a strategic shift mentioned in the 'Development Roadmap' section. 🌐\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260911-6-75d39\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260911-6-75d39\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"planning-EF_AIX\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-30c6d3\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_edf6a3fc\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-12T00:48:55\", \"text\": \"@here Explore TensorFlow Lite, a powerful library for deploying machine learning models on edge devices. Perfect for enhancing EF_AIX capabilities! https://www.tensorflow.org/lite\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260912-114-86809\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260912-114-86809\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"planning-EF_AIX\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-30c6d3\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_e51b439b\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-12T00:49:00\", \"text\": \"For the UI, let's add a focus on user-friendly design in the 'User Experience' section. We should incorporate more user feedback and possibly introduce customization options to cater to non-technical users. 🖥️\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260911-7-f0368\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260911-7-f0368\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"planning-EF_AIX\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-30c6d3\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_caa2e58d\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-12T00:54:00\", \"text\": \"Great suggestions, everyone! To summarize: we'll add automation tools and detailed guides for setup, optimize data processing and architecture for performance, expand integration options, enhance UI design, and improve update management. Let's draft these changes and reconvene next week to finalize. Thanks for the input! 👍\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260911-8-81ffa\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260911-8-81ffa\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"planning-EF_AIX\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-30c6d3\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_caa2e58d\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-14T03:03:00\", \"text\": \"Here is the updated <https://sf-internal.slack.com/archives/docs/new_ef_aix_product_requirements_document|Product Requirements Document>, thank you everyone!\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260914-0-66d4d\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260914-0-66d4d\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"planning-EF_AIX\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-30c6d3\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_a13234f2\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-14T08:54:16\", \"text\": \"@here This blog post explores the challenges and solutions in deploying AI models on edge devices, a must-read for EF_AIX enthusiasts! https://www.edge-ai-blog.com/challenges-and-solutions-in-edge-ai-deployment\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260914-114-106e5\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260914-114-106e5\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"planning-EF_AIX\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-30c6d3\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_a253c65a\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-15T14:34:00\", \"text\": \"Hi team, let's review the Technical Specifications Document and update it based on the latest issues reported. We've got a few areas to focus on, especially around setup complexity, performance inconsistencies, integration limitations, UI usability, and update disruptions. Let's dive in! 😊\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260915-0-dda1f\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260915-0-dda1f\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"planning-EF_AIX\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-30c6d3\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_91523bad\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-15T14:39:00\", \"text\": \"Hey @eid_a253c65a, for the setup complexity, I think we should add a section on setup automation tools. Maybe we can include scripts or a step-by-step guide to simplify the process. Thoughts? 🤔\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260915-1-14fd9\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260915-1-14fd9\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"planning-EF_AIX\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-30c6d3\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_b6a30126\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-15T14:40:00\", \"text\": \"I agree with Julia. We could also enhance the user guidance section with more detailed documentation. Perhaps a quick-start guide for non-technical users? 📚\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260915-2-5b178\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260915-2-5b178\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"planning-EF_AIX\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-30c6d3\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_c9c3d8d5\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-15T14:43:00\", \"text\": \"For the performance inconsistencies, should we look into optimizing the data processing algorithms? The document could include a section on performance tuning tips for large datasets. @eid_91523bad, what do you think?\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260915-3-b3572\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260915-3-b3572\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"planning-EF_AIX\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-30c6d3\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_91523bad\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-15T14:47:00\", \"text\": \"Absolutely, @eid_c9c3d8d5. We should also consider adding a note on recommended hardware specs to ensure consistent performance across devices. 💡\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260915-4-9b42e\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260915-4-9b42e\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"planning-EF_AIX\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-30c6d3\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_a9002ae2\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-15T14:48:00\", \"text\": \"Regarding integration options, we might want to expand the integration layer section to include potential APIs or connectors. This could help with third-party app compatibility. 🤝\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260915-5-b633c\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260915-5-b633c\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"planning-EF_AIX\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-30c6d3\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_1a7d9807\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-15T14:51:00\", \"text\": \"Good point, Bob. We should also address the closed ecosystem approach in the design section. Maybe suggest a more open architecture to enhance flexibility? 🔄\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260915-6-0851a\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260915-6-0851a\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"planning-EF_AIX\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-30c6d3\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_9db3abf4\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-15T14:56:00\", \"text\": \"For the UI, let's add a subsection on user feedback incorporation. We need to make sure the design is intuitive for non-technical users. Perhaps more user-friendly features or customization options? 🖥️\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260915-7-0eb18\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260915-7-0eb18\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"planning-EF_AIX\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-30c6d3\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_caa2e58d\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-15T14:57:00\", \"text\": \"And for update disruptions, we should include a section on update management and rollback procedures. Ensuring backward compatibility is crucial for reliability. 🔄\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260915-8-d26b9\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260915-8-d26b9\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"planning-EF_AIX\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-30c6d3\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_2d8eff4d\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-15T14:58:00\", \"text\": \"Agreed, @eid_caa2e58d. We could also emphasize the importance of thorough testing before deployment in the technical section. 🧪\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260915-9-ec3b0\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260915-9-ec3b0\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"planning-EF_AIX\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-30c6d3\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_a253c65a\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-15T15:03:00\", \"text\": \"Great suggestions, everyone! Here's a quick summary: \\n1. Add setup automation tools and detailed user guidance. \\n2. Optimize data processing algorithms and specify hardware recommendations. \\n3. Expand integration options with APIs/connectors. \\n4. Enhance UI with user feedback and customization options. \\n5. Improve update management and ensure backward compatibility. \\nLet's start drafting these changes and reconvene next week to finalize. Thanks for the input! 🚀\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260915-10-05054\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260915-10-05054\"}\n{\"title\": \"Write API Documentation\", \"summary\": \"Create detailed documentation for the RESTful API, including usage instructions and endpoint details for third-party developers.\", \"link\": \"https://github.com/salesforce/EF_AIX/pull/23\", \"mergeable\": \"True\", \"merged\": \"True\", \"number\": \"23\", \"state\": \"closed\", \"user\": {\"login\": \"eid_54905dcb\"}, \"created_at\": \"2026-12-09T07:08:00\", \"reviews\": [{\"state\": \"APPROVED\", \"user\": {\"login\": \"eid_2347b567\"}, \"comment\": \"The documentation is comprehensive and well-organized. The endpoint descriptions and example usage are clear and easy to follow. Nice work! 👍\", \"submitted_at\": \"2026-12-09T21:17:00\"}, {\"state\": \"COMMENTED\", \"user\": {\"login\": \"eid_4df3bcc2\"}, \"comment\": \"The request/response formats are clearly outlined, and the examples are super helpful. Everything looks complete to me. Great job! 👏\", \"submitted_at\": \"2026-12-09T21:21:00\"}], \"id\": \"github_com_salesforce_EF_AIX_pull_23\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-juliamartinez-EdgeForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-7bfbef\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_91523bad\", \"timestamp\": \"2027-01-18T20:23:00\", \"text\": \"Hi team, several customers are reporting issues with EdgeForce that need our attention. Let's go through them one by one. 🚀\", \"utterranceID\": \"20270118-0-db28c\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20270118-0-db28c\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-juliamartinez-EdgeForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-7bfbef\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_91523bad\", \"timestamp\": \"2027-01-18T20:25:00\", \"text\": \"First up, we have an issue titled 'Inconsistent Model Visualization Updates'. The problem is that model visualizations aren't updating consistently when new data is processed. This affects the User Interface & Visualization Module and is causing frustration for users like CUST-0041. @eid_4df3bcc2, can you take this one?\", \"utterranceID\": \"20270118-1-3c041\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20270118-1-3c041\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-juliamartinez-EdgeForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-7bfbef\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_4df3bcc2\", \"timestamp\": \"2027-01-18T20:29:00\", \"text\": \"Got it! I'll look into the visualization updates and see what's causing the discrepancies. Thanks for the heads-up! 👍\", \"utterranceID\": \"20270118-2-16cd9\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20270118-2-16cd9\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-juliamartinez-EdgeForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-7bfbef\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_91523bad\", \"timestamp\": \"2027-01-18T20:34:00\", \"text\": \"Great, thanks! Next, we have a 'Faulty Edge Device Firmware Update' issue. The recent update is disrupting the AI Processing Engine's ability to handle concurrent tasks efficiently, impacting real-time data processing for customers like CUST-0012. @eid_bac7c6c4, can you handle this?\", \"utterranceID\": \"20270118-3-1913b\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20270118-3-1913b\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-juliamartinez-EdgeForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-7bfbef\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_bac7c6c4\", \"timestamp\": \"2027-01-18T20:35:00\", \"text\": \"Sure thing! I'll dive into the firmware update and see what's causing the disruption. Real-time processing is crucial, so I'll prioritize this. 🔍\", \"utterranceID\": \"20270118-4-3ca5e\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20270118-4-3ca5e\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-juliamartinez-EdgeForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-7bfbef\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_91523bad\", \"timestamp\": \"2027-01-18T20:38:00\", \"text\": \"Thanks, @eid_bac7c6c4! Lastly, there's an 'Unresponsive UI During Data Synchronization' issue. The UI becomes unresponsive during data sync, affecting the User Interface & Visualization Module and causing workflow interruptions for users like CUST-0021. @eid_2347b567, can you take a look?\", \"utterranceID\": \"20270118-5-c8155\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20270118-5-c8155\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-juliamartinez-EdgeForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-7bfbef\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_2347b567\", \"timestamp\": \"2027-01-18T20:39:00\", \"text\": \"On it! I'll investigate why the UI is freezing during data sync and work on a fix. Thanks for assigning this to me! 😊\", \"