inputs or additional resources.\\nHannah Martinez: Lastly, we have the task of improving security measures with a JWT-based authentication mechanism. Hannah, you submitted a PR that needs revisions. Ian, you'll be working on a new PR for this, right?\\nIan Miller: Yes, I'll take care of this implementation. I'll focus on secure token generation, validation, and expiration handling.\\nAlice Martinez: Thanks, Ian. Make sure to review the security protocols thoroughly. We want to ensure our API flows are as secure as possible.\\nHannah Taylor: Alright, team. That wraps up our sprint review. Let's keep the communication open and ensure we meet our deadlines. If there are no further questions, let's get back to work.\\nFiona Davis: Sounds good. Thanks, everyone!\", \"date\": \"2026-06-02T17:47:00\", \"document_type\": \"product-planning\", \"participants\": [\"eid_e5e36dc1\", \"eid_294ba09d\", \"eid_610a4c21\", \"eid_4e8b2cdc\", \"eid_5827604d\", \"eid_9a7b2132\", \"eid_f2474622\", \"eid_8605f7ee\", \"eid_71071933\", \"eid_399e4119\", \"eid_d098d618\", \"eid_d0d918f1\", \"eid_fc0f17c3\", \"eid_ba9224d2\", \"eid_b6268ef7\"], \"id\": \"product_dev_FForceAIX_3\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-alicedavis-FlowForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-ceaix-1deacc\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_71071933\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-06-20T23:52:00\", \"text\": \"Hi team, please check my PR for integrating event-driven architecture into our API flow: https://github.com/salesforce/FForceAIX/pull/8. This transition aims to decouple components and improve scalability and responsiveness. Let me know your thoughts! 🚀\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260623-0-44ca7\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260623-0-44ca7\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-alicedavis-FlowForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-ceaix-1deacc\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_9a7b2132\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-06-20T23:53:00\", \"text\": \"Hey @eid_71071933, thanks for sharing! I'll start reviewing it now. Excited to see how the event-driven model is shaping up. 😊\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260623-1-e6981\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260623-1-e6981\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-alicedavis-FlowForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-ceaix-1deacc\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_8605f7ee\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-06-20T23:54:00\", \"text\": \"Hi @eid_71071933, I'll take a look as well. The decoupling sounds promising for our scalability goals. 👍\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260623-2-703c6\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260623-2-703c6\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-alicedavis-FlowForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-ceaix-1deacc\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_9a7b2132\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-06-20T23:55:00\", \"text\": \"Okay, I've gone through the PR. The integration of the event-driven architecture looks solid, and I can see how components are now decoupled and communicating via events. Great work on that front! 🎉\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260623-3-ded36\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260623-3-ded36\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-alicedavis-FlowForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-ceaix-1deacc\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_8605f7ee\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-06-20T23:56:00\", \"text\": \"I agree with Ian, the decoupling is well-executed. However, I noticed that the system tests don't fully confirm that the new architecture maintains or improves current performance metrics. Some tests are showing a slight lag in response times. 🤔\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260623-4-2b568\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260623-4-2b568\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-alicedavis-FlowForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-ceaix-1deacc\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_71071933\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-06-21T00:01:00\", \"text\": \"Thanks for the feedback, @eid_8605f7ee. I'll dive into the performance tests and see what's causing the lag. Maybe some event handling needs optimization. I'll update the PR once I have a fix. 🔍\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260623-5-fcc84\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260623-5-fcc84\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-alicedavis-FlowForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-ceaix-1deacc\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_9a7b2132\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-06-21T00:06:00\", \"text\": \"Sounds good, @eid_71071933. Also, I noticed the documentation could use a bit more detail on the architectural changes. It would be helpful for onboarding new team members. 📚\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260623-6-770a6\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260623-6-770a6\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-alicedavis-FlowForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-ceaix-1deacc\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_71071933\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-06-21T00:10:00\", \"text\": \"Got it, Ian. I'll expand the documentation to include more details on the new architecture. Thanks for pointing that out! 😊\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260623-7-1c2f3\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260623-7-1c2f3\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-alicedavis-FlowForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-ceaix-1deacc\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_8605f7ee\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-06-21T00:14:00\", \"text\": \"Looking forward to the updates, @eid_71071933. Let us know if you need any help with the performance tests. We're here to support! 🤝\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260623-8-e142b\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260623-8-e142b\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-alicedavis-FlowForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-ceaix-1deacc\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_71071933\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-06-21T00:17:00\", \"text\": \"Will do, @eid_8605f7ee. Thanks for the support, team! I'll ping you once the updates are ready for another round of review. 🙌\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260623-9-cfb23\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260623-9-cfb23\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-alicedavis-FlowForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-ceaix-1deacc\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_8605f7ee\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-06-23T11:24:00\", \"text\": \"@here try out our product with this live demo https://sf-internal.slack.com/archives/FlowForce/demo_2\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260623-0-47318\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260623-0-47318\"}\n{\"transcript\": \"Attendees\\nAlice Davis, Alice Martinez, Alice Martinez, Hannah Taylor, Hannah Martinez, Ian Miller, George Martinez, Julia Garcia, George Brown, Fiona Davis, Ian Miller, Charlie Miller, Fiona Brown, Alice Taylor, Charlie Taylor\\nTranscript\\nHannah Martinez: Team, let’s get started. Today our focus is on finalizing the feature set for the next release of the MuleSoft Flow Optimizer. We need to ensure that our tasks align with the product’s goals of enhancing API efficiency, reducing latency, and providing comprehensive analytics.\\nAlice Martinez: Absolutely, Hannah. I think we should start by discussing the high-level tasks. We have four main features to focus on: enhancing the AI Engine's predictive capabilities, optimizing the Real-Time Processing Modules, expanding the Analytics Dashboard, and improving security measures.\\nIan Miller: For the AI Engine, we need to incorporate more diverse training data to improve its adaptability. This means we’ll need to define new APIs for data ingestion and update our data structures to handle the increased volume.\\nHannah Taylor: Right, Ian. We should also consider the database schema changes required to support this. Perhaps we can use a NoSQL database to handle the unstructured data more efficiently?\\nJulia Garcia: I agree, Julia. A NoSQL database like MongoDB could be a good fit here. We’ll need to ensure that our indexing strategies are optimized for quick data retrieval to maintain performance.\\nAlice Martinez: For the Real-Time Processing Modules, we need to implement more efficient algorithms. George, do you think we should explore event-driven architecture to handle peak loads better?\\nGeorge Martinez: Yes, Alice. An event-driven approach could help us scale dynamically. We should also look into using Kafka for real-time data streaming to minimize latency.\\nFiona Davis: On the Analytics Dashboard, we need to add more visualization options. This will require new frontend components. Fiona, do you have any thoughts on the UI/UX considerations?\\nFiona Brown: We should focus on making the dashboard more intuitive. Using React for dynamic components could enhance user interaction. We also need to ensure that the dashboard is responsive across devices.\\nAlice Taylor: Regarding security, we need to enhance our authentication mechanisms. Implementing JWT authentication could provide a more secure and scalable solution.\\nCharlie Taylor: Agreed, Charlie. We should also conduct regular security audits and ensure compliance with GDPR and HIPAA. This will involve updating our encryption protocols.\\nIan Miller: Now, let's talk about task prioritization and assignments. Ian, can you take the lead on the AI Engine enhancements?\\nIan Miller: Sure, I’ll handle the API development and data structure updates for the AI Engine.\\nGeorge Brown: I can work on the Real-Time Processing Modules. I'll focus on implementing the event-driven architecture and integrating Kafka.\\nJulia Garcia: I’ll take on the Analytics Dashboard improvements. I’ll start by designing the new frontend components and ensuring they align with our UI/UX goals.\\nHannah Taylor: Great. I’ll oversee the security enhancements, focusing on implementing JWT and updating our encryption protocols.\\nHannah Martinez: Are there any concerns about timelines or resources? We need to ensure that no one is overloaded and that we can meet our deadlines.\\nAlice Martinez: I think we’re in good shape, but we should keep an eye on the AI Engine task. It’s quite complex and might require additional resources.\\nAlice Martinez: If needed, we can reallocate some resources from the Analytics Dashboard task once the initial components are developed.\\nHannah Martinez: Perfect. Let’s finalize our goals and deliverables. Ian, you’ll deliver the AI Engine enhancements. George, you’ll handle the Real-Time Processing Modules. Julia, you’re on the Analytics Dashboard, and Charlie, you’ll manage the security updates.\\nIan Miller: Understood. I’ll start working on the AI Engine APIs and data structures immediately.\\nGeorge Brown: I’ll begin setting up the event-driven architecture for the processing modules.\\nJulia Garcia: I’ll focus on the frontend components for the dashboard and ensure they’re user-friendly.\\nHannah Taylor: I’ll start with the JWT implementation and review our current encryption protocols.\\nHannah Martinez: Great teamwork, everyone. Let’s reconvene next week to review our progress. Meeting adjourned.\", \"date\": \"2026-05-19T08:05:00\", \"document_type\": \"product-planning\", \"participants\": [\"eid_e5e36dc1\", \"eid_294ba09d\", \"eid_610a4c21\", \"eid_4e8b2cdc\", \"eid_5827604d\", \"eid_9a7b2132\", \"eid_f2474622\", \"eid_8605f7ee\", \"eid_71071933\", \"eid_399e4119\", \"eid_d098d618\", \"eid_d0d918f1\", \"eid_fc0f17c3\", \"eid_ba9224d2\", \"eid_b6268ef7\"], \"id\": \"product_dev_FForceAIX_1\"}\n{\"title\": \"Update Encryption Protocols for Enhanced Security\", \"summary\": \"Upgrade existing encryption protocols to more secure and modern standards. This PR focuses on updating encryption algorithms and ensuring all data in transit and at rest is securely encrypted.\", \"link\": \"https://github.com/salesforce/FForceAIX/pull/19\", \"mergeable\": \"True\", \"merged\": \"False\", \"number\": \"19\", \"state\": \"open\", \"user\": {\"login\": \"eid_71071933\"}, \"created_at\": \"2026-07-29T01:16:00\", \"reviews\": [{\"state\": \"APPROVED\", \"user\": {\"login\": \"eid_399e4119\"}, \"comment\": \"The encryption protocols are updated to the latest standards, and all sensitive data is encrypted both in transit and at rest. Great job! LGTM, approved! ✅\", \"submitted_at\": \"2026-07-29T06:34:00\"}, {\"state\": \"PENDING\", \"user\": {\"login\": \"eid_9a7b2132\"}, \"comment\": \"Checked the backward compatibility, and everything looks good. No issues found with existing integrations. Well done! LGTM, approved! 🎉\", \"submitted_at\": \"2026-07-29T06:35:00\"}, {\"state\": \"PENDING\", \"user\": {\"login\": \"eid_4e8b2cdc\"}, \"comment\": \"Ran through the tests, and everything is working perfectly. The encryption updates are effective and robust. Nice work! LGTM, approved! 🛡️\", \"submitted_at\": \"2026-07-29T06:37:00\"}], \"id\": \"github_com_salesforce_FForceAIX_pull_19\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-alicedavis-FlowForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-ceaix-1deacc\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_71bfb0a9\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-06-17T05:46:00\", \"text\": \"Hi team, I've been reviewing the recent changes from PR# 6 and noticed some potential security risks. Can we discuss whether we should consider reverting it?\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260616-0-63f3e\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260616-0-63f3e\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-alicedavis-FlowForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-ceaix-1deacc\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_5636d3f5\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-06-17T05:49:00\", \"text\": \"Hey @eid_71bfb0a9, what specific security risks are you concerned about? I want to make sure we're all on the same page.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260616-1-52bc1\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260616-1-52bc1\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-alicedavis-FlowForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-ceaix-1deacc\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_71bfb0a9\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-06-17T05:51:00\", \"text\": \"The main issue is that the JWT implementation might not be handling token expiration and validation securely. There could be vulnerabilities that expose user data.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260616-2-bd414\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260616-2-bd414\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-alicedavis-FlowForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-ceaix-1deacc\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_51f50b3a\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-06-17T05:52:00\", \"text\": \"That's concerning. @eid_9a7b2132, can you provide more details on how the token expiration and validation are handled in the PR?\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260616-3-411fe\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260616-3-411fe\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-alicedavis-FlowForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-ceaix-1deacc\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_9a7b2132\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-06-17T05:54:00\", \"text\": \"Sure, the tokens are set to expire after 30 minutes, and we use a secret key for validation. However, I understand there might be concerns about the strength of the key and the validation process.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260616-4-e4f49\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260616-4-e4f49\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-alicedavis-FlowForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-ceaix-1deacc\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_6936f36d\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-06-17T05:59:00\", \"text\": \"Thanks for clarifying, @eid_9a7b2132. @eid_71071933, @eid_8605f7ee, @eid_4e8b2cdc, what are your thoughts on this? Should we revert the PR?\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260616-5-4cb51\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260616-5-4cb51\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-alicedavis-FlowForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-ceaix-1deacc\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_71071933\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-06-17T06:01:00\", \"text\": \"I think if there's a potential risk, we should be cautious. It's better to address these concerns before they become a bigger issue.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260616-6-1f3fe\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260616-6-1f3fe\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-alicedavis-FlowForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-ceaix-1deacc\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_8605f7ee\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-06-17T06:05:00\", \"text\": \"Agreed. We should prioritize security. If there's any doubt, reverting might be the safest option.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260616-7-96626\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260616-7-96626\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-alicedavis-FlowForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-ceaix-1deacc\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_4e8b2cdc\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-06-17T06:08:00\", \"text\": \"I concur with @eid_71071933 and @eid_8605f7ee. Let's ensure the implementation is robust before proceeding.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260616-8-1d2d3\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260616-8-1d2d3\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-alicedavis-FlowForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-ceaix-1deacc\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_71bfb0a9\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-06-17T06:09:00\", \"text\": \"Alright, it seems like the consensus is to revert the PR for now. @eid_9a7b2132, could you handle that?\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260616-9-4b8fe\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260616-9-4b8fe\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-alicedavis-FlowForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-ceaix-1deacc\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_9a7b2132\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-06-17T06:12:00\", \"text\": \"Understood. I'll start the process to revert the PR soon and will address the security concerns raised. Thanks for the feedback, everyone.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260616-10-40fec\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260616-10-40fec\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-alicedavis-FlowForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-ceaix-1deacc\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_9a7b2132\", \"timestamp\": \"20