configured Export Permissions' issue. I'll dive into their PR to see how they tackled unauthorized access. We might find some useful strategies for our Data Export Module. 🔍\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260914-4-a6990\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260914-4-a6990\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-ianjones-LeadForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-585771\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_99835861\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-14T11:08:00\", \"text\": \"Awesome, Ian! Lastly, we have a bug from Django titled 'Improper Access Control in Admin Panel'. Non-admin users can access sensitive admin features. Here's the PR link: https://github.com/django/django/pull/607\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260914-5-a4cd4\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260914-5-a4cd4\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-ianjones-LeadForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-585771\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_3f4b2681\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-14T11:13:00\", \"text\": \"This is very similar to our 'Improper Access Control in Export API' issue. I'll review their fix and see if we can implement something similar to tighten our access controls. Thanks, Ian! 🔧\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260914-6-ba6bc\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260914-6-ba6bc\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-ianjones-LeadForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-585771\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_99835861\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-14T11:14:00\", \"text\": \"Thanks, Hannah! Let's keep these insights in mind as we work on our bugs. If you find anything particularly useful, please share it with the team. Let's keep pushing forward! 🚀\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260914-7-0e545\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260914-7-0e545\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-ianjones-LeadForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-585771\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_9f4e2c6f\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-14T11:15:00\", \"text\": \"Will do, Ian! Thanks for coordinating this. 😊\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260914-8-ff111\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260914-8-ff111\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-ianjones-LeadForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-585771\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_3f4b2681\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-14T11:16:00\", \"text\": \"Thanks, Ian! I'll keep everyone updated on any progress. 👍\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260914-9-dcd26\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260914-9-dcd26\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-ianjones-LeadForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-585771\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_9f4e2c6f\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-12-02T05:18:00\", \"text\": \"Hi team, the bug titled 'Security Vulnerability in Lead Data Export' has been resolved. You can check the details in the approved PR here: https://github.com/salesforce/LeadForce/pull/60.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261201-0-4e189\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261201-0-4e189\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-ianjones-LeadForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-585771\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_3f4b2681\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-12-02T05:19:00\", \"text\": \"Great news, @eid_9f4e2c6f! Can you explain what the root cause was?\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261201-1-7f34a\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261201-1-7f34a\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-ianjones-LeadForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-585771\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_9f4e2c6f\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-12-02T05:24:00\", \"text\": \"Sure, Hannah. The root cause was that the export module lacked proper encryption protocols for securing data during file generation. This led to sensitive lead information being exposed during the export process.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261201-2-b3825\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261201-2-b3825\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-ianjones-LeadForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-585771\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_99835861\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-12-02T05:29:00\", \"text\": \"Thanks for the update, Ian. How did you manage to fix it?\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261201-3-d5d00\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261201-3-d5d00\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-ianjones-LeadForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-585771\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_9f4e2c6f\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-12-02T05:32:00\", \"text\": \"To resolve the issue, I implemented AES-256 encryption for the exported files. This ensures that all sensitive lead data is securely encrypted during the export process. Additionally, I added a verification step to ensure that the encryption is applied correctly before the files are made available for download.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261201-4-6aca5\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261201-4-6aca5\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-ianjones-LeadForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-585771\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_3f4b2681\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-12-02T05:33:00\", \"text\": \"That sounds like a solid fix, Ian. Thanks for handling this so quickly!\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261201-5-c2ea5\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261201-5-c2ea5\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-ianjones-LeadForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-585771\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_99835861\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-12-02T05:35:00\", \"text\": \"Agreed, @eid_9f4e2c6f. Thanks for the quick turnaround. Let me know if there's anything else you need from us.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261201-6-6d1bf\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261201-6-6d1bf\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-ianjones-LeadForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-585771\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_9f4e2c6f\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-12-02T05:36:00\", \"text\": \"Thanks, @eid_3f4b2681 and Ian. I'll keep you posted if anything else comes up. Appreciate the support!\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261201-7-5fc71\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261201-7-5fc71\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-ianjones-LeadForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-585771\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_99835861\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-12-14T10:30:00\", \"text\": \"Hi team, several customers are reporting issues with LeadForce that need our attention. Let's go through them one by one. 🚀\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261213-0-a1ebc\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261213-0-a1ebc\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-ianjones-LeadForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-585771\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_99835861\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-12-14T10:32:00\", \"text\": \"First up, we have an issue titled 'Insecure Data Transmission in Export Process'. The lead data is being transmitted over unsecured channels during export, which could lead to data breaches. This affects the Data Export Module and impacts customer CUST-0040. @eid_07cc9100, this one's for you. Can you take a look? 🔍\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261213-1-9c61e\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261213-1-9c61e\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-ianjones-LeadForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-585771\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_07cc9100\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-12-14T10:37:00\", \"text\": \"Got it! I'll prioritize this and ensure the data transmission is secured. Thanks for the heads-up! 🔒\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261213-2-8bc96\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261213-2-8bc96\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-ianjones-LeadForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-585771\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_99835861\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-12-14T10:40:00\", \"text\": \"Great, thanks! Next, we have 'Progress Bar Stalls During Import'. The progress bar isn't updating in real-time during lead import, making the system seem unresponsive. This affects the User Interface and impacts customer CUST-0003. @eid_c39dc658, can you handle this one? 🛠️\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261213-3-bb089\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261213-3-bb089\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-ianjones-LeadForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-585771\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_c39dc658\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-12-14T10:44:00\", \"text\": \"Sure thing! I'll dive into the UI code and see what's causing the delay. Thanks for assigning this to me! 👍\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261213-4-1a913\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261213-4-1a913\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-ianjones-LeadForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-585771\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_99835861\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-12-14T10:49:00\", \"text\": \"Awesome, thanks! Lastly, there's an issue with a 'Modal Dialog Blocks UI Interaction'. A modal dialog is blocking users from accessing other parts of the app during lead import. This also affects the User Interface and impacts customer CUST-0091. @eid_07cc9100, could you also take this one? 🖥️\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261213-5-0b1d4\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261213-5-0b1d4\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-ianjones-LeadForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-585771\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_07cc9100\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-12-14T10:53:00\", \"text\": \"No problem, I'll tackle this along with the data transmission issue. Let's make sure our users can multitask smoothly! 💪\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261213-6-023dc\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261213-6-023dc\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-ianjones-LeadForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-585771\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_99835861\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-12-14T10:54:00\", \"text\": \"Thanks, everyone! Let's keep our customers happy and productive. Feel free to reach out if you need any more details or support. 🙌\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261213-7-b34fd\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261213-7-b34fd\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-ianjones-LeadForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-585771\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_c39dc658\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-12-14T10:57:00\", \"text\": \"Will do! Let's get these sorted out. 💼\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261213-8-bce7c\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261213-8-bce7c\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-ianjones-LeadForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-585771\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_07cc9100\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-12-14T10:59:00\", \"text\": \"Absolutely, let's get to work! 🏃‍♂️\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261213-9-98f18\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261213-9-98f18\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-ianjones-LeadForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-585771\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_99835861\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-12-15T21:35:00\", \"text\": \"Hi team, I've found some interesting open-source bugs that might give us insights into our current issues. Let's take a look! 🚀\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261215-0-82689\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261215-0-82689\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-ianjones-LeadForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-585771\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_99835861\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-12-15T21:39:00\", \"text\": \"First up, there's an issue in OpenSSL titled 'Insecure Data Transmission in SSL Handshake'. It seems data is being transmitted without proper encryption during the SSL handshake, which is similar to our data transmission issue. Here's the PR link: https://github.com/openssl/openssl/pull/637. @George Garcia, what do you think?\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261215-1-bd08c\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261215-1-bd08c\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-ianjones-LeadForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-585771\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_07cc9100\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-12-15T21:43:00\", \"text\": \"Thanks, Ian! This is quite similar to what we're seeing with the Data Export Module. I'll review their approach to securing the transmission and see if we can apply any of their solutions. 🔒\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261215-2-dbc3a\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261215-2-dbc3a\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-ianjones-LeadForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-585771\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_99835861\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-12-15T21:48:00\", \"text\": \"Great, George! Next, there's a React issue titled 'Progress Bar Stalls During Component Loading'. The progress bar isn't updating in real-time, which is causing user confusion. Sounds familiar, right? Here's the PR: https://github.com/facebook/react/pull/638. Ian Miller, any thoughts?\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261215-3-fc669\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261215-3-fc669\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-ianjones-LeadForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-585771\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_c39dc658\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-12-15T21:49:00\", \"text\": \"Definitely sounds like our progress bar issue! I'll check out how they tackled the real-time update problem and see if we can implement something similar. Thanks for sharing! 👍\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261215-4-07e0d\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261215-4-07e0d\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-ianjones-LeadForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-585771\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_99835861\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-12-15T21:52:00\", \"text\": \"Awesome, Ian! Lastly, there's a Bootstrap issue titled 'Modal Dialog Blocks Background Interaction'. The modal dialogs are preventing users from interacting with other page elements, which disrupts the workflow. Here's the PR link: https://github.com/twbs/bootstrap/pull/639. George, since you're handling a similar issue, could you take a look?\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261215-5-b1039\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261215-5-b1039\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-ianjones-LeadForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-585771\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_07cc9100\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-12-15T21:54:00\", \"text\": \"Sure thing, Ian! I'll review their solution for allowing background interaction and see if we can adapt it for our UI. Let's make sure our users can multitask smoothly! 💪\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261215-6-92c14\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261215-6-92c14\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-ianjones-LeadForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-585771\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_99835861\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-12-15T21:58:00\", \"text\": \"Thanks, everyone! Let's use these insights to enhance our solutions. Feel free to reach out if you need any more details or support. 🙌\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261215-7-52af0\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261215-7-52af0\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-ianjones-LeadForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-585771\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_c39dc658\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-12-15T21:59:00\", \"text\": \"Will do! Let's get these sorted out. 💼\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261215-8-9db77\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261215-8-9db77\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-ianjones-LeadForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-585771\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_07cc9100\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-12-15T22:02:00\", \"text\": \"Absolutely, let's get to work! 🏃‍♂️\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261215-9-80513\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261215-9-80513\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-iangarcia-LeadForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-bd5140\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_f98d7490\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-28T12:44:00\", \"text\": \"Hi team, I've found some interesting open-source bugs that might give us insights into our current issues. Let's take a look and see how they tackled similar problems. 🚀\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260928-0-82a54\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260928-0-82a54\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-iangarcia-LeadForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-bd5140\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_f98d7490\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-28T12:46:00\", \"text\": \"First up, we have a bug in Redis titled 'Cache Invalidation Bug'. It deals with improper cache invalidation leading to stale data, similar to our 'Caching Layer Inconsistencies' issue. Here's the PR link: https://github.com/redis/redis/pull/613. @Fiona Miller, could you take a look and see if there are any strategies we can apply?\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260928-1-71619\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260928-1-71619\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-iangarcia-LeadForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-bd5140\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_a43a4389\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-28T12:48:00\", \"text\": \"Sure thing, Ian! I'll review the Redis PR and see if their approach to cache invalidation can help us refine our policies. Thanks for pointing this out! 🔍\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260928-2-5d11a\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260928-2-5d11a\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-iangarcia-LeadForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-bd5140\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_f98d7490\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-28T12:53:00\", \"text\": \"Next, there's a bug in TensorFlow titled 'Incorrect Weight Assignment in Neural Networks'. It involves misconfigured weight initialization, which is quite similar to our 'Incorrect Weighting of Engagement Metrics' issue. Check out the PR here: https://github.com/tensorflow/tensorflow/pull/614. Bob, could you dive into this one?\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260928-3-4c419\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260928-3-4c419\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-iangarcia-LeadForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-bd5140\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_a23a73c4\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-28T12:56:00\", \"text\": \"Absolutely, Ian! I'll analyze how TensorFlow addressed the weight assignment problem and see if we can adapt their solution to improve our scoring algorithm. 💪\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260928-4-136c0\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260928-4-136c0\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-iangarcia-LeadForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-bd5140\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_f98d7490\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-28T13:01:00\", \"text\": \"Lastly, there's an issue in Apache Kafka titled 'Delayed Message Processing'. It deals with asynchronous processing delays, much like our 'Asynchronous Processing Delays' problem. Here's the PR link: https://github.com/apache/kafka/pull/615. David, could you take a look at this one?\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260928-5-cceaf\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260928-5-cceaf\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-iangarcia-LeadForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-bd5140\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_cac9a0ac\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-28T13:06:00\", \"text\": \"On it, Ian! I'll review Kafka's approach to handling message processing delays and see if we can optimize our real-time data synchronization similarly. ⚡\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260928-6-b2a3d\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260928-6-b2a3d\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-iangarcia-LeadForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-bd5140\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_f98d7490\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-28T13:08:00\", \"text\": \"Thanks, everyone! Let's keep these insights in mind as we work on our issues. Feel free to share any findings or ideas that could help us improve. 🙌\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260928-7-1a899\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260928-7-1a899\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-iangarcia-LeadForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-bd5140\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_a43a4389\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-28T13:10:00\", \"text\": \"Will do! I'll update once I have more info from the Redis PR. 🛠️\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260928-8-e7607\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260928-8-e7607\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-iangarcia-LeadForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-bd5140\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_a23a73c4\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-28T13:13:00\", \"text\": \"Same here. Let's leverage these open-source solutions to enhance our products. 🚀\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260928-9-0c13c\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260928-9-0c13c\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-iangarcia-LeadForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-bd5140\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_cac9a0ac\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-28T13:18:00\", \"text\": \"Absolutely, I'll keep you posted on my progress with the Kafka insights. Thanks for coordinating, Ian!\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260928-10-34181\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260928-10-34181\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-iangarcia-LeadForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-bd5140\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_f98d7490\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-08T19:59:00\", \"text\": \"Hi team, several customers are reporting issues with LeadForce that need our attention. Let's go through them one by one. 😊\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261008-0-58285\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261008-0-58285\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-iangarcia-LeadForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-bd5140\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_f98d7490\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-08T20:04:00\", \"text\": \"First up, we have an issue titled 'Bias in Training Data Skews Lead Scores'. The AI model is trained on a dataset with inherent biases, leading to skewed lead scores. This affects the AI Scoring Algorithm and impacts Customer CUST-0006. @eid_207da0e7, this one's for you.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261008-1-64c2b\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261008-1-64c2b\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-iangarcia-LeadForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-bd5140\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_207da0e7\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-08T20:09:00\", \"text\": \"Got it, I'll dive into the training data and see how we can mitigate these biases. Thanks for the heads-up! 👍\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261008-2-721dd\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261008-2-721dd\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-iangarcia-LeadForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-bd5140\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_f98d7490\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-08T20:12:00\", \"text\": \"Great, thanks! Next, we have 'Incorrect Lead Scoring Due to Data Mismatch'. The AI model assigns incorrect scores when there's a mismatch between the historical data schema and the current input data format. This also affects the AI Scoring Algorithm and impacts Customer CUST-0037. @eid_a43a4389, can you take this one?\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261008-3-4a17d\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261008-3-4a17d\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-iangarcia-LeadForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-bd5140\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_a43a4389\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-08T20:14:00\", \"text\": \"Sure thing! I'll check the data schemas and ensure they align correctly. Let's get those scores back on track! 🚀\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261008-4-8fa38\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261008-4-8fa38\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-iangarcia-LeadForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-bd5140\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_f98d7490\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-08T20:17:00\", \"text\": \"Awesome, thanks! Lastly, we have 'UI Freezes During Bulk Lead Import'. The UI becomes unresponsive during large imports, affecting the User Interface and impacting Customer CUST-0040. @eid_90359c89, can you handle this?\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261008-5-83551\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261008-5-83551\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-iangarcia-LeadForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-bd5140\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_90359c89\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-08T20:19:00\", \"text\": \"On it! I'll look into optimizing the import process to keep the UI responsive. Thanks for assigning this to me! 💪\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261008-6-c1d0c\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261008-6-c1d0c\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-iangarcia-LeadForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-bd5140\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_f98d7490\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-08T20:23:00\", \"text\": \"Thanks, everyone! Let's keep our customers happy and resolve these issues ASAP. Feel free to reach out if you need any help or additional info. 🙌\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261008-7-9b71c\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261008-7-9b71c\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-iangarcia-LeadForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-bd5140\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_207da0e7\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-08T20:28:00\", \"text\": \"Will do! Let's get to work. 💼\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261008-8-e977c\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261008-8-e977c\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-iangarcia-LeadForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-bd5140\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_a43a4389\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-08T20:29:00\", \"text\": \"Thanks, team! Let's make it happen. 💪\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261008-9-25d1e\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261008-9-25d1e\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-iangarcia-LeadForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-bd5140\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_90359c89\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-08T20:33:00\", \"text\": \"Thanks, all! Let's fix these bugs! 🐛\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261008-10-c41a9\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261008-10-c41a9\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-ianjones-LeadForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-585771\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_99835861\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-15T06:19:00\", \"text\": \"Hi team, I've found some interesting open-source bugs that might help us with our current Salesforce issues. Let's take a look at them together! 😊\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261015-0-3ac85\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261015-0-3ac85\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-ianjones-LeadForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-585771\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_99835861\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-15T06:20:00\", \"text\": \"First up, there's a 'Data Type Mismatch in Query Results' in PostgreSQL. Users are facing errors due to mismatched data types, which is affecting data retrieval accuracy. Here's the PR link: https://github.com/postgres/postgres/pull/621. @eid_c39dc658, this seems similar to the data type mismatch issue you're working on. Thoughts?\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261015-1-5c3fa\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261015-1-5c3fa\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-ianjones-LeadForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-585771\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_c39dc658\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-15T06:21:00\", \"text\": \"Thanks, Ian! This is definitely relevant. I'll review the PR to see how they approached the problem and if there are any insights we can apply to our LeadForce issue. 👍\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261015-2-cd07d\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261015-2-cd07d\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-ianjones-LeadForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-585771\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_99835861\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-15T06:25:00\", \"text\": \"Great! Next, we have a 'UI Lag Due to Excessive Re-renders' in React. Frequent component re-renders are causing noticeable lag, impacting user interactions. Check out the PR here: https://github.com/facebook/react/pull/622. Hannah, this might be useful for the DOM updates issue you're tackling.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261015-3-dc107\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261015-3-dc107\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-ianjones-LeadForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-585771\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_3f4b2681\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-15T06:30:00\", \"text\": \"Perfect timing, Ian! I'll dive into this PR and see if their optimization strategies can help us reduce the lag in our UI. 🚀\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261015-4-4a194\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261015-4-4a194\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-ianjones-LeadForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-585771\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_99835861\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-15T06:32:00\", \"text\": \"Awesome! Lastly, there's an 'Incorrect Data Import Mapping' issue in MySQL. Their data import processes are resulting in incorrect field mappings, leading to erroneous database entries. Here's the PR: https://github.com/mysql/mysql-server/pull/623. Bob, this seems quite similar to the data import issue you're handling.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261015-5-e0fd7\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261015-5-e0fd7\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-ianjones-LeadForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-585771\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_652e8cd0\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-15T06:33:00\", \"text\": \"Thanks, Ian! I'll review the MySQL PR to see how they addressed the mapping issues. It might give us some good pointers for our own data import process. 🛠️\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261015-6-d5cc4\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261015-6-d5cc4\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-ianjones-LeadForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-585771\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_99835861\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-15T06:38:00\", \"text\": \"Thanks, everyone! Let's keep these open-source examples in mind as we work through our bugs. Feel free to share any insights or updates here. Let's get these resolved for our customers! 💪\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261015-7-7d60e\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261015-7-7d60e\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-ianjones-LeadForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-585771\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_c39dc658\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-15T06:40:00\", \"text\": \"Will do! If anyone finds more relevant examples, please share. 🤔\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261015-8-1c024\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261015-8-1c024\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-ianjones-LeadForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-585771\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_3f4b2681\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-15T06:43:00\", \"text\": \"Same here, any additional tips on optimizing re-renders are welcome! 🙌\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261015-9-6a309\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261015-9-6a309\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-ianjones-LeadForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-585771\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_652e8cd0\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-15T06:48:00\", \"text\": \"I'll keep you all posted on my progress. Thanks for the support, team! 😊\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261015-10-f5750\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261015-10-f5750\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-ianjones-LeadForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-585771\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_99835861\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-24T22:51:00\", \"text\": \"Hi team, several customers are reporting issues with LeadForce that we need to address ASAP. Let's go through them one by one. 🚀\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261024-0-e9730\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261024-0-e9730\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-ianjones-LeadForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-585771\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_99835861\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-24T22:53:00\", \"text\": \"First up, we have a security vulnerability in the Lead Data Export module. Sensitive lead information is exposed due to insufficient encryption during export. This is a big risk for data breaches and violates data protection regulations. Impacted customer is CUST-0065. @eid_9f4e2c6f, can you take this one?\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261024-1-ce85b\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261024-1-ce85b\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-ianjones-LeadForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-585771\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_9f4e2c6f\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-24T22:56:00\", \"text\": \"Got it! I'll prioritize this and start working on a fix right away. Thanks for the heads-up! 🔒\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261024-2-0806c\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261024-2-0806c\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-ianjones-LeadForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-585771\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_99835861\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-24T22:57:00\", \"text\": \"Thanks, @eid_9f4e2c6f! Next, we have an issue with UI thread starvation from background tasks. The lead scoring and qualification tasks are consuming too many resources, causing the UI to become unresponsive during import. This is affecting customer CUST-0054. @eid_3f4b2681, can you handle this?\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261024-3-3971c\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261024-3-3971c\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-ianjones-LeadForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-585771\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_3f4b2681\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-24T23:02:00\", \"text\": \"Sure thing! I'll dive into the resource management for those tasks and see how we can optimize it. 👍\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261024-4-53940\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261024-4-53940\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-ianjones-LeadForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-585771\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_99835861\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-24T23:04:00\", \"text\": \"Awesome, thanks! Lastly, there's a data corruption issue in the Lead Database. Some lead records are getting corrupted during write operations, leading to incomplete or incorrect data entries. This is impacting customer CUST-0013. @eid_3f4b2681, can you also take this one?\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261024-5-79ec8\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261024-5-79ec8\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-ianjones-LeadForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-585771\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_3f4b2681\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-24T23:05:00\", \"text\": \"No problem, I'll look into the database write operations and see what's causing the corruption. 🛠️\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261024-6-6eff1\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261024-6-6eff1\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-ianjones-LeadForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-585771\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_99835861\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-24T23:06:00\", \"text\": \"Great, thanks for jumping on these so quickly, team! If you need any more details or run into issues, just ping me. Let's get these resolved and keep our customers happy! 😊\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261024-7-9abee\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261024-7-9abee\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-ianjones-LeadForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-585771\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_9f4e2c6f\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-24T23:09:00\", \"text\": \"Will do! Thanks for coordinating, @eid_99835861!\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261024-8-4126f\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261024-8-4126f\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-ianjones-LeadForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-585771\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_3f4b2681\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-24T23:13:00\", \"text\": \"Thanks, everyone! Let's get to work! 💪\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261024-9-cb7b4\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261024-9-cb7b4\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-ianjones-LeadForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-585771\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_99835861\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-26T08:55:00\", \"text\": \"Hi team, I've found some interesting open-source bugs that might help us with our current Salesforce issues. Let's take a look and see what we can learn! 🚀\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261026-0-9fda9\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261026-0-9fda9\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-ianjones-LeadForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-585771\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_99835861\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-26T08:57:00\", \"text\": \"First up, there's a bug in OpenSSL related to weak encryption in data transmission. It seems similar to our Lead Data Export issue. Here's the PR link: https://github.com/openssl/openssl/pull/625. @eid_9f4e2c6f, what do you think?\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261026-1-64dd1\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261026-1-64dd1\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-ianjones-LeadForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-585771\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_9f4e2c6f\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-26T09:01:00\", \"text\": \"Thanks, Ian! This looks quite relevant. The outdated encryption algorithms in OpenSSL could give us insights into strengthening our encryption methods. I'll review the PR and see if there are any strategies we can apply. 🔒\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261026-2-ece17\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261026-2-ece17\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-ianjones-LeadForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-585771\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_99835861\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-26T09:04:00\", \"text\": \"Great, Ian! Next, there's a PR in the Electron project about UI freeze during heavy background processing. This is similar to our UI thread starvation issue. Check it out here: https://github.com/electron/electron/pull/626. Hannah, any thoughts?\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261026-3-6af1d\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261026-3-6af1d\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-ianjones-LeadForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-585771\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_3f4b2681\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-26T09:06:00\", \"text\": \"This is spot on, Ian! The Electron issue with background tasks consuming too many resources is just like what we're seeing. I'll dive into their approach and see if we can optimize our resource management similarly. 👍\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261026-4-138be\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261026-4-138be\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-ianjones-LeadForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-585771\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_99835861\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-26T09:07:00\", \"text\": \"Awesome, Hannah! Lastly, there's a PostgreSQL bug about data corruption in concurrent writes. Sounds a lot like our Lead Database issue. Here's the PR: https://github.com/postgres/postgres/pull/627. Can you take a look at this one too?\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261026-5-fa203\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261026-5-fa203\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-ianjones-LeadForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-585771\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_3f4b2681\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-26T09:12:00\", \"text\": \"Sure thing, Ian! The concurrent write operations causing data corruption in PostgreSQL could definitely give us some clues. I'll review their fix and see how we can apply it to our database operations. 🛠️\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261026-6-f6906\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261026-6-f6906\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-ianjones-LeadForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-585771\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_99835861\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-26T09:16:00\", \"text\": \"Thanks, team! Let's use these insights to tackle our issues effectively. If you find anything particularly useful, let's discuss it further. Keep me posted on your progress! 😊\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261026-7-b4b11\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261026-7-b4b11\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-ianjones-LeadForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-585771\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_9f4e2c6f\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-26T09:20:00\", \"text\": \"Will do, Ian! Thanks for finding these resources. Let's get to work! 💪\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261026-8-081f9\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261026-8-081f9\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-ianjones-LeadForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-585771\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_3f4b2681\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-26T09:24:00\", \"text\": \"Thanks, everyone! Let's make sure our fixes are as robust as possible. 🚀\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261026-9-949af\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261026-9-949af\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-ianjones-LeadForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-585771\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_9f4e2c6f\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-01T17:26:00\", \"text\": \"Hi team, the bug about incorrect lead scoring due to feature drift has been resolved. You can check out the details in the approved PR here: https://github.com/salesforce/LeadForce/pull/46.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261001-0-e22f7\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261001-0-e22f7\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-ianjones-LeadForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-585771\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_3f4b2681\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-01T17:29:00\", \"text\": \"Thanks for the update, Ian! Can you remind us what the root cause was?\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261001-1-57087\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261001-1-57087\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-ianjones-LeadForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-585771\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_9f4e2c6f\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-01T17:30:00\", \"text\": \"Sure, Hannah. The root cause was that our AI model hadn't been retrained to account for recent shifts in lead engagement patterns. This led to feature drift, causing the scoring algorithm to produce inconsistent and outdated lead scores.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261001-2-089c7\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261001-2-089c7\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-ianjones-LeadForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-585771\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_99835861\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-01T17:33:00\", \"text\": \"Got it, Ian. How did you manage to fix it?\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261001-3-9ae18\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261001-3-9ae18\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-ianjones-LeadForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-585771\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_9f4e2c6f\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-01T17:35:00\", \"text\": \"@eid_99835861, I addressed the issue by updating our model retraining schedule. Now, the model will be retrained every two weeks to ensure it captures any shifts in lead behavior. Additionally, I implemented a monitoring system to alert us if feature drift is detected in the future.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261001-4-17ab6\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261001-4-17ab6\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-ianjones-LeadForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-585771\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_3f4b2681\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-01T17:38:00\", \"text\": \"That sounds like a solid plan, Ian. Thanks for taking care of this so quickly!\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261001-5-fdaf3\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261001-5-fdaf3\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-ianjones-LeadForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-585771\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_99835861\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-01T17:41:00\", \"text\": \"Agreed, thanks Ian. This should help us maintain more accurate lead scores moving forward.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261001-6-6162f\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261001-6-6162f\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-ianjones-LeadForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-585771\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_9f4e2c6f\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-01T17:46:00\", \"text\": \"No problem, glad to help! Let me know if you notice any other issues.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261001-7-dd59f\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261001-7-dd59f\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-ianjones-LeadForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-585771\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_99835861\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-13T03:26:00\", \"text\": \"Hi team, several customers are reporting issues with LeadForce that we need to address. Let's go through them one by one. 😊\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261013-0-104eb\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261013-0-104eb\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-ianjones-LeadForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-585771\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_99835861\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-13T03:27:00\", \"text\": \"First up, we have a 'Data Type Mismatch in Lead Attributes'. This is affecting our Database Management System and causing errors in lead scoring algorithms. Impacted customer is CUST-0040. @eid_c39dc658, can you take this one?\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261013-1-1d019\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261013-1-1d019\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-ianjones-LeadForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-585771\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_c39dc658\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-13T03:32:00\", \"text\": \"Got it! I'll start looking into the data type mismatch issue right away. Thanks for the heads-up! 👍\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261013-2-0952b\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261013-2-0952b\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-ianjones-LeadForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-585771\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_99835861\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-13T03:36:00\", \"text\": \"Great, thanks! Next, there's a 'UI Lag Due to Excessive DOM Updates'. This is impacting the User Interface, making it hard for users to perform other tasks during the import process. Customer CUST-0032 is affected. @eid_3f4b2681, can you handle this?\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261013-3-7eab9\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261013-3-7eab9\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-ianjones-LeadForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-585771\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_3f4b2681\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-13T03:37:00\", \"text\": \"Sure thing! I'll dive into the DOM updates and see how we can optimize it to reduce the lag. 🚀\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261013-4-532a0\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261013-4-532a0\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-ianjones-LeadForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-585771\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_99835861\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-13T03:40:00\", \"text\": \"Awesome, thanks! Lastly, we have an 'Incorrect Data Import Process'. This is also affecting our Database Management System, leading to erroneous data entries. Customer CUST-0091 is impacted. @eid_652e8cd0, can you take care of this one?\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261013-5-e98a9\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261013-5-e98a9\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-ianjones-LeadForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-585771\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_652e8cd0\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-13T03:41:00\", \"text\": \"Absolutely, I'll investigate the data import process and work on correcting the mapping issues. 🛠️\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261013-6-193f5\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261013-6-193f5\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-ianjones-LeadForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-585771\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_99835861\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-13T03:44:00\", \"text\": \"Thanks, everyone! Let's keep communication open as you work through these. Feel free to ask questions or share updates here. Let's get these resolved for our customers! 💪\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261013-7-15a4a\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261013-7-15a4a\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-ianjones-LeadForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-585771\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_c39dc658\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-13T03:45:00\", \"text\": \"Will do! If anyone has insights on similar issues, feel free to share. 🤔\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261013-8-d5862\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261013-8-d5862\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-ianjones-LeadForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-585771\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_3f4b2681\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-13T03:46:00\", \"text\": \"Same here, any tips on optimizing DOM updates are welcome! 🙌\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261013-9-0c148\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261013-9-0c148\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-ianjones-LeadForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-585771\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_652e8cd0\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-13T03:51:00\", \"text\": \"I'll keep you all posted on my progress. Thanks for the support, team! 😊\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261013-10-4215c\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261013-10-4215c\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-ianjones-LeadForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-585771\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_07cc9100\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-12-27T07:23:00\", \"text\": \"Hi team, I looked into the reported issue about insecure data transmission during the export process.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261226-0-c7896\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261226-0-c7896\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-ianjones-LeadForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-585771\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_07cc9100\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-12-27T07:28:00\", \"text\": \"The concern was that lead data is being transmitted over unsecured channels, potentially exposing it to interception.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261226-1-c339a\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261226-1-c339a\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-ianjones-LeadForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-585771\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_07cc9100\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-12-27T07:32:00\", \"text\": \"After reviewing the export module, I found that the transmission is actually occurring over a secure internal network, which is isolated from external access.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261226-2-5bf01\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261226-2-5bf01\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-ianjones-LeadForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-585771\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_07cc9100\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-12-27T07:33:00\", \"text\": \"The module does not enforce HTTPS because it's designed to operate within this secure environment, where additional encryption is not necessary.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261226-3-5ccae\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261226-3-5ccae\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-ianjones-LeadForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-585771\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_99835861\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-12-27T07:34:00\", \"text\": \"Thanks for the update, George. So, it's functioning as intended within our internal network?\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261226-4-4f3db\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261226-4-4f3db\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-ianjones-LeadForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-585771\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_07cc9100\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-12-27T07:38:00\", \"text\": \"Exactly, @eid_99835861. The data is not exposed to the internet, so the risk of interception is negligible.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261226-5-3b877\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261226-5-3b877\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-ianjones-LeadForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-585771\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_c39dc658\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-12-27T07:41:00\", \"text\": \"Good to know. Did you verify the network configuration to ensure it's isolated as expected?\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261226-6-fba57\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261226-6-fba57\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-ianjones-LeadForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-585771\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_07cc9100\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-12-27T07:42:00\", \"text\": \"Yes, Ian Miller. I checked the network setup and confirmed that the environment is correctly configured to prevent external access.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261226-7-2ce37\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261226-7-2ce37\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-ianjones-LeadForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-585771\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_99835861\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-12-27T07:44:00\", \"text\": \"Great work, George. It's reassuring to know that our internal processes are secure.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261226-8-fc80c\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261226-8-fc80c\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-ianjones-LeadForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-585771\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_07cc9100\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-12-27T07:49:00\", \"text\": \"Thanks, everyone. I'll document this in the bug report and close it as 'No Fix Needed'. Let me know if there are any other concerns.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261226-9-01695\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261226-9-01695\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-ianjones-LeadForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-585771\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_c39dc658\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-12-29T17:47:00\", \"text\": \"Hi team, the bug titled 'Progress Bar Stalls During Import' has been resolved. You can check the approved PR here: https://github.com/salesforce/LeadForce/pull/63.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261229-0-c0df0\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261229-0-c0df0\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-ianjones-LeadForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-585771\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_c39dc658\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-12-29T17:52:00\", \"text\": \"The root cause was that the progress bar wasn't linked to the asynchronous import process, which meant it didn't update in real-time and appeared unresponsive to users.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261229-1-6a5e5\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261229-1-6a5e5\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-ianjones-LeadForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-585771\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_c39dc658\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-12-29T17:54:00\", \"text\": \"To fix this, I updated the progress bar to listen for events from the import process. Now, it receives real-time updates and reflects the actual progress accurately.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261229-2-4c99a\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261229-2-4c99a\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-ianjones-LeadForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-585771\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_07cc9100\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-12-29T17:56:00\", \"text\": \"Great work, @eid_c39dc658! This should improve the user experience significantly.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261229-3-82fbc\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261229-3-82fbc\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-ianjones-LeadForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-585771\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_99835861\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-12-29T18:01:00\", \"text\": \"Thanks, Ian Miller! I’ll test it out and confirm everything is working as expected.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261229-4-1af3a\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261229-4-1af3a\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-ianjones-LeadForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-585771\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_c39dc658\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-12-29T18:06:00\", \"text\": \"Thanks, George and Ian Jones. Let me know if you encounter any issues during testing.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261229-5-ca17e\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261229-5-ca17e\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-ianjones-LeadForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-585771\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_c39dc658\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-16T06:46:00\", \"text\": \"Hi team, the bug about incorrect data types in lead attributes has been resolved. You can check the details in the approved PR here: https://github.com/salesforce/LeadForce/pull/55.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261115-0-814e7\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261115-0-814e7\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-ianjones-LeadForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-585771\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_3f4b2681\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-16T06:48:00\", \"text\": \"Great news, Ian! Can you explain what caused the issue?\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261115-1-292d2\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261115-1-292d2\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-ianjones-LeadForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-585771\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_c39dc658\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-16T06:51:00\", \"text\": \"Sure, @eid_3f4b2681. The root cause was a schema mismatch between the application layer and the database. Some fields were being cast to incorrect types during data insertion, which led to errors in our lead scoring algorithms.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261115-2-c6531\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261115-2-c6531\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-ianjones-LeadForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-585771\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_652e8cd0\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-16T06:53:00\", \"text\": \"Thanks for the explanation, Ian. How did you manage to fix it?\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261115-3-3c371\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261115-3-3c371\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-ianjones-LeadForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-585771\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_c39dc658\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-16T06:56:00\", \"text\": \"To resolve the issue, I updated the data insertion logic to ensure that the fields are cast to the correct types. Additionally, I modified the database schema to enforce stricter type constraints, preventing similar issues in the future.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261115-4-2a505\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261115-4-2a505\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-ianjones-LeadForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-585771\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_99835861\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-16T06:59:00\", \"text\": \"Nice work, @eid_c39dc658! This should help improve the accuracy of our lead prioritization.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261115-5-ad831\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261115-5-ad831\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-ianjones-LeadForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-585771\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_3f4b2681\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-16T07:03:00\", \"text\": \"Thanks for the quick turnaround, Ian. Let’s keep an eye on the lead scoring results to ensure everything is working as expected.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261115-6-8f847\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261115-6-8f847\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-ianjones-LeadForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-585771\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_c39dc658\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-16T07:05:00\", \"text\": \"Absolutely, Hannah. I'll monitor the results closely and report any anomalies. Thanks, everyone!\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261115-7-59f1f\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261115-7-59f1f\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-ianjones-LeadForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-585771\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_652e8cd0\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-17T15:57:00\", \"text\": \"Hi team, the bug about incorrect data import process has been resolved. You can check the details in the PR here: https://github.com/salesforce/LeadForce/pull/56.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261117-0-319f5\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261117-0-319f5\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-ianjones-LeadForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-585771\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_652e8cd0\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-17T15:58:00\", \"text\": \"The root cause was a mapping error in our data import script. It was assigning external data fields to the wrong database columns, which led to erroneous data entries and flawed lead qualification.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261117-1-40c40\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261117-1-40c40\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-ianjones-LeadForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-585771\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_652e8cd0\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-17T16:02:00\", \"text\": \"To fix this, I updated the mapping logic in the script to correctly align the external data fields with the appropriate database columns. I also added some unit tests to ensure this doesn't happen again.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261117-2-c1176\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261117-2-c1176\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-ianjones-LeadForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-585771\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_c39dc658\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-17T16:07:00\", \"text\": \"Great work, @eid_652e8cd0! Thanks for jumping on this so quickly.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261117-3-8500a\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261117-3-8500a\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-ianjones-LeadForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-585771\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_3f4b2681\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-17T16:08:00\", \"text\": \"Thanks, Bob! This should really help improve the accuracy of our lead data. I'll run some tests on my end to double-check everything.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261117-4-43cee\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261117-4-43cee\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-ianjones-LeadForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-585771\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_99835861\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-17T16:09:00\", \"text\": \"Nice job, Bob. Let me know if there's anything else you need from the QA side.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261117-5-a8ab3\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261117-5-a8ab3\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-ianjones-LeadForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-585771\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_652e8cd0\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-17T16:12:00\", \"text\": \"Thanks, Ian and Hannah. @eid_99835861, I'll keep you posted if anything comes up during further testing.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261117-6-b741f\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261117-6-b741f\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-ianjones-LeadForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-585771\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_9f4e2c6f\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-04T05:46:00\", \"text\": \"Hi team, the bug about incorrect export permissions has been resolved. You can check the details in the approved PR here: https://github.com/salesforce/LeadForce/pull/47.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261003-0-a2f3f\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261003-0-a2f3f\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-ianjones-LeadForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-585771\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_3f4b2681\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-04T05:48:00\", \"text\": \"Great news, Ian! Can you explain what caused the issue?\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261003-1-63e1e\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261003-1-63e1e\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-ianjones-LeadForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-585771\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_9f4e2c6f\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-04T05:53:00\", \"text\": \"Sure, Hannah. The root cause was a misconfiguration in the export module's permission settings. It was granting users excessive data access rights, allowing them to export more data than they were authorized to access.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261003-2-8c05b\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261003-2-8c05b\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-ianjones-LeadForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-585771\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_99835861\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-04T05:55:00\", \"text\": \"Thanks for the update, @eid_9f4e2c6f. How did you manage to fix it?\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261003-3-808cf\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261003-3-808cf\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-ianjones-LeadForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-585771\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_9f4e2c6f\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-04T05:56:00\", \"text\": \"I updated the permission settings in the export module to correctly map user roles to their respective data access levels. This ensures that users can only export data they are authorized to access. We also added additional checks to validate permissions before any export action is performed.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261003-4-02377\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261003-4-02377\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-ianjones-LeadForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-585771\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_3f4b2681\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-04T06:01:00\", \"text\": \"Sounds like a solid fix. Thanks for handling this so quickly, Ian!\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261003-5-d94e9\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261003-5-d94e9\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-ianjones-LeadForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-585771\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_99835861\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-04T06:06:00\", \"text\": \"Yes, thanks @eid_9f4e2c6f. I'll make sure to test it thoroughly to ensure everything is working as expected.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261003-6-b83f5\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261003-6-b83f5\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-ianjones-LeadForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-585771\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_9f4e2c6f\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-04T06:09:00\", \"text\": \"Thanks, Ian. Let me know if you encounter any issues during testing.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261003-7-ebf31\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261003-7-ebf31\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-ianjones-LeadForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-585771\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_3f4b2681\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-20T05:21:00\", \"text\": \"Hi team, the bug titled 'UI Lag Due to Excessive DOM Updates' has been resolved. You can check out the approved PR here: https://github.com/salesforce/LeadForce/pull/57.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261119-0-79e15\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261119-0-79e15\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-ianjones-LeadForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-585771\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_3f4b2681\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-20T05:25:00\", \"text\": \"The root cause was inefficient DOM manipulation during the import process, which led to performance bottlenecks and caused the UI to lag.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261119-1-13ba7\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261119-1-13ba7\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-ianjones-LeadForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-585771\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_3f4b2681\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-20T05:26:00\", \"text\": \"To fix this, I optimized the DOM updates by batching them together instead of updating the DOM on every single change. This reduces the number of reflows and repaints, significantly improving performance.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261119-2-f4bc0\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261119-2-f4bc0\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-ianjones-LeadForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-585771\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_c39dc658\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-20T05:29:00\", \"text\": \"Great work, @eid_3f4b2681! That should make a big difference for users during the import process.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261119-3-dbfbf\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261119-3-dbfbf\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-ianjones-LeadForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-585771\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_652e8cd0\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-20T05:30:00\", \"text\": \"Thanks, Hannah! This should really help with the user experience. I'll test it out and let you know if I spot anything.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261119-4-12e46\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261119-4-12e46\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-ianjones-LeadForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-585771\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_99835861\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-20T05:33:00\", \"text\": \"Nice job, Hannah. Batching DOM updates sounds like a smart move. Let me know if you need any help with further testing.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261119-5-69a7e\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"Th