 PR here: https://github.com/salesforce/SentimentForce/pull/49.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261221-0-5835d\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261221-0-5835d\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-emmamiller-SentimentForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-664c13\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_13cb0e90\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-12-21T13:19:00\", \"text\": \"Great news, Ian! What was causing the inconsistency?\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261221-1-0e5f5\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261221-1-0e5f5\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-emmamiller-SentimentForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-664c13\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_8658e19c\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-12-21T13:21:00\", \"text\": \"The root cause was that our sentiment analysis engine didn't account for channel-specific language nuances or context. This led to significant variations in sentiment scores for similar messages across different channels.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261221-2-72918\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261221-2-72918\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-emmamiller-SentimentForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-664c13\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_d96fb219\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-12-21T13:24:00\", \"text\": \"Thanks for the update, Ian. How did you manage to fix it?\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261221-3-3e131\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261221-3-3e131\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-emmamiller-SentimentForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-664c13\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_8658e19c\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-12-21T13:26:00\", \"text\": \"To address the issue, I implemented a context-aware layer in the sentiment analysis engine. This layer now considers channel-specific language patterns and adjusts the sentiment scoring accordingly. This should ensure more consistent results across different channels.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261221-4-123a6\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261221-4-123a6\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-emmamiller-SentimentForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-664c13\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_13cb0e90\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-12-21T13:29:00\", \"text\": \"That sounds like a solid solution, Ian. Thanks for tackling this so quickly!\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261221-5-00928\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261221-5-00928\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-emmamiller-SentimentForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-664c13\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_d96fb219\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-12-21T13:32:00\", \"text\": \"Yes, thanks @eid_8658e19c! I'll keep an eye on the sentiment reports to ensure everything is working as expected.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261221-6-07f4e\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261221-6-07f4e\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-emmamiller-SentimentForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-664c13\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_8658e19c\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-12-21T13:36:00\", \"text\": \"No problem, happy to help! Let me know if you notice any other issues.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261221-7-64aef\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261221-7-64aef\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-emmamiller-SentimentForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-664c13\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_8658e19c\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-12-25T00:54:00\", \"text\": \"Hi team, the bug titled 'Suboptimal Data Caching Strategy' has been resolved. You can check out the details in the approved PR here: https://github.com/salesforce/SentimentForce/pull/50.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261224-0-3c8cb\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261224-0-3c8cb\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-emmamiller-SentimentForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-664c13\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_8658e19c\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-12-25T00:57:00\", \"text\": \"The root cause was an inadequate cache size and improper cache invalidation policies, which led to frequent cache misses and increased database load for sentiment data queries.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261224-1-b7d89\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261224-1-b7d89\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-emmamiller-SentimentForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-664c13\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_8658e19c\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-12-25T00:58:00\", \"text\": \"To fix this, I increased the cache size and implemented a more efficient cache invalidation strategy. This should significantly reduce the number of cache misses and alleviate the database load.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261224-2-62b27\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261224-2-62b27\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-emmamiller-SentimentForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-664c13\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_13cb0e90\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-12-25T01:01:00\", \"text\": \"Great work, Ian! Thanks for addressing this so quickly. The new caching strategy should help improve our system's performance.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261224-3-ab5fb\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261224-3-ab5fb\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-emmamiller-SentimentForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-664c13\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_d96fb219\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-12-25T01:05:00\", \"text\": \"Thanks, @eid_8658e19c! I'll monitor the database load over the next few days to ensure everything is running smoothly.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261224-4-0cb86\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261224-4-0cb86\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-emmamiller-SentimentForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-664c13\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_8658e19c\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-12-25T01:06:00\", \"text\": \"Thanks, @eid_d96fb219. Let me know if you notice any issues. I'm here to help.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261224-5-297b0\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261224-5-297b0\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-emmamiller-SentimentForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-664c13\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_13cb0e90\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-12-25T01:11:00\", \"text\": \"Thanks again, Ian. This should make a big difference for our users. Let's keep an eye on the metrics and see how it performs.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261224-6-bee21\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261224-6-bee21\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-emmamiller-SentimentForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-664c13\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_d96fb219\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-09T11:13:00\", \"text\": \"Hi team, I've found some interesting open-source bugs that mirror the issues we're tackling. Let's take a look and see what we can learn! 😊\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261109-0-f83af\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261109-0-f83af\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-emmamiller-SentimentForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-664c13\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_d96fb219\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-09T11:17:00\", \"text\": \"First up, we have a bug in PostgreSQL titled 'Data Fragmentation in Indexes'. It deals with high levels of index fragmentation leading to slow query performance, especially for users with large datasets. Here's the PR link: https://github.com/postgres/postgres/pull/175. @eid_13cb0e90, this seems similar to our data fragmentation issue. Thoughts?\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261109-1-81a4c\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261109-1-81a4c\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-emmamiller-SentimentForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-664c13\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_13cb0e90\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-09T11:22:00\", \"text\": \"Thanks, Emma! This is definitely relevant. The approach they took to optimize index usage could be insightful for our database management system. I'll dive into their solution and see how we can apply it. 🚀\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261109-2-92f42\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261109-2-92f42\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-emmamiller-SentimentForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-664c13\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_d96fb219\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-09T11:25:00\", \"text\": \"Great, Julia! Next, there's a Kubernetes issue titled 'API Rate Limiting Misconfiguration'. It describes excessive rate limiting on the API server, causing delays in pod scaling operations. Here's the PR: https://github.com/kubernetes/kubernetes/pull/176. Ian, this sounds a lot like our API rate limiting problem. What do you think?\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261109-3-f74c0\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261109-3-f74c0\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-emmamiller-SentimentForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-664c13\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_8658e19c\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-09T11:29:00\", \"text\": \"Absolutely, Emma! The Kubernetes team's approach to adjusting rate limits could help us refine our own settings. I'll review their changes and see how we can adapt them for our backend server. 💪\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261109-4-48c0f\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261109-4-48c0f\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-emmamiller-SentimentForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-664c13\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_d96fb219\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-09T11:33:00\", \"text\": \"Awesome, Ian! Lastly, there's an OAuth2 Proxy issue titled 'OAuth Token Validation Flaw'. It involves a misconfiguration in token validation that allows unauthorized access to protected resources. Check out the PR here: https://github.com/oauth2-proxy/oauth2-proxy/pull/177. Fiona, this seems directly related to our OAuth misimplementation. Any insights?\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261109-5-91ea1\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261109-5-91ea1\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-emmamiller-SentimentForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-664c13\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_fa6ec727\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-09T11:37:00\", \"text\": \"Thanks, Emma! This is spot on. The way they addressed token validation flaws could be crucial for us. I'll analyze their fix and ensure our OAuth implementation is secure. 🔒\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261109-6-06cb5\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261109-6-06cb5\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-emmamiller-SentimentForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-664c13\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_d96fb219\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-09T11:41:00\", \"text\": \"Thanks, everyone! Let's keep these open-source solutions in mind as we work through our issues. Feel free to reach out if you need any more resources or support. 🙌\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261109-7-12546\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261109-7-12546\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-emmamiller-SentimentForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-664c13\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_13cb0e90\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-09T11:43:00\", \"text\": \"Will do! Thanks for bringing these to our attention, Emma. 😊\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261109-8-1b3ec\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261109-8-1b3ec\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-emmamiller-SentimentForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-664c13\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_8658e19c\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-09T11:45:00\", \"text\": \"Thanks, team! Let's leverage these insights to enhance our solutions. 🚀\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261109-9-f10fd\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261109-9-f10fd\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-emmamiller-SentimentForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-664c13\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_fa6ec727\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-09T11:48:00\", \"text\": \"On it! Appreciate the guidance, Emma. 👍\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261109-10-fd917\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261109-10-fd917\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-emmamiller-SentimentForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-664c13\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_13cb0e90\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-14T03:55:00\", \"text\": \"Hi team, the bug titled 'Data Fragmentation Issues' has been resolved. You can check the details in the approved PR here: https://github.com/salesforce/SentimentForce/pull/44.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261113-0-44007\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261113-0-44007\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-emmamiller-SentimentForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-664c13\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_13cb0e90\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-14T04:00:00\", \"text\": \"The root cause was frequent updates and deletions in our database tables without regular defragmentation, which led to fragmented data storage and increased I/O operations.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261113-1-20be0\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261113-1-20be0\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-emmamiller-SentimentForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-664c13\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_13cb0e90\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-14T04:01:00\", \"text\": \"To fix this, I implemented a scheduled defragmentation process that runs during off-peak hours. This should help maintain optimal data retrieval speeds by reducing fragmentation.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261113-2-05847\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261113-2-05847\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-emmamiller-SentimentForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-664c13\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_fa6ec727\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-14T04:06:00\", \"text\": \"Great work, @eid_13cb0e90! Thanks for addressing this so quickly. The scheduled defragmentation sounds like a solid solution.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261113-3-22814\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261113-3-22814\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-emmamiller-SentimentForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-664c13\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_d96fb219\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-14T04:08:00\", \"text\": \"Thanks, Julia! This should really help with the performance issues we've been seeing. I'll monitor the retrieval speeds over the next few days.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261113-4-26bf0\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261113-4-26bf0\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-emmamiller-SentimentForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-664c13\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_8658e19c\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-14T04:09:00\", \"text\": \"Awesome job, Julia Davis! Let me know if you need any help with further testing or monitoring.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261113-5-25fb6\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261113-5-25fb6\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-emmamiller-SentimentForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-664c13\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_13cb0e90\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-14T04:14:00\", \"text\": \"Thanks, everyone! @eid_d96fb219, please keep me posted on the performance metrics. @eid_8658e19c, I'll reach out if we need additional testing. Appreciate the support!\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261113-6-1853f\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261113-6-1853f\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-emmamiller-SentimentForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-664c13\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_d96fb219\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-12-16T20:47:00\", \"text\": \"Hi team, I found some interesting open-source bugs that might help us with our current issues. Let's take a look at them! 😊\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261216-0-15ecf\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261216-0-15ecf\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-emmamiller-SentimentForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-664c13\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_d96fb219\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-12-16T20:48:00\", \"text\": \"First up, we have a bug in Django related to 'Timezone Misalignment in DateTimeField'. This is similar to our timezone issue in SentimentForce. You can check out the PR here: https://github.com/django/django/pull/187. Julia, any thoughts on this?\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261216-1-ee216\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261216-1-ee216\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-emmamiller-SentimentForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-664c13\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_13cb0e90\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-12-16T20:52:00\", \"text\": \"Thanks, Emma! This looks quite similar to what we're facing. I'll review the PR to see how they handled the timezone logic. It might give us some insights for our API Integration Module. 👍\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261216-2-c6e8f\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261216-2-c6e8f\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-emmamiller-SentimentForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-664c13\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_d96fb219\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-12-16T20:53:00\", \"text\": \"Great, thanks Julia! Next, there's a Redis bug titled 'Inefficient Cache Eviction Policy'. This is quite similar to our caching strategy issue. Here's the PR link: https://github.com/redis/redis/pull/188. Ian, what do you think?\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261216-3-813c4\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261216-3-813c4\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-emmamiller-SentimentForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-664c13\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_8658e19c\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-12-16T20:55:00\", \"text\": \"This is spot on, Emma! I'll dive into the Redis PR to understand their approach to optimizing cache eviction. It could be really helpful for improving our sentiment reports' response times. 🚀\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261216-4-07af9\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261216-4-07af9\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-emmamiller-SentimentForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-664c13\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_d96fb219\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-12-16T20:59:00\", \"text\": \"Awesome, Ian! Lastly, there's a TensorFlow bug about 'Inconsistent Model Predictions Across Devices'. This reminds me of our sentiment scoring inconsistency. Check it out here: https://github.com/tensorflow/tensorflow/pull/189. Ian, since you're already on the sentiment scoring issue, could you take a look at this one too?\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261216-5-01b57\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261216-5-01b57\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-emmamiller-SentimentForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-664c13\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_8658e19c\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-12-16T21:01:00\", \"text\": \"Sure thing, Emma! I'll review the TensorFlow PR to see how they tackled prediction variability. It might offer some clues for ensuring consistent sentiment scoring across channels. 💪\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261216-6-05d39\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261216-6-05d39\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-emmamiller-SentimentForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-664c13\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_d96fb219\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-12-16T21:03:00\", \"text\": \"Thanks, Ian! Let's keep these references in mind as we work on our issues. Feel free to reach out if you need any more info or run into any roadblocks. Let's get these resolved for our customers! 🙌\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261216-7-cfc9a\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261216-7-cfc9a\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-emmamiller-SentimentForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-664c13\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_13cb0e90\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-12-16T21:05:00\", \"text\": \"Will do, thanks for the resources, Emma! 😊\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261216-8-4b4db\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261216-8-4b4db\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-emmamiller-SentimentForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-664c13\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_8658e19c\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-12-16T21:07:00\", \"text\": \"Thanks, Emma! I'll keep you posted on any progress or insights. 🛠️\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261216-9-a9c02\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261216-9-a9c02\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-emmamiller-SentimentForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-664c13\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_8658e19c\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-29T12:11:00\", \"text\": \"Hi team, the bug about incorrect OAuth token handling has been resolved. You can check the details in the PR here: https://github.com/salesforce/SentimentForce/pull/47.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261129-0-8ac30\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261129-0-8ac30\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-emmamiller-SentimentForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-664c13\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_8658e19c\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-29T12:12:00\", \"text\": \"To recap, the issue was that our API Integration Module wasn't refreshing expired OAuth tokens automatically. This led to unauthorized API requests and interruptions in data retrieval from Slack channels.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261129-1-40bc9\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261129-1-40bc9\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-emmamiller-SentimentForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-664c13\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_fa6ec727\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-29T12:14:00\", \"text\": \"Thanks for the update, Ian! What was causing the token refresh mechanism to fail?\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261129-2-121e7\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261129-2-121e7\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-emmamiller-SentimentForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-664c13\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_8658e19c\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-29T12:18:00\", \"text\": \"Good question, @eid_fa6ec727. The root cause was a missing trigger in our token management logic. The system wasn't set up to initiate a refresh when a token expired.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261129-3-561d3\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261129-3-561d3\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-emmamiller-SentimentForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-664c13\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_d96fb219\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-29T12:19:00\", \"text\": \"How did you manage to fix it, Ian?\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261129-4-07641\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261129-4-07641\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-emmamiller-SentimentForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-664c13\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_8658e19c\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-29T12:23:00\", \"text\": \"I added a check for token expiration before each API request. If a token is expired, the system now automatically triggers a refresh and retries the request with the new token. This ensures uninterrupted data retrieval.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261129-5-f54dc\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261129-5-f54dc\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-emmamiller-SentimentForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-664c13\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_fa6ec727\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-29T12:28:00\", \"text\": \"That sounds like a solid fix. Thanks for handling this so quickly, Ian!\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261129-6-8fc36\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261129-6-8fc36\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-emmamiller-SentimentForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-664c13\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_d96fb219\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-29T12:30:00\", \"text\": \"Agreed, great work! I'll keep an eye on the logs to ensure everything runs smoothly.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261129-7-fc6d8\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261129-7-fc6d8\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-emmamiller-SentimentForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-664c13\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_8658e19c\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-29T12:35:00\", \"text\": \"Thanks, @eid_d96fb219 and Fiona. Let me know if you notice any issues. I'll be monitoring the system as well.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261129-8-5fb62\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261129-8-5fb62\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-emmamiller-SentimentForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-664c13\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_d96fb219\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-12-01T23:29:00\", \"text\": \"Hi team, several customers are reporting issues with SentimentForce that we need to address ASAP. Let's go through them one by one. 🚀\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261201-0-6fd9c\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261201-0-6fd9c\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-emmamiller-SentimentForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-664c13\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_d96fb219\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-12-01T23:30:00\", \"text\": \"First up, we have a 'Slack API Integration Failure'. The integration with Slack's API is intermittently failing, causing gaps in the sentiment data on the dashboard. This affects the Real-Time Dashboard & Backend Server, impacting customer CUST-0087. @eid_fa6ec727, this one's for you.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261201-1-dca04\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261201-1-dca04\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-emmamiller-SentimentForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-664c13\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_fa6ec727\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-12-01T23:35:00\", \"text\": \"Got it! I'll start investigating the API integration issues right away. Thanks for the heads-up! 👍\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261201-2-1486b\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261201-2-1486b\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-emmamiller-SentimentForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-664c13\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_d96fb219\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-12-01T23:38:00\", \"text\": \"Great, thanks! Next, we have 'Delayed Sentiment Updates in Real-Time Dashboard'. The dashboard is experiencing delays in updating sentiment scores, which affects the same areas as the previous issue. This impacts customer CUST-0105. @eid_8658e19c, can you take this one?\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261201-3-36b87\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261201-3-36b87\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-emmamiller-SentimentForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-664c13\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_8658e19c\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-12-01T23:41:00\", \"text\": \"Sure thing! I'll look into the delays and see what's causing the lag. Let's get this sorted for CUST-0105. 💪\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261201-4-e115b\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261201-4-e115b\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-emmamiller-SentimentForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-664c13\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_d96fb219\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-12-01T23:46:00\", \"text\": \"Awesome, thanks! Lastly, we have a 'Language Model Bias' issue. The sentiment analysis engine is showing bias towards certain phrases, which is skewing sentiment scores. This affects the Sentiment Analysis Engine and impacts customer CUST-0005. @eid_4df5d4b7, can you handle this?\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261201-5-e2aaf\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261201-5-e2aaf\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-emmamiller-SentimentForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-664c13\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_4df5d4b7\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-12-01T23:47:00\", \"text\": \"Absolutely, I'll dive into the sentiment analysis engine and address the bias issue. We need to ensure accurate sentiment reports for our users. 🔍\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261201-6-baf95\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261201-6-baf95\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-emmamiller-SentimentForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-664c13\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_d96fb219\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-12-01T23:48:00\", \"text\": \"Thanks, everyone! Let's keep communication open and update each other on progress. Feel free to ask questions or share insights as you work through these. 🙌\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261201-7-bd055\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261201-7-bd055\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-emmamiller-SentimentForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-664c13\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_fa6ec727\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-12-01T23:52:00\", \"text\": \"Will do! If anyone has insights on the API integration, let me know. 🤔\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261201-8-c31d5\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261201-8-c31d5\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-emmamiller-SentimentForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-664c13\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_8658e19c\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-12-01T23:53:00\", \"text\": \"Same here, any tips on optimizing real-time updates are welcome! 🚀\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261201-9-f759f\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261201-9-f759f\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-emmamiller-SentimentForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-664c13\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_4df5d4b7\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-12-01T23:56:00\", \"text\": \"I'll reach out if I find any patterns in the bias issue. Let's get these fixed! 💪\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261201-10-d526f\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261201-10-d526f\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-emmamiller-SentimentForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-664c13\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_d96fb219\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-12-05T10:05:00\", \"text\": \"Hi team, I've found some interesting open-source bugs that might help us with our current issues. Let's take a look and see what we can learn! 🚀\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261205-0-59ced\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261205-0-59ced\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-emmamiller-SentimentForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-664c13\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_d96fb219\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-12-05T10:07:00\", \"text\": \"First up, we have a 'Slack API Integration Failure' in the Mattermost project. They're experiencing intermittent failures in Slack API integration, causing message sync issues. Here's the PR link: https://github.com/mattermost/mattermost-server/pull/183. @eid_fa6ec727, this sounds similar to what you're working on, right?\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261205-1-56b81\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261205-1-56b81\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-emmamiller-SentimentForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-664c13\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_fa6ec727\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-12-05T10:08:00\", \"text\": \"Absolutely, Emma! This is quite similar to our Slack API issue. I'll review their PR to see if there are any insights or solutions we can apply. Thanks for sharing! 👍\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261205-2-a0da5\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261205-2-a0da5\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-emmamiller-SentimentForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-664c13\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_d96fb219\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-12-05T10:09:00\", \"text\": \"Great! Next, we have a 'Delayed Dashboard Updates' issue in Grafana. Their dashboard panels are experiencing delays in updating metrics, which impacts real-time data visualization. Check out the PR here: https://github.com/grafana/grafana/pull/184. Ian, this might be relevant to your current task.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261205-3-dc9e7\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261205-3-dc9e7\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-emmamiller-SentimentForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-664c13\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_8658e19c\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-12-05T10:11:00\", \"text\": \"Thanks, Emma! This is definitely relevant. I'll dive into their PR and see if there are any optimization techniques we can leverage for our real-time dashboard. 🚀\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261205-4-3e186\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261205-4-3e186\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-emmamiller-SentimentForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-664c13\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_d96fb219\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-12-05T10:12:00\", \"text\": \"Awesome! Lastly, there's a 'Language Model Bias in Sentiment Analysis' issue in the Hugging Face Transformers project. They're dealing with biased sentiment analysis, similar to our bias issue. Here's the PR: https://github.com/huggingface/transformers/pull/185. Bob, this seems right up your alley.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261205-5-42e36\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261205-5-42e36\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-emmamiller-SentimentForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-664c13\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_4df5d4b7\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-12-05T10:13:00\", \"text\": \"Thanks, Emma! I'll take a look at their approach to handling bias. It might give us some ideas on how to improve our sentiment analysis engine. 🔍\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261205-6-7ea76\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261205-6-7ea76\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-emmamiller-SentimentForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-664c13\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_d96fb219\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-12-05T10:18:00\", \"text\": \"Thanks, everyone! Let's keep these open-source projects in mind as we work through our issues. Feel free to share any insights or solutions you find. 🙌\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261205-7-3a992\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261205-7-3a992\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-emmamiller-SentimentForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-664c13\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_fa6ec727\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-12-05T10:21:00\", \"text\": \"Will do! If anyone else finds something useful, let me know. 🤔\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261205-8-3c904\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261205-8-3c904\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-emmamiller-SentimentForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-664c13\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_8658e19c\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-12-05T10:26:00\", \"text\": \"Same here, any tips on optimizing real-time updates are welcome! 🚀\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261205-9-df5fd\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261205-9-df5fd\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-emmamiller-SentimentForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-664c13\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_4df5d4b7\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-12-05T10:30:00\", \"text\": \"I'll reach out if I find any patterns in the bias issue. Let's get these fixed! 💪\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261205-10-fb9c3\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261205-10-fb9c3\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-emmamiller-SentimentForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-664c13\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_8658e19c\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-13T00:44:00\", \"text\": \"Hi team, I looked into the reported issue about the weak password policy enforcement. The concern was that our system allows users to set weak passwords, potentially making it easier for brute force attacks.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260912-0-ed551\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260912-0-ed551\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-emmamiller-SentimentForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-664c13\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_8658e19c\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-13T00:49:00\", \"text\": \"After reviewing the system configuration and policies, I found that this is actually expected behavior. Our current setup is designed to allow flexibility for users who prefer simpler passwords, as long as they are aware of the risks.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260912-1-6129b\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260912-1-6129b\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-emmamiller-SentimentForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-664c13\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_4df5d4b7\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-13T00:54:00\", \"text\": \"Thanks for the update, Ian. So, there's no need for a fix because it's a user choice issue?\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260912-2-1ca49\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260912-2-1ca49\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-emmamiller-SentimentForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-664c13\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_8658e19c\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-13T00:59:00\", \"text\": \"Exactly, Bob. We provide users with the option to set stronger passwords, and we also have additional security measures in place, like two-factor authentication, to mitigate potential risks.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260912-3-279e6\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260912-3-279e6\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-emmamiller-SentimentForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-664c13\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_13cb0e90\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-13T01:01:00\", \"text\": \"That makes sense. Did you check if there were any misconfigurations that might have led to this report?\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260912-4-20c25\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260912-4-20c25\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-emmamiller-SentimentForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-664c13\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_8658e19c\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-13T01:03:00\", \"text\": \"Yes, Julia. I verified the configurations and everything is set up as intended. The report seems to stem from a misunderstanding of our policy flexibility rather than a technical issue.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260912-5-ae0da\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260912-5-ae0da\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-emmamiller-SentimentForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-664c13\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_d96fb219\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-13T01:08:00\", \"text\": \"Good to know, Ian. Should we consider updating our documentation to make this clearer to users?\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260912-6-e2dfd\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260912-6-e2dfd\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-emmamiller-SentimentForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-664c13\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_8658e19c\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-13T01:13:00\", \"text\": \"That's a great idea, Emma. I'll coordinate with the documentation team to ensure our password policy and security measures are clearly communicated to users.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260912-7-68edb\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260912-7-68edb\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-emmamiller-SentimentForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-664c13\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_4df5d4b7\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-13T01:18:00\", \"text\": \"Thanks, Ian. Appreciate the thorough review and follow-up on this.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260912-8-8dbb9\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260912-8-8dbb9\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-emmamiller-SentimentForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-664c13\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_8658e19c\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-13T01:20:00\", \"text\": \"No problem, Bob. If anyone has further questions or concerns, feel free to reach out!\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260912-9-a5680\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260912-9-a5680\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-emmamiller-SentimentForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-664c13\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_d96fb219\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-14T09:28:00\", \"text\": \"Hi team, several customers are reporting issues with SentimentForce that we need to address. Let's go through them one by one. 😊\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260914-0-af559\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260914-0-af559\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-emmamiller-SentimentForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-664c13\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_d96fb219\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-14T09:29:00\", \"text\": \"First up, we have a 'Database Locking Causes System Slowdown' issue. This is affecting our Database Management System, causing slow response times for users like CUST-0105. @eid_4df5d4b7, this one's for you. Can you take a look?\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260914-1-6e533\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260914-1-6e533\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-emmamiller-SentimentForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-664c13\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_4df5d4b7\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-14T09:30:00\", \"text\": \"Got it, @eid_d96fb219! I'll dive into the database locking issue and see what's causing the slowdown. Thanks for the heads-up! 🚀\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260914-2-31445\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260914-2-31445\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-emmamiller-SentimentForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-664c13\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_d96fb219\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-14T09:34:00\", \"text\": \"Great, thanks! Next, we have a 'Real-Time Processing Lag' in the Sentiment Analysis Engine. This is causing delays in processing real-time Slack messages, impacting leaders like CUST-0087. @eid_92294e45, can you handle this one?\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260914-3-99fbb\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260914-3-99fbb\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-emmamiller-SentimentForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-664c13\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_92294e45\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-14T09:35:00\", \"text\": \"Sure thing, I'll check out the real-time processing lag and work on getting those sentiment reports back up to speed. 👍\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260914-4-81809\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260914-4-81809\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-emmamiller-SentimentForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-664c13\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_d96fb219\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-14T09:37:00\", \"text\": \"Awesome, thanks @eid_92294e45! Lastly, there's a 'Malformed JSON Response Parsing' issue in the API Integration Module. This is leading to dropped messages for users like CUST-0012. @eid_4df5d4b7, can you also take this one?\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260914-5-31034\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260914-5-31034\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-emmamiller-SentimentForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-664c13\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_4df5d4b7\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-14T09:40:00\", \"text\": \"No problem, I'll tackle the JSON parsing issue too. Let's make sure our data is complete and accurate! 💪\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260914-6-70929\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260914-6-70929\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-emmamiller-SentimentForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-664c13\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_d96fb219\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-14T09:42:00\", \"text\": \"Thanks, everyone! Let me know if you need any more details or support. Let's get these issues resolved for our customers! 🙌\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260914-7-20d25\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260914-7-20d25\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-emmamiller-SentimentForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-664c13\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_92294e45\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-14T09:43:00\", \"text\": \"Will do, thanks for coordinating, @eid_d96fb219! 😊\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260914-8-fc877\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260914-8-fc877\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-emmamiller-SentimentForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-664c13\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_4df5d4b7\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-14T09:47:00\", \"text\": \"Thanks, team! Let's keep our customers happy! 🚀\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260914-9-e55c8\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260914-9-e55c8\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-emmamiller-SentimentForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-664c13\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_d96fb219\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-17T18:02:00\", \"text\": \"Hi team, I've found some interesting open-source projects that have tackled issues similar to the ones we're facing. Let's take a look and see if we can draw any insights! 😊\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260917-0-7e5a3\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260917-0-7e5a3\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-emmamiller-SentimentForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-664c13\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_d96fb219\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-17T18:03:00\", \"text\": \"First up, we have a PostgreSQL issue titled 'Database Locking Causes System Slowdown'. It deals with heavy locking during concurrent transactions, leading to performance degradation. Here's the PR link: https://github.com/postgres/postgres/pull/159. @eid_4df5d4b7, this seems quite similar to the database locking issue you're working on. Thoughts?\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260917-1-30cfc\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260917-1-30cfc\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-emmamiller-SentimentForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-664c13\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_4df5d4b7\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-17T18:08:00\", \"text\": \"Thanks, Emma! This is definitely relevant. The PostgreSQL team has some interesting approaches to managing locks that we might be able to adapt. I'll dive into their PR and see what we can learn. 🚀\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260917-2-8883b\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260917-2-8883b\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-emmamiller-SentimentForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-664c13\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_d96fb219\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-17T18:12:00\", \"text\": \"Great, Bob! Next, there's an Apache Kafka issue titled 'Real-Time Processing Lag'. It describes delays in message processing under high throughput conditions, which sounds a lot like our real-time processing lag. Check out the PR here: https://github.com/apache/kafka/pull/160. Hannah, could you take a look at this one?\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260917-3-93677\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260917-3-93677\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-emmamiller-SentimentForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-664c13\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_92294e45\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-17T18:13:00\", \"text\": \"Sure thing, Emma! The Kafka team's approach to handling high throughput might give us some ideas on optimizing our sentiment analysis engine. I'll review their PR and see what strategies we can apply. 👍\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260917-4-a45eb\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260917-4-a45eb\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-emmamiller-SentimentForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-664c13\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_d96fb219\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-17T18:15:00\", \"text\": \"Awesome, thanks Hannah! Lastly, there's a Django REST Framework issue titled 'Malformed JSON Response Parsing'. It involves incorrect handling of malformed JSON responses, leading to dropped API requests. Here's the PR link: https://github.com/encode/django-rest-framework/pull/161. Bob, since you're already on the JSON parsing issue, could you also check this out?\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260917-5-9a47e\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260917-5-9a47e\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-emmamiller-SentimentForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-664c13\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_4df5d4b7\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-17T18:19:00\", \"text\": \"Absolutely, Emma! The Django REST Framework's handling of JSON parsing could provide some valuable insights. I'll compare their solution with our current approach and see if we can improve our API integration module. 💪\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260917-6-273fa\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260917-6-273fa\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-emmamiller-SentimentForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-664c13\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_d96fb219\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-17T18:21:00\", \"text\": \"Thanks, Bob! Let's keep these insights in mind as we work on resolving our issues. Let me know if you need any more details or support. Let's get these bugs squashed for our customers! 🙌\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260917-7-d2836\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260917-7-d2836\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-emmamiller-SentimentForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-664c13\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_92294e45\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-17T18:26:00\", \"text\": \"Will do, thanks for coordinating, Emma! 😊\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260917-8-29569\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260917-8-29569\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-emmamiller-SentimentForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-664c13\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_4df5d4b7\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-17T18:31:00\", \"text\": \"Thanks, team! Let's keep our customers happy! 🚀\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260917-9-8adec\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260917-9-8adec\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-emmamiller-SentimentForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-664c13\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_4df5d4b7\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-22T10:09:00\", \"text\": \"Hi team, I looked into the reported issue about the 'Malformed JSON Response Parsing'.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260921-0-c43da\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260921-0-c43da\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-emmamiller-SentimentForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-664c13\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_4df5d4b7\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-22T10:12:00\", \"text\": \"The system was encountering errors when parsing JSON responses from Slack, which was leading to dropped messages and incomplete sentiment data.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260921-1-c727b\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260921-1-c727b\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-emmamiller-SentimentForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-664c13\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_4df5d4b7\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-22T10:15:00\", \"text\": \"After reviewing the issue, I've determined that it does not require a fix.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260921-2-72c6a\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260921-2-72c6a\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-emmamiller-SentimentForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-664c13\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_92294e45\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-22T10:16:00\", \"text\": \"Hey Bob, could you explain why it's not a bug?\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260921-3-cf27f\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260921-3-cf27f\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-emmamiller-SentimentForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-664c13\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_4df5d4b7\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-22T10:20:00\", \"text\": \"Sure, @eid_92294e45. The JSON parser is actually functioning as expected. The errors were due to malformed JSON responses that were not compliant with Slack's API documentation.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260921-4-e84f1\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260921-4-e84f1\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-emmamiller-SentimentForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-664c13\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_4df5d4b7\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-22T10:23:00\", \"text\": \"These malformed responses are rare and typically result from network issues or third-party integrations sending unexpected data.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260921-5-012cb\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260921-5-012cb\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-emmamiller-SentimentForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-664c13\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_d96fb219\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-22T10:26:00\", \"text\": \"So, it's more of a data integrity issue rather than a bug in our system?\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260921-6-bdb18\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260921-6-bdb18\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-emmamiller-SentimentForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-664c13\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_4df5d4b7\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-22T10:27:00\", \"text\": \"Exactly, Emma. Our system is designed to handle well-formed JSON as per the API specs. Handling every possible malformed structure would be inefficient and unnecessary.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260921-7-325fc\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260921-7-325fc\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-emmamiller-SentimentForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-664c13\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_92294e45\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-22T10:31:00\", \"text\": \"Thanks for clarifying, Bob. Did you take any action to verify this?\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260921-8-6f7e7\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260921-8-6f7e7\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-emmamiller-SentimentForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-664c13\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_4df5d4b7\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-22T10:34:00\", \"text\": \"Yes, I reviewed the logs and tested with both valid and intentionally malformed JSON. The system processed valid JSON correctly and only failed on malformed data, which is expected.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260921-9-3c2d0\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260921-9-3c2d0\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-emmamiller-SentimentForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-664c13\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_d96fb219\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-22T10:37:00\", \"text\": \"Got it. Thanks for the thorough investigation, Bob.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260921-10-949ce\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260921-10-949ce\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-emmamiller-SentimentForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-664c13\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_4df5d4b7\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-09-22T10:41:00\", \"text\": \"No problem, happy to help! If any further issues arise, feel free to reach out.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260921-11-8b26d\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260921-11-8b26d\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-emmamiller-SentimentForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-664c13\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_d96fb219\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-20T07:48:00\", \"text\": \"Hi team, several customers are reporting issues with SentimentForce that we need to address. Let's go through them one by one. 😊\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261119-0-6377e\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261119-0-6377e\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-emmamiller-SentimentForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-664c13\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_d96fb219\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-20T07:51:00\", \"text\": \"First up, we have an issue titled 'API Rate Limiting Causes Data Fetch Failures'. This is affecting the API Integration Module and causing gaps in sentiment analysis data for CUST-0014. @eid_8658e19c, this one's for you. Can you take a look?\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261119-1-a9849\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"