terranceID\": \"20261105-1-ec0a7\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261105-1-ec0a7\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-davidmiller-AutoTuneForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-cca2c2\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_b67edbb4\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-06T00:10:00\", \"text\": \"Hi team, several customers are reporting issues with AutoTuneForce that we need to address. Let's go through them one by one. 😊\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261105-0-5a93b\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261105-0-5a93b\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-davidmiller-AutoTuneForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-cca2c2\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_b67edbb4\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-06T00:11:00\", \"text\": \"First up, we have an issue titled 'Incorrect Model Version Logging'. The logs are recording incorrect model version numbers, which is causing problems for users trying to audit model training processes. This affects the Database Logging System and is impacting customer CUST-0003. @eid_9307fe85, this one's for you.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261105-1-ca841\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261105-1-ca841\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-davidmiller-AutoTuneForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-cca2c2\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_9307fe85\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-06T00:15:00\", \"text\": \"Got it! I'll start looking into the logging system to identify the root cause. Thanks for the heads-up! 👍\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261105-2-87354\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261105-2-87354\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-davidmiller-AutoTuneForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-cca2c2\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_b67edbb4\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-06T00:16:00\", \"text\": \"Great, thanks! Next, we have 'Error Messages Obscuring Controls'. Error messages are blocking critical UI controls, which is preventing users from accessing necessary functions. This is impacting the User Interface and customer CUST-0115. @eid_67f8a879, can you take this one?\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261105-3-ae0c1\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261105-3-ae0c1\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-davidmiller-AutoTuneForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-cca2c2\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_67f8a879\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-06T00:19:00\", \"text\": \"Sure thing! I'll check the UI components and see how we can reposition those error messages. Let's make sure our users can interact with the system smoothly. 🚀\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261105-4-f118a\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261105-4-f118a\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-davidmiller-AutoTuneForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-cca2c2\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_b67edbb4\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-06T00:20:00\", \"text\": \"Awesome, thanks! Lastly, we have 'Graphical Artifacts in Parameter Charts'. Users are seeing graphical artifacts in parameter charts, which is affecting their ability to interpret model performance. This is also impacting the User Interface and customer CUST-0012. @eid_9307fe85, could you handle this one as well?\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261105-5-8da9a\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261105-5-8da9a\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-davidmiller-AutoTuneForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-cca2c2\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_9307fe85\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-06T00:23:00\", \"text\": \"Absolutely, I'll dive into the chart rendering issues and see what's causing those artifacts. Let's get this sorted out for our users! 💪\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261105-6-30aa7\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261105-6-30aa7\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-davidmiller-AutoTuneForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-cca2c2\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_b67edbb4\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-06T00:26:00\", \"text\": \"Thanks, everyone! If you need any more details or run into any roadblocks, feel free to reach out. Let's keep our customers happy! 😊\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261105-7-992ae\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261105-7-992ae\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-davidmiller-AutoTuneForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-cca2c2\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_67f8a879\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-06T00:30:00\", \"text\": \"Will do! Thanks for organizing everything. Let's get these issues fixed! 🔧\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261105-8-55d2a\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261105-8-55d2a\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-davidmiller-AutoTuneForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-cca2c2\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_9307fe85\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-06T00:34:00\", \"text\": \"Thanks, team! Let's make it happen! 🚀\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261105-9-d80dd\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261105-9-d80dd\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"planning-ATF_AIX\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-3a5e7c\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_6bd20afa\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-06-11T05:21:00\", \"text\": \"Hi team, I just wanted to kick off our discussion about the ATF_AIX product. Let's start by reviewing the documents from the last release. Here are the <https://sf-internal.slack.com/archives/docs/tuneprox_market_research_report_final|tuneprox_market_research_report_final> and <https://sf-internal.slack.com/archives/docs/latest_atf_aix_market_research_report|latest_atf_aix_market_research_report>.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260611-0-0d2b7\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260611-0-0d2b7\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"planning-ATF_AIX\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-3a5e7c\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_8c71a7a9\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-06-11T05:23:00\", \"text\": \"Thanks, Julia! I'll take a look at the market research reports. It's crucial to understand the market needs before we dive into any changes.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260611-1-a5186\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260611-1-a5186\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"planning-ATF_AIX\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-3a5e7c\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_5e3edafc\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-06-11T05:27:00\", \"text\": \"Agreed, @eid_8c71a7a9. I'll review the <https://sf-internal.slack.com/archives/docs/tuneprox_product_vision_document_final|tuneprox_product_vision_document_final> and <https://sf-internal.slack.com/archives/docs/latest_atf_aix_product_vision_document|latest_atf_aix_product_vision_document> to ensure we're aligned with the product's long-term goals.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260611-2-17368\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260611-2-17368\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"planning-ATF_AIX\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-3a5e7c\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_35e32fec\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-06-11T05:30:00\", \"text\": \"I'll focus on the <https://sf-internal.slack.com/archives/docs/tuneprox_product_requirements_document_final|tuneprox_product_requirements_document_final> and <https://sf-internal.slack.com/archives/docs/latest_atf_aix_product_requirements_document|latest_atf_aix_product_requirements_document>. We need to make sure all requirements are still relevant.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260611-3-eefba\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260611-3-eefba\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"planning-ATF_AIX\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-3a5e7c\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_19f537cf\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-06-11T05:34:00\", \"text\": \"I'll handle the technical side. Reviewing the <https://sf-internal.slack.com/archives/docs/tuneprox_technical_specifications_document_final|tuneprox_technical_specifications_document_final> and <https://sf-internal.slack.com/archives/docs/latest_atf_aix_technical_specifications_document|latest_atf_aix_technical_specifications_document> now.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260611-4-0dc7b\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260611-4-0dc7b\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"planning-ATF_AIX\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-3a5e7c\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_ea95d983\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-06-11T05:37:00\", \"text\": \"Great! I'll check out the <https://sf-internal.slack.com/archives/docs/tuneprox_system_design_document_final|tuneprox_system_design_document_final> and <https://sf-internal.slack.com/archives/docs/latest_atf_aix_system_design_document|latest_atf_aix_system_design_document> to understand the current system architecture.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260611-5-560a7\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260611-5-560a7\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"planning-ATF_AIX\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-3a5e7c\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_6f719d21\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-06-11T05:39:00\", \"text\": \"Once everyone has reviewed their documents, let's regroup and discuss any potential areas for improvement or updates.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260611-6-a55d6\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260611-6-a55d6\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"planning-ATF_AIX\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-3a5e7c\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_961f0487\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-06-11T05:42:00\", \"text\": \"Sounds good. I'll also keep an eye on any feedback or issues reported by customers and QA specialists. We should address those in our next steps.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260611-7-6d051\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260611-7-6d051\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"planning-ATF_AIX\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-3a5e7c\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_6bd20afa\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-06-11T05:44:00\", \"text\": \"Perfect, thanks everyone! Let's aim to reconvene tomorrow to share our insights and plan the next steps.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260611-8-e3ebc\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260611-8-e3ebc\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"planning-ATF_AIX\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-3a5e7c\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_19f537cf\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-06-11T07:17:00\", \"text\": \"@here here’s a quick video showcasing the updates in our last release https://sf-internal.slack.com/archives/TuneProX/demo_4\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260717-0-14582\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260717-0-14582\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"planning-ATF_AIX\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-3a5e7c\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"slack_admin_bot\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-06-12T08:55:00\", \"text\": \"@eid_7d27f1fd joined planning-ATF_AIX.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260612-12-72759\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260612-12-72759\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"planning-ATF_AIX\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-3a5e7c\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"slack_admin_bot\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-06-14T12:35:00\", \"text\": \"@eid_ad0725a2, @eid_2490c02c joined planning-ATF_AIX.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260614-13-24ffd\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260614-13-24ffd\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"planning-ATF_AIX\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-3a5e7c\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_ad0725a2\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-06-15T00:36:00\", \"text\": \"Hi team, one of the common issues reported for ATF_AIX is the limited integration with certain third-party data sources. This was reported by Customer ID: CUST-0003.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260613-0-7a323\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260613-0-7a323\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"planning-ATF_AIX\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-3a5e7c\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_8c71a7a9\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-06-15T00:41:00\", \"text\": \"Thanks for bringing this up, David. Since the product was developed by a different team, we might need to dig into their documentation to understand the current integration capabilities.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260613-1-20eba\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260613-1-20eba\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"planning-ATF_AIX\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-3a5e7c\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_b67edbb4\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-06-15T00:43:00\", \"text\": \"Could it be a compatibility issue with certain data source APIs? Maybe the APIs have been updated and our system hasn't caught up.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260613-2-f6cae\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260613-2-f6cae\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"planning-ATF_AIX\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-3a5e7c\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_35e32fec\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-06-15T00:47:00\", \"text\": \"@eid_b67edbb4 That's a good point. We should check if there have been any recent changes in the APIs of the data sources we're trying to integrate with.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260613-3-e3bde\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260613-3-e3bde\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"planning-ATF_AIX\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-3a5e7c\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_2490c02c\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-06-15T00:48:00\", \"text\": \"Another angle could be the design. Maybe there's limited support for diverse data formats or protocols. We should review the supported formats.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260613-4-5ef53\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260613-4-5ef53\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"planning-ATF_AIX\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-3a5e7c\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_6f719d21\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-06-15T00:52:00\", \"text\": \"Agreed, Bob. Also, we might not have enough partnerships or agreements with third-party data providers. This could be an operational issue.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260613-5-5c4fd\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260613-5-5c4fd\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"planning-ATF_AIX\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-3a5e7c\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_ad0725a2\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-06-15T00:57:00\", \"text\": \"Great insights, everyone. Let's make sure to document these issues and potential causes in our planning documents for the next release of ATF_AIX.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260613-6-0a7bc\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260613-6-0a7bc\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"planning-ATF_AIX\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-3a5e7c\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_6f719d21\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-06-17T08:30:00\", \"text\": \"Hi team, QA team found some issues in the last release of ATF_AIX. The issue was reported by QA Specialist eid_dc8bf84e.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260705-0-c5811\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260705-0-c5811\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"planning-ATF_AIX\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-3a5e7c\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_8c71a7a9\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-06-17T08:33:00\", \"text\": \"Thanks for the update, Ian. What exactly did they find?\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260705-1-21738\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260705-1-21738\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"planning-ATF_AIX\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-3a5e7c\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_6f719d21\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-06-17T08:38:00\", \"text\": \"Some users are having trouble understanding the parameter adjustment process due to a lack of detailed documentation.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260705-2-9e09b\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260705-2-9e09b\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"planning-ATF_AIX\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-3a5e7c\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_35e32fec\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-06-17T08:40:00\", \"text\": \"Wasn't the product developed and tested by a different team before we took over?\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260705-3-9bb58\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260705-3-9bb58\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"planning-ATF_AIX\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-3a5e7c\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_2490c02c\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-06-17T08:45:00\", \"text\": \"Yes, it was. Maybe they didn't provide enough documentation with the product.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260705-4-5901f\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260705-4-5901f\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"planning-ATF_AIX\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-3a5e7c\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_b67edbb4\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-06-17T08:48:00\", \"text\": \"Could be. Also, do we have comprehensive user guides or tutorials available?\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260705-5-89894\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260705-5-89894\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"planning-ATF_AIX\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-3a5e7c\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_84b3cc1f\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-06-17T08:52:32\", \"text\": \"@here Stay updated with this article on the latest advancements in AI model optimization. It highlights trends that align with the goals of ATF_AIX. https://venturebeat.com/ai/ai-model-optimization-trends/\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260617-27-ef5f1\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260617-27-ef5f1\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"planning-ATF_AIX\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-3a5e7c\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_ad0725a2\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-06-17T08:53:00\", \"text\": \"Good point, David. If the guides are lacking, that could definitely be a factor.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260705-6-f4f8c\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260705-6-f4f8c\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"planning-ATF_AIX\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-3a5e7c\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_8c71a7a9\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-06-17T08:57:00\", \"text\": \"What about the design? Is the parameter adjustment process too complex to explain easily?\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260705-7-1aa09\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260705-7-1aa09\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"planning-ATF_AIX\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-3a5e7c\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_6f719d21\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-06-17T08:58:00\", \"text\": \"That's possible. We might need to simplify the process or at least make the explanation clearer.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260705-8-f96b0\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260705-8-f96b0\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"planning-ATF_AIX\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-3a5e7c\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_35e32fec\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-06-17T09:01:00\", \"text\": \"Agreed. We should look into all these aspects and see where improvements can be made.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260705-9-0a24a\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260705-9-0a24a\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"planning-ATF_AIX\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-3a5e7c\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_2490c02c\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-06-17T09:02:00\", \"text\": \"Let's make sure these issues are documented in the planning documents for the next release of ATF_AIX.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260705-10-9ff94\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260705-10-9ff94\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"planning-ATF_AIX\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-3a5e7c\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_b67edbb4\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-06-17T09:06:00\", \"text\": \"Absolutely. I'll start drafting some notes on this.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260705-11-99d08\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260705-11-99d08\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"planning-ATF_AIX\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-3a5e7c\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_ad0725a2\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-06-17T09:07:00\", \"text\": \"Great. Thanks, everyone, for the input. Let's keep this momentum going.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260705-12-1d006\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260705-12-1d006\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"planning-ATF_AIX\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-3a5e7c\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"slack_admin_bot\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-06-11T01:22:00\", \"text\": \"@'eid_6bd20afa' created this channel on 2026-06-11 01:22:00. This is the very beginning of the planning-ATF_AIX channel.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260611-0-57ff7\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260611-0-57ff7\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"planning-ATF_AIX\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-3a5e7c\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"slack_admin_bot\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-06-11T01:22:00\", \"text\": \"@'eid_6bd20afa' joined planning-ATF_AIX. Also, @eid_35e32fec, @eid_6bd20afa, @eid_961f0487, @eid_576f3f62, @eid_36569bb7, @eid_8c71a7a9, @eid_b67edbb4, @eid_84b3cc1f, @eid_5e3edafc, @eid_ea95d983, @eid_e42b000f, @eid_6f719d21, @eid_19f537cf joined via invite.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260611-1-0be76\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260611-1-0be76\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-davidmiller-AutoTuneForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-cca2c2\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_67f8a879\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-16T12:28:00\", \"text\": \"Hi team, I looked into the reported issue about error messages obscuring UI controls. After a thorough review, I've determined that this does not require a fix.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261116-0-b6c6b\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261116-0-b6c6b\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-davidmiller-AutoTuneForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-cca2c2\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_b67edbb4\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-16T12:30:00\", \"text\": \"Hey Bob Williams, could you elaborate on why it's not a bug?\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261116-1-fb32b\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261116-1-fb32b\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-davidmiller-AutoTuneForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-cca2c2\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_67f8a879\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-16T12:31:00\", \"text\": \"Sure, David. The issue stems from a CSS layering configuration that was intentionally set to prioritize error visibility. This is actually expected behavior to ensure users are immediately aware of critical errors.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261116-2-49e2f\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261116-2-49e2f\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-davidmiller-AutoTuneForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-cca2c2\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_9307fe85\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-16T12:34:00\", \"text\": \"@eid_67f8a879 So, the error message overlay is supposed to cover those elements?\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261116-3-8a058\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261116-3-8a058\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-davidmiller-AutoTuneForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-cca2c2\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_67f8a879\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-16T12:39:00\", \"text\": \"Exactly, Bob Davis. The design decision was made to ensure that users address errors before proceeding with any other actions. It's a safeguard to prevent further issues.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261116-4-23167\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261116-4-23167\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-davidmiller-AutoTuneForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-cca2c2\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_b67edbb4\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-16T12:43:00\", \"text\": \"Got it. Did you take any steps to verify this?\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261116-5-a1c85\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261116-5-a1c85\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-davidmiller-AutoTuneForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-cca2c2\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_67f8a879\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-16T12:48:00\", \"text\": \"Yes, I reviewed the design documentation and confirmed with the UX team that this is intentional. Additionally, I tested various scenarios to ensure the overlay behaves as expected.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261116-6-8d45a\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261116-6-8d45a\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-davidmiller-AutoTuneForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-cca2c2\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_9307fe85\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-16T12:53:00\", \"text\": \"Thanks for clarifying, Bob Williams. It's good to know it's not an oversight.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261116-7-666d2\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261116-7-666d2\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-davidmiller-AutoTuneForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-cca2c2\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_67f8a879\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-16T12:56:00\", \"text\": \"No problem! If there are any more questions or concerns, feel free to reach out.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261116-8-830e0\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261116-8-830e0\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-davidmiller-AutoTuneForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-cca2c2\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_b67edbb4\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-18T19:12:00\", \"text\": \"Hi team, the customer has reopened the 'Error Messages Obscuring Controls' bug. It seems like it's still causing issues for CUST-0115. 😕\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261118-0-8e29f\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261118-0-8e29f\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-davidmiller-AutoTuneForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-cca2c2\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_67f8a879\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-18T19:13:00\", \"text\": \"Oh, that's unexpected. I thought we had this covered as per the design decision. @eid_b67edbb4, do we have more details on why it's been reopened?\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261118-1-5fa3d\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261118-1-5fa3d\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-davidmiller-AutoTuneForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-cca2c2\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_b67edbb4\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-18T19:18:00\", \"text\": \"Yes, David. The customer mentioned that the error messages are still preventing them from accessing some critical functions, which is impacting their workflow significantly.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261118-2-707f8\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261118-2-707f8\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-davidmiller-AutoTuneForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-cca2c2\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_9307fe85\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-18T19:23:00\", \"text\": \"Hmm, that's interesting. @Bob Williams, do you think there might be a specific scenario we missed during testing?\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261118-3-315e6\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261118-3-315e6\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-davidmiller-AutoTuneForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-cca2c2\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_67f8a879\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-18T19:28:00\", \"text\": \"It's possible, Bob Davis. I'll need to dive back into the UI components and see if there's a way to balance error visibility with control accessibility. Let's make sure we address this thoroughly. 🔍\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261118-4-24a2c\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261118-4-24a2c\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-davidmiller-AutoTuneForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-cca2c2\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_b67edbb4\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-18T19:30:00\", \"text\": \"Thanks, Bob Williams. I'll reassign the bug to you so you can take another look. Let us know if you need any additional resources or support. 👍\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261118-5-08ec6\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261118-5-08ec6\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-davidmiller-AutoTuneForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-cca2c2\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_67f8a879\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-18T19:34:00\", \"text\": \"Got it, David. I'll start by reviewing the customer feedback and then coordinate with the UX team to explore possible adjustments. I'll keep everyone updated. 🚀\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261118-6-20a2c\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261118-6-20a2c\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-davidmiller-AutoTuneForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-cca2c2\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_9307fe85\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-18T19:38:00\", \"text\": \"Sounds like a plan. Let us know if you need any help with testing once you have a fix in place. Good luck, Bob Williams! 💪\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261118-7-15623\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261118-7-15623\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-davidmiller-AutoTuneForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-cca2c2\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_b67edbb4\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-23T07:19:00\", \"text\": \"Hi team, several customers are reporting issues with AutoTuneForce that we need to address. Let's go through them one by one. 😊\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261122-0-82409\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261122-0-82409\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-davidmiller-AutoTuneForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-cca2c2\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_b67edbb4\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-23T07:20:00\", \"text\": \"First up, we have an issue titled 'Unresponsive Control Sliders'. The control sliders for adjusting model parameters are becoming unresponsive intermittently. This affects the User Interface and is impacting Customer CUST-0090. @eid_67f8a879, this one's for you. Can you take a look?\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261122-1-f7f08\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261122-1-f7f08\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-davidmiller-AutoTuneForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-cca2c2\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_67f8a879\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-23T07:21:00\", \"text\": \"Got it! I'll dive into the UI to see what's causing the unresponsiveness. Thanks for the heads-up! 👍\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261122-2-d0fb3\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261122-2-d0fb3\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-davidmiller-AutoTuneForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-cca2c2\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_b67edbb4\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-23T07:25:00\", \"text\": \"Great, thanks! Next, we have an 'Insecure Parameter Storage Mechanism'. Model parameters are being stored unencrypted, which is a security risk. This affects the Security Layer of the Parameter Adjustment Module and impacts Customer CUST-0019. @eid_9307fe85, can you handle this one?\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261122-3-19c5a\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261122-3-19c5a\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-davidmiller-AutoTuneForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-cca2c2\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_9307fe85\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-23T07:28:00\", \"text\": \"Absolutely, I'll prioritize encrypting the storage mechanism to secure those parameters. Thanks for assigning this to me! 🔒\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261122-4-ab1e6\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261122-4-ab1e6\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-davidmiller-AutoTuneForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-cca2c2\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_b67edbb4\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-23T07:30:00\", \"text\": \"Awesome, thanks! Lastly, there's a 'Log Truncation During High Load' issue. Logs are getting truncated during high system load, affecting the Database Logging System. This is impacting Customer CUST-0053. @eid_15ac3a3b, can you take this on?\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261122-5-401d1\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261122-5-401d1\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-davidmiller-AutoTuneForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-cca2c2\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_15ac3a3b\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-23T07:33:00\", \"text\": \"Sure thing! I'll investigate the logging system to ensure complete log entries even under high load. Let's keep those logs intact! 📈\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261122-6-6461c\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261122-6-6461c\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-davidmiller-AutoTuneForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-cca2c2\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_b67edbb4\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-23T07:37:00\", \"text\": \"Thanks, everyone! Let's keep communication open as you work through these. Feel free to reach out if you need any help or additional info. 🚀\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261122-7-b3cdd\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261122-7-b3cdd\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-davidmiller-AutoTuneForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-cca2c2\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_67f8a879\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-23T07:41:00\", \"text\": \"Will do! I'll update once I have more info on the UI issue. 😊\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261122-8-2dd7f\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261122-8-2dd7f\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-davidmiller-AutoTuneForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-cca2c2\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_9307fe85\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-23T07:43:00\", \"text\": \"Same here, I'll keep you posted on the security fix progress. 🔐\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261122-9-bd8bd\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261122-9-bd8bd\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-davidmiller-AutoTuneForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-cca2c2\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_15ac3a3b\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-23T07:45:00\", \"text\": \"I'll share updates on the logging issue soon. Thanks for the support, team! 🙌\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261122-10-33673\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261122-10-33673\"}\n{\"transcript\": \"Attendees\\nHannah Martinez, Ian Taylor, David Miller, Ian Smith, Julia Garcia, Hannah Johnson, Julia Williams, George Davis, Emma Williams, George Johnson, Hannah Jones, Alice Brown, Julia Taylor, Bob Martinez, George Taylor, George Jones, David Martinez, Bob Williams, George Jones, Bob Davis, Fiona Williams, Alice Davis, George Smith, Ian Smith, Alice Davis\\nTranscript\\nHannah Martinez: Alright, everyone, let's get started with our sprint review. First up, let's discuss the completed PRs. Bob, can you give us an update on the Automated Security Monitoring for Blockchain?\\nBob Martinez: Sure, Hannah. The automated security monitoring tools have been successfully implemented. We've set up continuous assessments for the blockchain network's security posture, and everything is running smoothly.\\nJulia Garcia: That's great to hear, Bob. This is a crucial feature for our product's security. Well done!\\nJulia Williams: Absolutely, great job, Bob. Now, let's move on to the pending tasks. We have the task of improving the analytics dashboard. Julia, can you update us on the status of the PR for simplifying the dashboard design?\\nJulia Taylor: Yes, the PR titled 'Simplify Dashboard Design and Improve UI/UX' was submitted, but it needs additional revisions. I'll be working on a new PR to address the feedback and submit it soon.\\nHannah Martinez: Great, Julia. Just to confirm, you'll be handling the new PR for the dashboard improvements?\\nJulia Taylor: Yes, I confirm. I'll take care of this implementation.\\nGeorge Davis: Julia, if you need any assistance with the UI/UX aspects, feel free to reach out. We want to ensure the dashboard is as user-friendly as possible.\\nJulia Taylor: Thanks, George. I'll definitely reach out if I need any help.\\nJulia Garcia: Perfect. Let's make sure we keep the user experience at the forefront. Anything else on the dashboard task?\\nHannah Martinez: I think that's it for now. Julia, just keep us posted on your progress. Now, are there any other tasks or PRs we need to discuss today?\\nJulia Williams: Not from my side. I think we've covered the main points for this session.\\nJulia Garcia: Alright, if there are no further updates, let's wrap up. Thanks, everyone, for your hard work. Let's keep the momentum going!\\nHannah Martinez: Thanks, team. Have a great day!\", \"date\": \"2026-10-06T22:56:00\", \"document_type\": \"product-planning\", \"participants\": [\"eid_8c71a7a9\", \"eid_35e32fec\", \"eid_b67edbb4\", \"eid_6f719d21\", \"eid_6bd20afa\", \"eid_e42b000f\", \"eid_5e3edafc\", \"eid_19f537cf\", \"eid_ea95d983\", \"eid_84b3cc1f\", \"eid_576f3f62\", \"eid_961f0487\", \"eid_36569bb7\", \"eid_65324b8a\", \"eid_04a698e5\", \"eid_6a0f49ba\", \"eid_e81cfe3f\", \"eid_67f8a879\", \"eid_15ac3a3b\", \"eid_9307fe85\", \"eid_1fd8457f\", \"eid_d5987f51\", \"eid_e9652ef0\", \"eid_e1bcb754\", \"eid_5780b68c\"], \"id\": \"product_dev_AutoTuneForce_9\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"planning-ATF_AIX\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-3a5e7c\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_e42b000f\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-06-27T15:28:00\", \"text\": \"Hi team, let's review the Product Vision Document and update it based on the latest issues reported. 🚀 We need to address the performance, documentation, integration, reliability, and UI concerns. @eid_6f719d21, @eid_b67edbb4, @eid_35e32fec, @eid_8c71a7a9, @eid_ad0725a2, @eid_2490c02c, please share your thoughts and suggestions.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260626-0-b297f\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260626-0-b297f\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"planning-ATF_AIX\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-3a5e7c\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_6f719d21\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-06-27T15:33:00\", \"text\": \"Hey @eid_e42b000f, for the auto-tuning process, we should consider optimizing the algorithms for low-power systems. Maybe we can add a section in the document about optimizing resource management and providing clearer system requirements. This could help users better assess compatibility. 💡\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260626-1-1c725\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260626-1-1c725\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"planning-ATF_AIX\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-3a5e7c\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_2490c02c\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-06-27T15:36:00\", \"text\": \"I agree with Ian. Also, for the documentation issue, we should include a detailed user guide and tutorials in the vision document. This will help users understand the parameter adjustment process better. We can also simplify the process itself if possible. 📚\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260626-2-1fa67\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260626-2-1fa67\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"planning-ATF_AIX\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-3a5e7c\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_b67edbb4\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-06-27T15:41:00\", \"text\": \"On the integration front, we need to expand our API support and ensure compatibility with more data sources. This should be reflected in the 'Integration' section of the document. We might also want to explore partnerships with third-party providers to enhance data diversity. 🔗\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260626-3-d1641\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260626-3-d1641\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"planning-ATF_AIX\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-3a5e7c\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_35e32fec\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-06-27T15:46:00\", \"text\": \"For the reliability issues, we should focus on improving our error handling and failover mechanisms. Adding a section on robust testing under high-load scenarios in the document could be beneficial. This will ensure we are prepared for real-time updates even under heavy data loads. ⚙️\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260626-4-58a05\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260626-4-58a05\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"planning-ATF_AIX\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-3a5e7c\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_8c71a7a9\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-06-27T15:51:00\", \"text\": \"Regarding the UI, we need to make it more intuitive. Perhaps adding user-friendly navigation and guidance features could help. We should also include plans for better onboarding resources in the document. This will reduce the learning curve for new users. 🎨\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260626-5-04217\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260626-5-04217\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"planning-ATF_AIX\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-3a5e7c\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_ad0725a2\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-06-27T15:56:00\", \"text\": \"Great points, everyone. Let's ensure the document reflects these changes. We should also consider adding a 'User Feedback' section to continuously gather insights and improve the product. This will keep us aligned with user needs and expectations. 📈\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260626-6-4aaae\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260626-6-4aaae\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"planning-ATF_AIX\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-3a5e7c\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_e42b000f\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-06-27T15:59:00\", \"text\": \"Thanks for the input, team! Here's a summary of the key changes: \\n1. Optimize algorithms for low-power systems and update system requirements.\\n2. Enhance documentation with detailed guides and tutorials.\\n3. Expand API support and explore third-party partnerships.\\n4. Improve error handling and testing for high-load scenarios.\\n5. Make the UI more intuitive with better onboarding resources.\\n6. Add a 'User Feedback' section.\\n\\nI'll draft the updates and share them for review. Let's aim to finalize this by the end of the week. 👍\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260626-7-b1a17\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260626-7-b1a17\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"planning-ATF_AIX\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-3a5e7c\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_e42b000f\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-06-27T23:00:00\", \"text\": \"Here is the updated <https://sf-internal.slack.com/archives/docs/new_atf_aix_product_vision_document|Product Vision Document>, thank you everyone!\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260627-0-d2ee7\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260627-0-d2ee7\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"planning-ATF_AIX\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-3a5e7c\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"slack_admin_bot\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-06-28T00:24:00\", \"text\": \"@eid_0719bc3e joined planning-ATF_AIX.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260628-98-34f99\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260628-98-34f99\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"planning-ATF_AIX\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-3a5e7c\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_e42b000f\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-06-28T08:49:00\", \"text\": \"Hi team, let's review the Product Requirements Document and update it based on the latest issues reported. 🚀 We need to address the performance, documentation, integration, reliability, and UI challenges. @eid_b67edbb4, could you start with the auto-tuning performance issue?\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260628-0-4df70\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260628-0-4df70\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"planning-ATF_AIX\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-3a5e7c\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_b67edbb4\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-06-28T08:50:00\", \"text\": \"Sure, @eid_e42b000f. The auto-tuning process is resource-intensive, especially on less powerful systems. I suggest we add a section in the document about optimizing the algorithms for low-power systems and improving resource management. This could involve simplifying some of the computational processes or offering a 'light' mode for less powerful hardware. Thoughts, @eid_6f719d21?\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260628-1-1fdbf\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260628-1-1fdbf\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"planning-ATF_AIX\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-3a5e7c\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_6f719d21\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-06-28T08:53:00\", \"text\": \"I agree, David. We should also update the system requirements documentation to help users assess compatibility better. This could prevent performance issues before they arise. @eid_061285c7, do you think this would help with QA testing?\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260628-2-2c277\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260628-2-2c277\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"planning-ATF_AIX\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-3a5e7c\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_061285c7\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-06-28T08:55:00\", \"text\": \"Absolutely, Ian. Clearer system requirements would streamline our testing process and ensure we're covering all bases. We should also consider adding more detailed documentation for the parameter adjustment process. @eid_2490c02c, any thoughts on making the documentation more user-friendly?\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260628-3-6a94f\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260628-3-6a94f\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"planning-ATF_AIX\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-3a5e7c\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_2490c02c\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-06-28T09:00:00\", \"text\": \"Good point, Julia. We could include step-by-step guides and video tutorials to make the parameter adjustment process clearer. This would help users understand the system better and reduce the learning curve. @eid_8c71a7a9, how do you feel about the integration issues?\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260628-4-7264b\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260628-4-7264b\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"planning-ATF_AIX\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-3a5e7c\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_8c71a7a9\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-06-28T09:04:00\", \"text\": \"Thanks, Bob. For integration, we should expand the document to include support for more data formats and protocols. This would enhance compatibility with third-party data sources. We might also need to establish more partnerships with data providers. @eid_9c46088d, any input on reliability issues?\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260628-5-4744e\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260628-5-4744e\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"planning-ATF_AIX\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-3a5e7c\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_9c46088d\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-06-28T09:09:00\", \"text\": \"Yes, Hannah. We need to improve our error handling and failover mechanisms to handle high data loads better. Adding a section on robust testing under high-load scenarios in the document would be beneficial. @eid_0719bc3e, do you think this aligns with our current testing strategies?\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260628-6-1e60e\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260628-6-1e60e\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"planning-ATF_AIX\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-3a5e7c\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_0719bc3e\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-06-28T09:12:00\", \"text\": \"It does, Charlie. We should also consider adding more real-time monitoring tools to detect and address issues quickly. This could be included in the analytics dashboard section. @eid_7f22371d, any thoughts on the UI challenges?\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260628-7-ec5ec\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260628-7-ec5ec\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"planning-ATF_AIX\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-3a5e7c\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_7f22371d\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-06-28T09:16:00\", \"text\": \"For the UI, we need to simplify the interface and improve navigation. Adding user-friendly guidance features and onboarding resources in the document would help new users get up to speed faster. @eid_35e32fec, do you think this covers the design aspects?\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260628-8-5b74b\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260628-8-5b74b\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"planning-ATF_AIX\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-3a5e7c\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_35e32fec\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-06-28T09:19:00\", \"text\": \"Yes, Fiona. Simplifying the UI and adding intuitive navigation will definitely help. We should also consider user feedback to continuously improve the design. @eid_e42b000f, do you think these changes cover the key issues?\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260628-9-6db2b\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260628-9-6db2b\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"planning-ATF_AIX\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-3a5e7c\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_e42b000f\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-06-28T09:22:00\", \"text\": \"Great discussion, everyone! 👍 Here's a summary of the key changes: optimize algorithms for low-power systems, update system requirements, enhance documentation with guides and tutorials, expand integration support, improve error handling, and simplify the UI. Let's incorporate these into the document and set up a follow-up meeting to finalize. Thanks for your input! 😊\", \"utterranceID\": \"20260628-10-6afd5\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20260628-10-6afd5\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-iantaylor-AutoTuneForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-66a156\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_7f22371d\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-15T00:40:00\", \"text\": \"Hi team, I noticed that PR# 26 was approved and merged, but I've heard that our product direction has changed. Should we consider reverting this PR?\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261014-0-91bba\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261014-0-91bba\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-iantaylor-AutoTuneForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-66a156\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_6a0f49ba\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-15T00:41:00\", \"text\": \"Hey everyone, yes, I approved the PR because it seemed aligned with our goals at the time. Can someone clarify how our product direction has changed?\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261014-1-272b6\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261014-1-272b6\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-iantaylor-AutoTuneForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-66a156\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_061285c7\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-15T00:45:00\", \"text\": \"From what I understand, we're shifting focus away from real-time updates to prioritize other features. This PR might not be necessary anymore.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261014-2-08c88\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261014-2-08c88\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-iantaylor-AutoTuneForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-66a156\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_04a698e5\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-15T00:48:00\", \"text\": \"I approved it too. If the real-time updates are no longer a priority, it makes sense to discuss reverting it. @eid_65324b8a, could you provide some insight on the impact of this PR?\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261014-3-62d29\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261014-3-62d29\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-iantaylor-AutoTuneForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-66a156\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_65324b8a\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-15T00:53:00\", \"text\": \"Sure, the PR optimizes backend processes specifically for real-time updates. If we're not focusing on that, reverting it could prevent unnecessary complexity in our codebase.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261014-4-d248f\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261014-4-d248f\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-iantaylor-AutoTuneForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-66a156\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_9c46088d\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-15T00:58:00\", \"text\": \"Thanks for the clarification. It seems like reverting might be the best option to keep our codebase clean and aligned with our current goals.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261014-5-413a8\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261014-5-413a8\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-iantaylor-AutoTuneForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-66a156\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_0719bc3e\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-15T01:00:00\", \"text\": \"Agreed. We should revert it to avoid maintaining code that doesn't serve our current objectives.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261014-6-d424d\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261014-6-d424d\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-iantaylor-AutoTuneForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-66a156\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_7f22371d\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-15T01:02:00\", \"text\": \"Alright, @eid_65324b8a, could you please handle reverting the PR? Let us know if you need any assistance.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261014-7-1bbd8\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261014-7-1bbd8\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-iantaylor-AutoTuneForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-66a156\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_65324b8a\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-15T01:05:00\", \"text\": \"Got it, I'll take care of reverting the PR soon. I'll update everyone once it's done. Thanks for the heads-up!\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261014-8-5ca52\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261014-8-5ca52\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-iantaylor-AutoTuneForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-66a156\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_65324b8a\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-15T04:36:00\", \"text\": \"https://github.com/salesforce/ATF_AIX/pull/27\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261015-0-953f9\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261015-0-953f9\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-iantaylor-AutoTuneForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-66a156\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_6a0f49ba\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-15T04:40:00\", \"text\": \"Looks good\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261015-1-dc157\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261015-1-dc157\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"develop-iantaylor-AutoTuneForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-f_aix-66a156\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_04a698e5\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-15T04:44:00\", \"text\": \"LGTM\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261015-2-1054a\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261015-2-1054a\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-iantaylor-AutoTuneForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-35b4b2\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"slack_admin_bot\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-25T11:18:00\", \"text\": \"@eid_35e32fec created this channel on 2026-10-25 11:18:00. This is the very beginning of the bug-iantaylor-AutoTuneForce channel.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261025-0-cdbc2\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261025-0-cdbc2\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-iantaylor-AutoTuneForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-35b4b2\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"slack_admin_bot\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-25T11:18:00\", \"text\": \"@eid_35e32fec joined bug-iantaylor-AutoTuneForce. Also, @eid_36569bb7, @eid_6a0f49ba, @eid_65324b8a, @eid_04a698e5 joined via invite.\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261025-1-21bfb\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261025-1-21bfb\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-iantaylor-AutoTuneForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-35b4b2\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_35e32fec\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-10-25T21:08:00\", \"text\": \"Hi team, several customers are reporting issues with AutoTuneForce that need our attention. Let's go through them one by one. 🚀\", \"utterranceID\": \"20261025-0-7f0d9\"}, \"Reactions\": []}, \"ThreadReplies\": [], \"id\": \"20261025-0-7f0d9\"}\n{\"Channel\": {\"name\": \"bug-iantaylor-AutoTuneForce\", \"channelID\": \"ch-force-35b4b2\"}, \"Message\": {\"User\": {\"userId\": \"eid_